-- Lesson flow v3 data import (adult/teen/child, 52 weeks each).
-- Idempotent: ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE by (week_number) and (week_number, audience).

Most of us live on autopilot — reacting to noise instead of tuning into what actually matters. The first step in personal growth is learning to tell the difference between your signal (inner wisdom, real values, genuine responses) and the noise (external pressure, inherited stories, fear-based reactions).', 'Ask the room: On a scale of 1–10, how much of your day do you actually choose — versus simply react? Take 30 seconds. No thinking. Just a number. Then: what''s driving the reactions?', 'Most of us live on autopilot — reacting to noise instead of tuning into what actually matters. The first step in personal growth is learning to tell the difference between your signal (inner wisdom, real values, genuine responses) and the noise (external pressure, inherited stories, fear-based reactions).', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kJ_Gg5DPCQU', 'Emotional Labour — the invisible mental load in relationships: naming the work, making it visible, and moving from ''helping out'' to ''taking ownership''. Runtime ~20 min.', '', '', '', 'What have you been carrying silently that no one else can see?', 'MAKE THE INVISIBLE VISIBLE: For one week, track everything you carry — seen and unseen. Two columns: ''Visible tasks'' (dishes, laundry, bills) and ''Invisible load'' (remembering, planning, anticipating, following up). Be specific. Then compare your list with the person beside you. What''s on your list that they''d never notice? What would happen if you stopped carrying one item silently? Share one thing from the ''invisible'' column that surprised you.', 'What invisible load have you been carrying silently — and what would it take to name it, so it could finally be seen and shared?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Catch the hum. Once today, notice the mental list running in the background and write down one invisible thing you''re carrying that no one else can see.', 'Make one thing visible. Name one invisible responsibility out loud to the person who shares your life — not as a complaint, as information: ''I carry this. I''d like us to see it together.''', 'Move from helping to owning. Identify one task you''ve been ''helping with'' that you could own — and one task you''re carrying that someone else could own. Take one concrete step toward real ownership.', '', '', 'I see the invisible load, I name it without blame, and I share it so we can carry it together.', 'Week 1: keep loose and welcoming. Goal is connection and curiosity, not depth. Everyone leaves knowing the signal/noise framework and feeling the room is safe. Resist the urge to go deep too fast.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

We all have a narrative running about who we are, what we deserve, and what''s possible for us. Most of those narratives were written before we were old enough to question them — by family, culture, early experiences, and how people responded to us. This week we examine the stories.', 'Complete this sentence without overthinking: ''People like me don''t...'' Whatever came up — that''s a story. Where did it come from?', 'We all have a narrative running about who we are, what we deserve, and what''s possible for us. Most of those narratives were written before we were old enough to question them — by family, culture, early experiences, and how people responded to us. This week we examine the stories.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=D9Ihs241zeg', 'TED Talk: ''The Power of Vulnerability'' by Brené Brown — directly addresses how shame-based stories shape our sense of worthiness and connection. One of the most-watched TED Talks of all time. Runtime ~20 min.', '', '', '', 'What do you believe about yourself that you have never once questioned?', 'MY STORY AUDIT: Take 5 minutes. Write the 3–5 beliefs you hold most deeply about yourself — not what you wish you believed, but what you actually seem to operate from. Try finishing: ''I''m the kind of person who...'' / ''I''ve always struggled with...'' / ''The reason things don''t work out for me is...'' For each one, ask: How old was I when I first believed this? Who taught me? What was happening? Share one — the least threatening one — with your small group.', 'Write the oldest story you carry about yourself. Then write what you would tell someone you love who had that same story about themselves.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Catch one moment where an old story seems to be making a decision for you.', 'Share the story you''re examining with someone you trust. Just naming it — not fixing it.', 'Bring one insight from the week about a story you noticed running — however small.', '', '', 'I can see the stories I carry. Seeing them means I am no longer only inside them.', 'This session can surface real vulnerability. Have tissues available. Make explicit: ''You don''t have to share anything you''re not ready to share.'' Watch for anyone who seems deeply activated — follow up individually.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Once we can see our patterns, the next question is: can we pause before they run? Not suppress them — pause. The space between stimulus and response is where genuine choice lives. This week is about learning to find that space.', 'Think of a behaviour you keep repeating that you''d genuinely like to change — not a big shameful thing, just a pattern. Something you do and then think ''why did I do that again?'' What is it?', 'Once we can see our patterns, the next question is: can we pause before they run? Not suppress them — pause. The space between stimulus and response is where genuine choice lives. This week is about learning to find that space.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZizdB0TgAVM', 'TED Talk: ''You Aren''t at the Mercy of Your Emotions'' by Lisa Feldman Barrett — neuroscience-grounded explanation of how emotions are constructed and how we have more agency than we think. Runtime ~18 min.', '', '', '', 'When did you last react in a way you didn''t choose?', 'TRIGGER MAPPING: For the pattern you named, trace it backwards. What is the behaviour specifically? What usually happens just before it — the trigger (a person, place, time, emotion, thought)? What does the behaviour give you short-term? What does it cost long-term? Now: what''s the smallest possible pause you could introduce between trigger and behaviour? Even one breath. Even just noticing. Share your trigger (not the behaviour) with your small group.', 'Describe a recent moment when a familiar pattern ran. What triggered it? What were you feeling just before?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'When you notice a familiar trigger today, just name it silently: ''There it is.'' You don''t have to change anything yet.', 'Tell someone what you''re learning to notice. Naming it to another person makes the awareness more real.', 'Bring one example of a moment you caught a trigger before (or just as) the pattern ran. What happened?', '', '', 'I am bigger than my patterns. I can see them. I can pause. And in that pause, I choose.', 'Keep this practical and non-shaming. Normalise that patterns exist for good reasons. Nobody''s patterns are shameful. The work is curious, not critical.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

The body keeps the score — and most of us stopped listening a long time ago. Chronic stress and the cultural pressure to push through means we''ve learned to override our most reliable source of real-time information. This week we tune back in.', 'Put one hand on your chest and one hand on your belly. Take one breath. What do you notice? Most people can''t answer that quickly — we''re that disconnected. That disconnection is what this session is about.', 'The body keeps the score — and most of us stopped listening a long time ago. Chronic stress and the cultural pressure to push through means we''ve learned to override our most reliable source of real-time information. This week we tune back in.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OidBsNLjD1Q', 'YouTube: Bessel van der Kolk interview on ''The Body Keeps the Score'' — foundational understanding of how the body holds emotional experience. Various clip lengths available. Book: ''The Body Keeps the Score'' by Bessel van der Kolk is core reading for this pillar.', '', '', '', 'Where in your body do you feel most at ease, and where most contracted?', 'BODY SCAN + MAPPING: Guide a slow body scan (facilitator reads aloud, 4–5 minutes): ''Start at the top of your head. Notice any tension, warmth, tingling, numbness. Move slowly down — face, jaw, throat, shoulders, chest, belly, hips, legs, feet. No fixing. Just noticing.'' Then on a body outline: mark where you''re holding tension, where you feel open, where you feel numb. Discuss in pairs: Are there patterns? Do certain areas always carry the same thing?', 'Where in your body do you feel stress first? When did you learn to override that signal rather than respond to it?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Three times today, do a 30-second body scan. Just notice. No analysis required.', 'Talk to someone about one physical sensation you''ve been ignoring. What might it be trying to tell you?', 'Bring one observation from this week''s body scan practice — what did you notice?', '', '', 'My body is speaking. I am learning its language.', 'The body scan is often deeply unfamiliar for adults who live in their heads. Go slowly. Strong emotional responses are normal with somatic work. Have a grounding tool ready: feet on floor, slow breath, name 5 things you can see.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

We don''t see ourselves clearly. We see ourselves through a filter built from years of feedback, comparison, shame, and selective memory. This week is about developing accurate self-perception — honest, compassionate, and grounded in evidence.', 'Write down three words you''d use to describe yourself. How long have you been using those words? Did you choose them — or were they given to you?', 'We don''t see ourselves clearly. We see ourselves through a filter built from years of feedback, comparison, shame, and selective memory. This week is about developing accurate self-perception — honest, compassionate, and grounded in evidence.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=haLsNaHmBhE', 'YouTube: Tasha Eurich — ''What Self-Awareness Really Is (and How to Cultivate It)'' talk. Evidence-based research on why most people who think they''re self-aware actually aren''t — and what actually builds it. Runtime ~20 min.', '', '', '', 'If you described yourself accurately — not aspirationally, not apologetically — what would you say?', 'THE HONEST INVENTORY: Three columns: 1. Strengths you genuinely see in yourself (not performative modesty — what are you actually good at?). 2. Limitations you genuinely see (not self-flagellation — what do you actually find difficult?). 3. Blind spots you suspect — things others might see in you that you''re not sure about. For column 3: what have multiple people independently said to you over the years, even if you dismissed it? Discuss in pairs: how did it feel to write column 1 vs column 3?', 'If you had to give yourself an honest character reference — the kind you''d give someone you respected and cared for — what would you write?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Notice once today when your self-perception shifts based on external feedback. What happened to your inner voice?', 'Ask one person you trust: ''What do you think is a genuine strength of mine that I don''t fully own?'' Listen without deflecting.', 'Bring the answer from your Wednesday conversation — and what you noticed about how it landed.', '', '', 'I see myself with honest, compassionate eyes. I am neither the worst nor the best version I have imagined.', 'People may discover uncomfortable things about themselves. Reinforce: ''Self-awareness is not self-criticism. It''s self-honesty in the service of growth.'' The asking-someone-else exercise is powerful but should be truly voluntary.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Comparison is one of the most subtle and pervasive sources of suffering in contemporary life. We compare upward (to those who appear more successful) and downward (to validate our position). Neither makes us genuinely happier. This week we examine the loop — and find the exit.', 'Complete this sentence: ''I would feel like I''d made it if...'' Whatever came up — whose voice is that? Did you write that script, or did someone hand it to you?', 'Comparison is one of the most subtle and pervasive sources of suffering in contemporary life. We compare upward (to those who appear more successful) and downward (to validate our position). Neither makes us genuinely happier. This week we examine the loop — and find the exit.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SuF_mdyVNdM', 'YouTube: Johann Hari on the social drivers of anxiety — search ''Johann Hari lost connections talk.'' Deeply researched, compassionate, and directly relevant. Book: ''Lost Connections'' by Johann Hari is essential reading for this session.', '', '', '', 'Who do you compare yourself to, and what do you imagine they have?', 'THE COMPARISON AUDIT: Track comparison moments this week in three columns: 1. WHO — context, not names (colleague, friend, social media, public figure). 2. WHAT you''re comparing (status, appearance, relationships, success, parenting, intelligence). 3. HOW IT FELT and what story it activated. Today: do a quick 5-minute version for the past week from memory. Discuss in pairs: what do your comparison patterns reveal about what you most care about — or most fear?', 'Name one area of your life where you consistently compare unfavourably. Where did that standard come from — and is it actually yours?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Each time you catch a comparison thought, ask: ''Is this measuring me against my values — or against someone else''s life?''', 'Tell someone about one comparison loop you''re working to exit. Name the alternative measure you''re choosing instead.', 'Bring back your comparison audit from the week — what patterns did you notice?', '', '', 'My worth is not relative. It does not go up or down based on what others are doing.', 'The comparison audit is a powerful ongoing tool — encourage people to continue beyond this week. Some will find comparison patterns connected to early experiences of being ranked or found lacking. This session pairs well with Week 2 content.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Most of us have an inner voice far harsher than anything we''d say to someone we love. The inner critic is not healthy self-reflection — it is an internalised judge, often formed in childhood, that works against our growth while appearing to support it. This week we learn to hear it clearly and choose differently.', 'Read this sentence as if it were your own thought: ''You''re probably not as good as you think you are. Other people are doing this so much better.'' How familiar is that voice? What does it actually sound like in your head?', 'Most of us have an inner voice far harsher than anything we''d say to someone we love. The inner critic is not healthy self-reflection — it is an internalised judge, often formed in childhood, that works against our growth while appearing to support it. This week we learn to hear it clearly and choose differently.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IvtZBUSplr4', 'TED Talk: ''The Space Between Self-Esteem and Self-Compassion'' by Kristin Neff — evidence-based, warm, directly addresses the inner critic and what actually replaces it. Runtime ~20 min.', '', '', '', 'If that voice were a person, would you choose to spend time with them?', 'MEET YOUR CRITIC: Write down the inner critic''s greatest hits — the specific phrases it returns to most often. Now: imagine this voice belonged to a specific person in your life — past or present. Who does it most sound like? Next: write a response from your wisest, most compassionate self to each critic statement — not a denial, but a grounded honest alternative. Share: the most common theme your inner critic returns to (not the specific content).', 'If your inner critic wrote a review of your life, what would it say? Then: if your wisest friend wrote the same review, what would they say? What''s the gap?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Each time your inner critic fires today, name it: ''There''s the critic.'' Don''t argue. Just see it.', 'Tell someone about your inner critic — what it says, where you think it came from. Naming it to another person takes some of its power away.', 'Bring back one moment where you caught the inner critic and chose to respond differently.', '', '', 'I hear the critic. I see where it came from. And I choose the voice of my wiser self.', 'This session often releases strong emotional responses — normalise it. For many it''s the first time they''ve examined the inner critic with compassion rather than trying to fight or indulge it. Keep the tone warm and non-clinical. Refer to professionals for anyone showing signs of severe self-criticism or depression.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Most of us have two modes with emotions: suppress or flood. We either push them down or get overwhelmed by them. This week we develop a third option: emotions as information. Every emotion is communicating something — about our values, our needs, our history. Learning to read that communication is a core growth skill.', 'Name three emotions you''ve felt in the past 48 hours. Now: what was each one actually telling you? If you can answer that quickly, you''re already ahead of most people.', 'Most of us have two modes with emotions: suppress or flood. We either push them down or get overwhelmed by them. This week we develop a third option: emotions as information. Every emotion is communicating something — about our values, our needs, our history. Learning to read that communication is a core growth skill.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HJSK3HpgFdM', 'TED Talk: ''You Aren''t at the Mercy of Your Emotions'' by Lisa Feldman Barrett — groundbreaking neuroscience on how emotions are constructed and how we have more agency than we think. Runtime ~18 min.', '', '', '', 'What were you feeling just before you got angry?', 'THE EMOTIONAL INTELLIGENCE AUDIT: Think of a difficult emotion you experienced recently — something that felt too much, wrong, or that you tried to suppress. Ask it these questions and write your answers: What exactly am I feeling (be specific — not just ''bad'')? When did this feeling start? What triggered it? What is this feeling telling me about what I value, need, or fear? Is there a secondary emotion underneath this one? Share: the one question from that list you found hardest to answer.', 'Think of your dominant emotional response pattern: do you tend to suppress, explode, analyse, deflect, or something else? Where did you learn that response?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Once today when an emotion arises, pause before responding and ask: ''What is this actually telling me?''', 'Share with one person an emotion you''ve been avoiding. Not the story around it — just: ''I''ve been carrying [emotion] and I think it''s because [what it''s pointing at].''', 'Bring back one moment where you paused to read an emotion as information rather than reacting to or suppressing it.', '', '', 'My emotions are data, not drama. They are always pointing at something true.', 'This is a technically rich session — don''t rush the concepts. The key insight (emotions as information, not drama) is paradigm-shifting for most people. Ground the theory in immediate personal experience. The ''secondary emotion'' concept often produces significant revelations — give space for that.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

All of us have been hurt — by people who were supposed to protect us, by experiences that exceeded our capacity to cope, by systems that didn''t see us. Some of those experiences left marks that continue to shape how we move through the world. This week we look at what we carry — with honesty, courage, and enormous compassion.', 'Without going into detail: what''s one experience from your past that you suspect is still shaping you in ways you haven''t fully examined? You don''t have to name it specifically — just acknowledge it''s there.', 'All of us have been hurt — by people who were supposed to protect us, by experiences that exceeded our capacity to cope, by systems that didn''t see us. Some of those experiences left marks that continue to shape how we move through the world. This week we look at what we carry — with honesty, courage, and enormous compassion.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=95ovIJ3dsNk', 'TED Talk: ''How Childhood Trauma Affects Health Across a Lifetime'' by Nadine Burke Harris — landmark ACEs research presented with compassion and hope. Runtime ~16 min.', '', '', '', 'What is something you have never fully allowed yourself to grieve?', 'LEGACY CODE MAPPING — quiet and private: In your journal, explore whichever prompt feels right: ''One experience I know is still with me is...'' / ''A pattern I have that I suspect came from being hurt is...'' / ''Something I learned about love/safety/trust from an early wound is...'' / ''Something I''ve been carrying that doesn''t fully belong to the present is...'' Write as much or as little as you choose. This is for you. After 5–7 minutes: take a breath. Place your hand on your heart. Notice any shifts in your body.', 'If the wound you''ve been carrying could finally speak clearly — what would it need you to know?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Notice once today when a present situation triggers what feels like an old wound. You don''t have to resolve it. Just notice: ''This feels older than now.''', 'If it feels right, speak the name of something you''re carrying to one trusted person — not the full story, just: ''I''m carrying something and I''m starting to look at it.''', 'Bring one reflection from this week''s journal exercise — or simply how it felt to acknowledge the question.', '', '', 'What I carry does not define me. I see it clearly. And in seeing it, I begin the repair.', 'CRITICAL: Most emotionally sensitive session of Phase 1. Make crystal clear this is NOT trauma processing — it is an awareness session. Have professional referral resources printed and available. Never ask anyone to share specific trauma content publicly. Some participants may need to step out — have a quiet space and support person available. Follow duty of care protocol if any safety concerns arise.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Most of us present different versions of ourselves in different contexts — and that''s not inherently a problem. But when the mask becomes more familiar than the face underneath, we''ve lost something important. This week we examine the performances we give and the cost of maintaining them.', 'Think of the most socially managed version of yourself — the performance you give when you''re trying to be received well. How different is that person from the version that exists when no one is watching?', 'Most of us present different versions of ourselves in different contexts — and that''s not inherently a problem. But when the mask becomes more familiar than the face underneath, we''ve lost something important. This week we examine the performances we give and the cost of maintaining them.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iCvmsMzlF7o', 'TED Talk: ''The Power of Vulnerability'' by Brené Brown — the foundational research on authenticity, connection, and the cost of armoured performance. One of the most-watched TED Talks ever. Runtime ~20 min.', '', '', '', 'Is there something you feel or want that you have never let yourself express?', 'THE MASK INVENTORY: Draw or describe three masks you wear regularly: 1. The professional/competence mask. 2. The ''everything''s fine'' mask. 3. The mask that hides the need for help. For each: What does it protect? What does it cost? Who in your life has seen most clearly behind it? Now: what would happen if one of those masks came down a little? What is the specific fear — and how likely is it to actually happen? Share: one mask and what it costs you.', 'Think of a relationship where you''ve maintained a significant mask. What do you think would actually happen if that person saw more of the real you? What does your answer tell you about the relationship?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Notice once today when you put a mask on — and ask: ''Is this necessary right now, or is it fear?''', 'Show someone a tiny bit of what''s usually behind one of your masks — something genuine and slightly vulnerable. Notice what happens.', 'Bring back: what happened when you experimented with a little more authenticity this week?', '', '', 'I know my own face. The masks I wear are chosen — not required. I choose from security, not fear.', 'The mask metaphor is universally resonant and often produces significant insight without requiring dramatic disclosure. Watch for the person who has maintained very rigid masks — dropping them even conceptually can be destabilising. Ensure the session ends in a place of safety and agency.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

We don''t just have distorted views of ourselves — we have distorted views of other people. We project our fears, needs, and stories onto others. We mistake interpretation for objective reality. And we often fail to genuinely see the person in front of us. This week we develop clearer perception of others.', 'Think of someone who genuinely frustrates or irritates you. Now: honestly, what about them most bothers you? And is there any chance that quality exists — even in small measure — in yourself?', 'We don''t just have distorted views of ourselves — we have distorted views of other people. We project our fears, needs, and stories onto others. We mistake interpretation for objective reality. And we often fail to genuinely see the person in front of us. This week we develop clearer perception of others.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=baHrcC8B4WM', 'YouTube: ''The Power of Empathy'' — Brené Brown RSA animation. Short, brilliant, directly addresses the difference between empathy and sympathy. Runtime ~3 min.', '', '', '', 'Think of someone you find difficult. What might they be carrying?', 'PROJECTION AUDIT: Think of three people who currently frustrate or trigger you. For each one: 1. What specifically bothers you about them? 2. Honestly: does any version of that quality or behaviour exist in you? 3. What story are you telling about why they do what they do? Is there an alternative story? 4. What do you actually know — objectively — about their situation, history, and internal state? Share: one insight about the gap between your story about someone and what you actually know.', 'Think of a relationship where you have consistently interpreted someone''s behaviour negatively. Is there an alternative interpretation you have been avoiding? Why might you be avoiding it?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Once today when you have a negative judgment about someone, ask: ''What do I actually know — versus what have I assumed or projected?''', 'Tell someone a story you''ve been telling about a difficult relationship — and then tell them the most generous alternative interpretation you can construct.', 'Bring back one example of catching yourself in projection or attribution error this week.', '', '', 'I see people as clearly as I can — as complex, contextual human beings, not as characters in my story.', 'The projection audit can be genuinely confronting — some people will realise mid-exercise that they''ve been unfair to someone for a long time. Hold space for that without forcing resolution. The point is clarity, not reconciliation.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Most of our daily behaviour — researchers estimate up to 45% — is habit, not conscious choice. Understanding how habits form, how they''re maintained, and what function they serve is the foundation of genuine behaviour change. This week we map the loops.', 'Think of a habit you have that you genuinely want to change — not a moral failing, just a pattern. You''ve probably tried before. What happened?', 'Most of our daily behaviour — researchers estimate up to 45% — is habit, not conscious choice. Understanding how habits form, how they''re maintained, and what function they serve is the foundation of genuine behaviour change. This week we map the loops.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-moW9jvvMr4', 'YouTube: Charles Duhigg book talk or animated summary of ''The Power of Habit'' — the habit loop explained clearly and engagingly. Also: James Clear on atomic habits is widely available. Runtime ~10–20 min.', '', '', '', 'What do you do — reliably, almost without deciding — when you are uncomfortable?', 'THE HABIT LOOP AUDIT: For one habit you want to change, map it completely: 1. THE CUE — what triggers the habit? (Time of day, location, emotional state, preceding event, social context?) 2. THE ROUTINE — what is the habit itself, specifically? 3. THE REWARD — what does the habit actually give you short-term? Be honest — there IS a reward or it wouldn''t persist. 4. THE REAL NEED — what underlying need is the reward meeting? (Connection? Stress relief? Stimulation? Numbness?) 5. ALTERNATIVE ROUTINE — what else could meet that same underlying need more functionally? Share: the reward and the underlying need from your loop.', 'Think of a habit in your life you''ve maintained for years. What original need was it meeting? Is it still meeting that need — or just running on autopilot?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Catch one habit running today — not to judge it, just to see the full loop: cue, routine, reward. Write it down.', 'Tell someone about the underlying need your habit is meeting. Not the habit itself — the need. How does it feel to name that directly?', 'Bring back your complete habit loop map — cue, routine, reward, real need, and one alternative you''re considering.', '', '', 'I understand my patterns. That understanding is the foundation of everything I want to change.', 'The habit loop audit is one of the most practically valuable exercises of Phase 1 — give people enough time to genuinely work through all five columns. The ''real need'' column is often the revelation. This session sets up Phase 2 directly.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Thirteen weeks of honest looking. This is not the end of seeing clearly — it is the beginning. Phase 1 closes with integration: taking stock of what has shifted, what has become visible, and what you''re carrying into Phase 2 with new eyes. This is a threshold, not a summary.', 'If you had to describe who you were before this phase started — and who you are now, 13 weeks later — what would be most different? Not externally. In what you can see.', 'Thirteen weeks of honest looking. This is not the end of seeing clearly — it is the beginning. Phase 1 closes with integration: taking stock of what has shifted, what has become visible, and what you''re carrying into Phase 2 with new eyes. This is a threshold, not a summary.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sPOuCd6cBao', 'YouTube: ''This Is Water'' — David Foster Wallace 2005 commencement speech, animated. About the transformation of ordinary awareness into genuine seeing. One of the most important short pieces of content of the year. Runtime ~9 min.', '', '', '', 'What have you noticed about yourself in the last thirteen weeks that you hadn''t before?', 'INTEGRATION CIRCLE: In your journal, spend 10 minutes: 1. What is the clearest thing I can now see about myself that I couldn''t see 13 weeks ago? 2. What pattern have I been most challenged to acknowledge? 3. What have I been carrying that I now understand a little better? 4. What am I choosing to take into Phase 2 as an honest commitment? Then, if you choose: share one insight with the group — not what you need to change, but what you can now see clearly. Listen without response. This is witnessing, not fixing.', 'Write a letter to yourself from 13 weeks ago. What does the version of you that has done this work want them to know?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Revisit your very first week of observations — what have you noticed that has shifted since Week 1?', 'Share with someone who isn''t in this group: ''I''ve been working on understanding myself better. One thing I can see now that I couldn''t before is...'' Notice what it feels like to own that growth.', 'Come to the final session of Phase 1 ready to read your letter to yourself if you choose.', '', '', 'I see myself more clearly now. And in that clearer seeing, I am more free.', 'This is a ceremonial session — treat it as such. Create intentional ritual: candles, music, a physical symbol of crossing a threshold if appropriate to your group. Allow letters to be read aloud if people consent. This closing should feel genuinely significant. People have done real work. Honour it.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Many of us are living on hold — waiting for someone to tell us it''s okay to start, to change, to be who we actually are. We''re waiting for a parent''s approval, a partner''s green light, the right moment, or enough confidence. This week we examine the permission we''ve been waiting for — and recognise that it was always ours to give.', 'What is something you''ve been waiting to do — start, say, become — until some condition is met? What exactly are you waiting for? And who, specifically, would need to give you that permission?', 'Many of us are living on hold — waiting for someone to tell us it''s okay to start, to change, to be who we actually are. We''re waiting for a parent''s approval, a partner''s green light, the right moment, or enough confidence. This week we examine the permission we''ve been waiting for — and recognise that it was always ours to give.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iG9CE55wbtY', 'TED Talk: ''Why You Should Define Your Fears Instead of Your Goals'' by Tim Ferriss — explores the internal barriers we construct and the self-authorisation required to move past them. Runtime ~13 min.', '', '', '', 'What are you waiting for permission to do?', 'PERMISSION AUDIT: In your journal, complete these sentences honestly: ''I''ve been waiting to [action] until [condition].'' List as many as you can find — big and small. For each one, ask: Who would be giving me this permission if I received it? What would they actually be saying? Is there any reason — real, present-day reason — why I cannot give myself that same permission right now? Share: one permission you''ve been waiting for — and what you''d do immediately if you gave it to yourself today.', 'What is the oldest permission you''ve been waiting for — and from whom? Is that person actually the authority you''ve made them?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Notice once today when you catch yourself waiting for permission. Ask: from whom? And why do they have that authority?', 'Tell someone about one thing you''re giving yourself permission to pursue — and ask them to hold you to it.', 'Come back with the first small act of self-permission you took this week. What happened?', '', '', 'I do not need to wait. I am the authority over my own becoming.', 'This session often surfaces deep emotion — particularly for people who have been waiting in significant areas of their life (leaving relationships, changing careers, starting creative work). Keep the tone empowering rather than urgent. This is not about impulsive action — it is about reclaiming authority.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Most of us are carrying an image of who we were supposed to become — defined by family expectation, cultural script, early ambition, or the version of success we absorbed from our environment. When life doesn''t match that image, it can feel like failure. This week we examine that image — and ask whether it was ever actually ours.', 'Describe the person you were supposed to become — the version your family, culture, or early self expected. How closely does your current life match that image? And how do you feel about the gap?', 'Most of us are carrying an image of who we were supposed to become — defined by family expectation, cultural script, early ambition, or the version of success we absorbed from our environment. When life doesn''t match that image, it can feel like failure. This week we examine that image — and ask whether it was ever actually ours.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NiuDFBNDoSk', 'YouTube: ''There''s More to Life Than Being Happy'' by Emily Esfahani Smith — explores meaning vs. expected happiness and the freedom of living by your own values. Runtime ~12 min.', '', '', '', 'Whose expectations are you still living inside?', 'THE LIFE SCRIPT AUDIT: In your journal, write the life script you were given — the explicit or implicit expectations about your career, relationships, values, lifestyle, success markers. Be specific: who wrote it? What were the exact expectations? Now: which parts of that script did you consciously choose? Which parts are you living out of habit, obligation, or fear of disappointing someone? Which parts would you rewrite, if you had full permission? Share: one expectation you''ve been carrying that you''re ready to examine.', 'What is one thing you''ve continued doing primarily because it matches who you were supposed to be — not who you actually are?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Notice once today a choice you make that aligns with your actual values rather than your inherited script.', 'Tell one person about one way your life has diverged from ''the plan'' — and share how you actually feel about that divergence.', 'Bring back: what emerged when you wrote your life script? What surprised you?', '', '', 'I am not the person I was supposed to be. I am something more honest, more mine, and more alive.', 'This session carries real grief for many people — particularly those who have sacrificed significant life choices to meet family or cultural expectations. Honour the grief without rushing to reframe it as positive. The work is witnessing, not fixing.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Unforgiveness is one of the heaviest things a human being can carry. Not because the other person deserves forgiveness — but because the person carrying the resentment is the one paying the physiological and psychological cost. This week we examine what forgiveness actually is — and what it isn''t.', 'Think of someone you have not forgiven — or only partially forgiven. Don''t name them aloud. Just notice: what happens in your body when you bring them to mind? That physiological response is the cost you''re currently paying to keep the resentment running.', 'Unforgiveness is one of the heaviest things a human being can carry. Not because the other person deserves forgiveness — but because the person carrying the resentment is the one paying the physiological and psychological cost. This week we examine what forgiveness actually is — and what it isn''t.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ik_V3UIqoQ0', 'YouTube: ''Forgiveness'' — Fred Luskin Stanford Forgiveness Project talk on what forgiveness actually is, the science behind it, and why it matters for health. Search for available versions. Runtime ~15–20 min.', '', '', '', 'What are you still holding against someone, and what does holding it give you?', 'THE FORGIVENESS INVENTORY: In your journal, write about one person or situation where you''re carrying unforgiveness. Work through these steps: 1. Name the harm fully — what actually happened, what it cost you. 2. Acknowledge your emotional response — all of it, without editing. 3. Identify the story you''ve been repeating — how you''ve been re-telling this harm internally. 4. Ask honestly: what has carrying this cost you? What has it kept you from? 5. What would it mean — not to excuse the harm, but to release your own grip on it? Share: one insight from working through this — not necessarily the specific harm.', 'What is the oldest resentment you''re still carrying? What has it cost you — not them — to hold it this long?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Once today, when you notice a resentment replaying, say internally: ''I acknowledge this hurt. I choose to release my grip on the story.'' See what happens.', 'Share with one trusted person that you are working on releasing a resentment. You don''t have to name who or what — just that you''re doing the work.', 'Bring back: what shifted — even slightly — when you worked through the forgiveness inventory?', '', '', 'I release the grip of resentment — not for them, but for myself. The energy is mine again.', 'This session can be deeply moving. Some participants will be carrying resentment toward deceased people — acknowledge that forgiveness does not require the other person to be present or even alive. Others will be carrying resentment toward themselves — gently note that self-forgiveness is Week 17. Never pressure anyone to forgive before they are ready.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

For many people, forgiving others is difficult — but forgiving themselves is nearly impossible. We hold ourselves to a standard of perfection that we would never apply to someone we loved. The result is a chronic state of internal prosecution — always on trial, never acquitted. This week we examine what it would mean to finally offer yourself the verdict of enough.', 'Think of something you have not forgiven yourself for — a decision, a failure, a harm you caused, a version of yourself you''re ashamed of. Notice: how long have you been carrying this? What has it cost you?', 'For many people, forgiving others is difficult — but forgiving themselves is nearly impossible. We hold ourselves to a standard of perfection that we would never apply to someone we loved. The result is a chronic state of internal prosecution — always on trial, never acquitted. This week we examine what it would mean to finally offer yourself the verdict of enough.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IvtZBUSplr4', 'TED Talk: Kristin Neff on self-compassion — the most research-backed resource on self-forgiveness available. Also search ''Kristin Neff self-forgiveness'' for specific talks on this topic. Runtime ~15–20 min.', '', '', '', 'Is there something you have not forgiven yourself for?', 'SELF-FORGIVENESS PRACTICE: In your journal, work through one thing you haven''t forgiven yourself for: 1. State clearly what happened — without minimising or catastrophising. 2. Acknowledge the harm caused — to yourself or others. 3. Acknowledge the remorse genuinely — not performed guilt, but real accountability. 4. Ask: what did I learn from this? What would I do differently? 5. Now write the response from your wisest, most compassionate self — as if you were responding to a close friend who had told you the same story. What would you say to them? Share: one insight from this process — not the specific content.', 'Write the letter you would send a close friend if they confessed to you the thing you haven''t forgiven yourself for. Then read it back — to yourself.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Once today, when self-critical thoughts arise, try: ''I acknowledge what happened. I am learning. I am enough.'' Notice the physiological difference from the usual self-prosecution.', 'Tell one person something you''ve been hard on yourself about — and let them respond without fixing it. Receive their response.', 'Bring back: what was it like to write the letter to yourself? What did your wisest self say?', '', '', 'I extend to myself the same compassion I would give to someone I love. I am accountable and I am enough.', 'This is one of the most emotionally significant sessions of the year. Many people are carrying decades of self-judgment. The three-component process (acknowledge, remorse, compassion) is important — rushing to the compassion step without genuine acknowledgment feels hollow. Go slowly. Allow silence.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

In Phase 1 we identified the inner critic — where it came from and what it costs. Now, in Phase 2, we do the rewiring. This is not about silencing the critical voice forever. It is about replacing it with something more functional: an inner coach who is honest, grounded, and genuinely on your side.', 'Think of the most effective mentor, teacher, or coach you''ve ever had — real or imagined. What was the quality of their inner voice toward you? How did they deliver honest feedback without destroying your confidence? That voice is the template.', 'In Phase 1 we identified the inner critic — where it came from and what it costs. Now, in Phase 2, we do the rewiring. This is not about silencing the critical voice forever. It is about replacing it with something more functional: an inner coach who is honest, grounded, and genuinely on your side.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pN34FNbOKXc', 'YouTube: Carol Dweck on growth mindset and the language of coaching — search ''Carol Dweck growth mindset feedback'' for talks specifically about how we talk to ourselves and others about challenges. Runtime ~15 min.', '', '', '', 'What would a fair version of that voice have said instead?', 'BUILDING THE COACH: For the inner critic''s 5 most common statements about you, write the inner coach''s response to the same situation. Use this template — Coach response: Acknowledge the difficulty (e.g. ''That was genuinely hard''), state the specific observation (not global judgment), ask a growth question (e.g. ''What can I learn here?''), and affirm forward capacity (e.g. ''You''ve handled harder things than this''). Practise reading the coach response aloud to yourself — notice the physiological difference. Share: what the coach says that the critic never says.', 'Write a ''coach''s briefing'' for yourself before a challenging situation this week — the kind of preparation a truly skilled coach would give an athlete before a high-stakes moment.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Once today when the critic fires, deliberately run the coach script instead. Even if it feels artificial at first — do it anyway. The neural pathway is built through repetition, not feeling.', 'Share with one person: what does your inner coach say that your critic doesn''t? Ask them to reinforce the coach voice when they see you defaulting to self-criticism.', 'Bring back: what happened when you ran the coach script this week? What shifted?', '', '', 'My inner coach is honest, grounded, and genuinely on my side. That voice gets stronger every time I use it.', 'This session is highly practical and actionable — people leave with a specific skill they can use immediately. The coach script template should be practiced in the room, not just discussed. Some people will find the coach voice feels ''fake'' at first — normalise this: it IS a new neural pathway and it does feel strange before it feels natural.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

People-pleasing is rarely about kindness. It is almost always about fear — fear of conflict, rejection, disapproval, or the discomfort of being seen as inadequate. The result is a life lived in service of other people''s comfort at the expense of one''s own authenticity and wellbeing. This week we examine the pattern — and begin to dismantle it.', 'Complete this sentence: ''I find it hardest to say no to...'' Now ask: is the difficulty about genuine care for that person — or about the discomfort of their potential disappointment?', 'People-pleasing is rarely about kindness. It is almost always about fear — fear of conflict, rejection, disapproval, or the discomfort of being seen as inadequate. The result is a life lived in service of other people''s comfort at the expense of one''s own authenticity and wellbeing. This week we examine the pattern — and begin to dismantle it.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MIte_1vcOqs', 'YouTube: Search ''people pleasing fawn response psychology'' or Nedra Tawwab on boundaries — practical, evidence-based content on the people-pleasing pattern and how to shift it. Runtime ~10–20 min.', '', '', '', 'When did you last say yes when you meant no?', 'THE PEOPLE-PLEASING AUDIT: In three columns: 1. Situations where you consistently say yes when you mean no (be specific). 2. What you fear would happen if you said no. 3. What the realistic outcome would actually be. For column 2: examine the fear carefully. Is it based on evidence — or on an old pattern? For column 3: distinguish between ''they might be temporarily disappointed'' (usually tolerable) and ''there would be a genuine, serious consequence'' (sometimes real). Share: one pattern from column 1 — without necessarily naming the specific person or situation.', 'Write about a relationship where people-pleasing is most active. What are you protecting? What are you sacrificing? What would honest, boundaried engagement actually look like?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Practice a small, low-stakes no today — something where the consequence is mild discomfort rather than serious harm. Notice what happens before, during, and after.', 'Tell one person you are working on this pattern. Ask them to notice when you agree to things that don''t align with your values.', 'Bring back: what happened when you practised the small no this week? What did you fear vs. what actually happened?', '', '', 'I am not defined by other people''s approval. My authenticity is a contribution, not a risk.', 'People-pleasing is often seen as a virtue — be clear that the session is not encouraging selfishness, but rather distinguishing between genuine care (choosing to help from a full place) and fear-based compliance (saying yes to manage anxiety). Some people will realise their entire relationship history has been shaped by this pattern. Go gently.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Scarcity thinking is one of the most pervasive and unexamined belief systems in contemporary life. It runs in the background of most decisions — there isn''t enough time, money, love, opportunity, or worthiness to go around. This week we examine the scarcity operating system and explore what becomes possible when we uninstall it.', 'Complete this sentence: ''There is never enough...'' What came up most quickly? Time? Money? Love? Recognition? Worthiness? That''s your dominant scarcity programme.', 'Scarcity thinking is one of the most pervasive and unexamined belief systems in contemporary life. It runs in the background of most decisions — there isn''t enough time, money, love, opportunity, or worthiness to go around. This week we examine the scarcity operating system and explore what becomes possible when we uninstall it.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iCvmsMzlF7o', 'TED Talk: ''The Scarcity Trap: Why We Keep Digging When We''re Stuck in a Hole'' — Sendhil Mullainathan. Evidence-based exploration of how scarcity thinking shapes behaviour and cognition. Runtime ~15 min.', '', '', '', 'What do you hold back on, in case there isn''t enough?', 'SCARCITY AUDIT: In your journal, explore which domains your scarcity thinking is most active: time, money, love/connection, recognition/success, worthiness. For each active domain: What is the specific fear? Is the scarcity real and current — or is it inherited, historical, or projected? What decisions have you made from this scarcity that you wouldn''t make from abundance? What would you do differently if you genuinely believed there was enough? Share: one domain where scarcity thinking runs most strongly — and one decision it has driven.', 'Write about a relationship in your life where you''ve been operating from scarcity — guarding connection, withholding yourself, competing rather than collaborating. What would that relationship look like if you approached it from genuine abundance?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Notice one scarcity thought today — ''there isn''t enough time / I''m not enough / there won''t be enough.'' Ask: is this actually true right now? Or is it a pattern running on old data?', 'Tell someone about a scarcity pattern you''re unlearning. Share specifically what abundance in that area would feel and look like.', 'Bring back: where did you notice scarcity thinking running this week — and what happened when you questioned it?', '', '', 'There is enough. I am enough. And I generate more of both when I believe this.', 'Scarcity around worthiness (''I am not enough'') is particularly prevalent and often connects back to Week 2 (stories we carry) and Week 9 (wounds we carry). This session can land very deep — allow adequate time for the journalling component. The distinction between genuine material scarcity and inherited/projected scarcity is important to hold carefully.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

We are relational beings. The relationships that formed us — primary caregivers, siblings, early friendships, romantic partners, authority figures — have shaped our templates for intimacy, trust, conflict, and belonging. This week we examine those templates honestly, with the goal of choosing which ones to carry forward.', 'Think of the relationship that has most shaped how you love, trust, and connect with others. Not necessarily your most positive relationship — the most formative one. What template did it install?', 'We are relational beings. The relationships that formed us — primary caregivers, siblings, early friendships, romantic partners, authority figures — have shaped our templates for intimacy, trust, conflict, and belonging. This week we examine those templates honestly, with the goal of choosing which ones to carry forward.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WjOowWxOXCg', 'YouTube: Search ''attachment theory explained adults'' or ''John Bowlby attachment theory animated'' for accessible explainers. Also: search ''anxious avoidant attachment adult relationships'' for practical content. Runtime ~10–20 min.', '', '', '', 'What did you learn about love from the people who raised you?', 'RELATIONAL TEMPLATE MAPPING: In your journal, map the key relationships that shaped you: a primary caregiver, a significant early friendship or romantic relationship, an authority figure. For each: What did this relationship teach you about trust, love, conflict, and your own worth in connection? What relational patterns do you now carry that trace back to this relationship? Which of those patterns are assets? Which are limitations? Where do you see these patterns showing up in your current relationships? Share: one pattern you''ve identified — without necessarily naming its origin.', 'Write about one relational pattern you''d like to unlearn. Where did it come from? What function did it originally serve? What would the upgraded version look like?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Notice once today in a relationship interaction when an old template seems to be running. You don''t have to change it — just see it.', 'Tell one trusted person about a relational pattern you''re examining. Ask them if they see it showing up in your relationship with them.', 'Bring back: what did you notice about old templates running in your relationships this week?', '', '', 'I understand how I was shaped by the relationships I''ve been part of. I choose which templates I carry forward.', 'This is potentially the most psychologically rich session of Phase 2. Attachment theory can produce profound recognition and strong emotion. Keep the tone curious and compassionate — this is mapping, not blame. Some participants may need referral to a therapist to do deeper work with what emerges.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

We all developed protective mechanisms — ways of keeping ourselves safe from vulnerability, hurt, and rejection. Those mechanisms were often necessary once. But armour that once protected you can become a prison. This week we examine what we''re defended against, what the defence is costing us, and what becomes possible when we begin to set it down.', 'What is your most reliable piece of emotional armour — the strategy you go to most reliably when you feel vulnerable? Humour? Intellectualising? Disappearing? Overworking? Aggression? Agreeing too quickly?', 'We all developed protective mechanisms — ways of keeping ourselves safe from vulnerability, hurt, and rejection. Those mechanisms were often necessary once. But armour that once protected you can become a prison. This week we examine what we''re defended against, what the defence is costing us, and what becomes possible when we begin to set it down.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iCvmsMzlF7o', 'TED Talk: ''The Power of Vulnerability'' by Brené Brown — the foundational research on armour and what lies on the other side of it. Runtime ~20 min.', '', '', '', 'What are you protecting, and who is it keeping out?', 'ARMOUR AUDIT: In your journal, map your primary armour pieces: What is my main defensive strategy when I feel vulnerable? What specific situations reliably trigger it? What was the original threat this armour was built against? What does it protect me from now — and what does it also block that I actually want? What would I need to feel safe enough to set it down, even temporarily, in one low-risk situation? Share: one armour piece and what it costs you.', 'Write about what you most protect yourself from feeling or showing. What is the most realistic ''worst case'' if that protection came down — and what is the most realistic ''best case''?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Choose one low-risk relationship or situation this week where you deliberately set a small piece of armour down — let something real show. Notice what happens.', 'Tell one person about a defensive strategy you''re examining. Let them respond — and receive the response without retreating.', 'Bring back: what happened when you set a small piece of armour down this week?', '', '', 'I am strong enough to be soft. I choose openness not because danger has disappeared but because connection is worth the risk.', 'The armour session is often the one where people cry. That is appropriate — the armour has often been up for decades. Go slowly. Never push anyone to be more vulnerable than they are ready to be. Model the approach yourself as a facilitator: let something real show in how you hold the room.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Grief is not only about death. It is the appropriate response to any genuine loss — of a relationship, an identity, a version of your future, a belief that no longer holds. Most of us have been taught to get through grief quickly rather than move through it honestly. This week we honour what grief actually is — and what becomes possible on the other side.', 'What is something you''ve lost — a relationship, a life chapter, a version of yourself, a dream — that you haven''t fully grieved? Not because the loss wasn''t real, but because there wasn''t space, or permission, or understanding of what grief actually requires.', 'Grief is not only about death. It is the appropriate response to any genuine loss — of a relationship, an identity, a version of your future, a belief that no longer holds. Most of us have been taught to get through grief quickly rather than move through it honestly. This week we honour what grief actually is — and what becomes possible on the other side.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=khkJkR-ipfw', 'YouTube: David Kessler on the sixth stage of grief — meaning-making after loss. Search ''David Kessler sixth stage grief meaning'' for his talks. Also: search ''post-traumatic growth research'' for wider context. Runtime ~15–20 min.', '', '', '', 'What ended that you have not properly mourned?', 'GRIEF AND GROWTH INVENTORY: In your journal, explore a loss you haven''t fully grieved. Work through: What was lost — be specific and honest? What did that thing represent to you (identity, hope, belonging, safety)? What have you done instead of grieving it (numbed, kept busy, minimised, intellectualised)? What would fully honouring this loss require — what would genuine acknowledgment look like? And: what has this loss — or the process of beginning to grieve it — made possible, or is beginning to make possible? Share: one loss you are beginning to move through more honestly.', 'Write a letter to something or someone you''ve lost — thanking it, honouring it, and consciously saying goodbye.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Allow yourself one grief moment this week — not performed, but real. A few minutes to acknowledge what was lost and what it meant.', 'Tell one person about a loss you''re still carrying. Let them simply witness it — no advice, no fixing, just witnessing.', 'Bring back: what was it like to write the goodbye letter? What shifted?', '', '', 'I honour what I have lost. And in that honouring, I make space for what is coming.', 'CRITICAL: Grief sessions can activate deep and sometimes unexpected material. Ensure the room is safe and unhurried. Have tissues and a quiet space available. Acknowledge at the start that ''loss'' here is broad — relationships, identities, life chapters, not only death. Have grief counselling referral resources available.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Fear is not the problem. Fear is information. But most of us have fear responses that are miscalibrated — firing at situations that don''t warrant the intensity, categorising opportunity as threat, treating discomfort as danger. This week we examine our fear responses, understand their origins, and begin the rewiring.', 'Name a fear that significantly shapes your choices. Now: is this fear about genuine, present-day danger — or about the possibility of discomfort, judgment, failure, or uncertainty?', 'Fear is not the problem. Fear is information. But most of us have fear responses that are miscalibrated — firing at situations that don''t warrant the intensity, categorising opportunity as threat, treating discomfort as danger. This week we examine our fear responses, understand their origins, and begin the rewiring.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RcGyVTAoXEU', 'TED Talk: Search ''fear vs discomfort psychology talk'' or Susan Jeffers ''Feel the Fear and Do It Anyway'' for evidence-based content on fear rewiring. Also: search ''amygdala hijack fear response'' for the neuroscience. Runtime ~15 min.', '', '', '', 'What are you afraid of that has never actually happened?', 'FEAR AUDIT: Map your significant fears in two columns. Column 1: ''Genuine danger'' fears (realistic threats that warrant the alarm). Column 2: ''Discomfort disguised as danger'' fears (situations that are uncomfortable, uncertain, or risky but not genuinely dangerous). For Column 2 fears: What would happen if you moved toward this thing rather than away from it? What have you missed or avoided because of this fear? What''s the smallest possible step toward it? Share: one Column 2 fear and what avoiding it has cost you.', 'Write about one significant fear that has shaped your choices. Be honest about what it has cost you to avoid the feared thing. Then write: what would you do if this fear were calibrated accurately — as discomfort rather than danger?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Walk toward one small Column 2 fear today. Not the biggest one. The smallest accessible one. Report what you notice.', 'Tell one person about a fear you''re rewiring. Ask them to notice when you avoid it — and to gently call it out.', 'Bring back: what happened when you walked toward the small fear? Fear prediction vs. actual experience?', '', '', 'Fear is information. I distinguish danger from discomfort — and I walk toward discomfort.', 'This session complements Phase 1 Week 3 (Pattern Interrupt) — revisit that material if helpful. The Column 2 fear category is often a revelation. Ensure the distinction is clear: this is not about suppressing fear or being reckless. It is about accurate calibration and voluntarily expanding the window of tolerance.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

In Phase 1 we identified the stories we carry. Now, in the final weeks of Phase 2, we do the unlearning. Not all stories can be released immediately — but some of them are ready. This week we identify which stories have passed their use-by date — and practise the deliberate, conscious act of writing a new one.', 'Think of a story about yourself that you''ve been carrying since Phase 1. Now ask: has anything shifted in how you hold that story over the past 12 weeks? Even slightly — has the story loosened?', 'In Phase 1 we identified the stories we carry. Now, in the final weeks of Phase 2, we do the unlearning. Not all stories can be released immediately — but some of them are ready. This week we identify which stories have passed their use-by date — and practise the deliberate, conscious act of writing a new one.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=D9Ihs241zeg', 'TED Talk: ''The Power of Vulnerability'' by Brené Brown — or search specifically ''Dan McAdams narrative identity talk'' for the direct research on personal narrative and identity. Runtime ~15–20 min.', '', '', '', 'What story about yourself protected you once and now costs you?', 'STORY REVISION: Choose one significant limiting story you''ve been carrying. Write the current version — the way you''ve been telling it. Then rewrite it from a more complete perspective: What context have you excluded from the story? What strengths or capacities did you develop in response to the difficult parts? What does the full story — including hardship AND growth — actually show about who you are? What would the new story enable that the old story prevents? Share: the ending of the new story — what it now makes possible.', 'Write the final line of your old story. Then write the opening line of the new one.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Tell someone the new story — not as a performance, but as a genuine attempt to live from it for one week. Notice how it changes what you do.', 'Ask one person who knows you well: ''What would you say the story of my life is really about?'' Listen to their answer.', 'Bring back: what was it like to tell the new story? Did it change anything?', '', '', 'I am the author of my story. I write from what is most true, most mine, and most alive.', 'This session is one of the most practically powerful of the year — revisit and build on everything from Phase 1 Week 2. Give generous time for the writing exercise. The distinction between ''denial'' and ''more complete narrative'' is important to hold carefully.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Thirteen weeks of unlearning. Phase 2 closes with integration — taking stock of what has been released, what has been rewired, and what you''re carrying into Phase 3 lighter than you arrived. This is not a summary. It is a ceremony of release — and a threshold into rebuilding.', 'If you had to name the three most significant things you''ve released or loosened in Phase 2 — what are they? Not what you''ve fixed or solved. What you''ve set down, loosened, or begun to move through.', 'Thirteen weeks of unlearning. Phase 2 closes with integration — taking stock of what has been released, what has been rewired, and what you''re carrying into Phase 3 lighter than you arrived. This is not a summary. It is a ceremony of release — and a threshold into rebuilding.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sPOuCd6cBao', 'YouTube: ''This Is Water'' — David Foster Wallace animated. One of the most profound short pieces of content on awareness, choice, and the ongoing work of conscious living. Runtime ~9 min.', '', '', '', 'What have you set down, and what is still in your hands?', 'RELEASE CEREMONY: In your journal, write — or if the group is willing, read aloud — a release statement for Phase 2. Include: what you arrived with that you are setting down, what has shifted in how you see yourself, what you are moving into Phase 3 carrying, and one genuine commitment for the rebuild. If the group is willing: share one item from your release statement — witnessed in silence by those around you. Then: a moment of deliberate silence together. Acknowledge what has been done.', 'Write a letter to the version of you who began Phase 2 — thirteen weeks ago. What do you want them to know? What have you released that they were still holding?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Revisit Week 14 journal entries — what has shifted between the beginning and end of Phase 2?', 'Tell someone who isn''t in this group: ''I''ve been doing some deep work on releasing things that no longer serve me. One thing that''s genuinely lighter is...'' Notice what it feels like to own that.', 'Come to the final Phase 2 session ready to share your release statement — or one line from it.', '', '', 'I have released what no longer serves me. I arrive at Phase 3 with cleared ground and an open hand.', 'Create ceremony for this closing — as with Phase 1 Week 13, this deserves ritual. The release statement read aloud in witnessed silence is one of the most powerful moments of the year. Ensure the transition to Phase 3 carries genuine anticipation — the group has done extraordinary work. Honour it fully.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Having released much of what was inherited, imposed, or outdated in Phase 2, the question that opens Phase 3 is genuinely new: who are you now? Not the story you were given, not the role you were assigned — but the person currently standing on cleared ground, with the ability to consciously author what comes next.', 'If someone who didn''t know your history — didn''t know what you''d done, what roles you''d played, what others had said about you — met you today, what would they discover? Who actually shows up when the performance and the history are set aside?', 'Having released much of what was inherited, imposed, or outdated in Phase 2, the question that opens Phase 3 is genuinely new: who are you now? Not the story you were given, not the role you were assigned — but the person currently standing on cleared ground, with the ability to consciously author what comes next.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iG9CE55wbtY', 'TED Talk: ''Why You Should Define Your Fears Instead of Your Goals'' by Tim Ferriss — about moving from fear-driven identity toward values-driven identity. Also search ''Dan McAdams narrative identity'' for the research. Runtime ~13 min.', '', '', '', 'If nobody had told you who you were, who would you be?', 'IDENTITY INVENTORY: In your journal, complete these prompts from a fresh perspective — not from your history, but from your current experiencing: ''When I am most alive, I am...'' / ''The qualities I most want to embody are...'' / ''What I am building toward is...'' / ''The person I am becoming believes...'' / ''What feels most true about who I am right now is...'' Now look at what you''ve written. Does it match how you''re currently living? Where is the greatest alignment? Where is the greatest gap? Share: one quality from your identity inventory that you want to build toward.', 'Write a ''living biography'' of yourself — not what has happened, but who you are in terms of values, qualities, and direction. Write it in present tense, as if it''s already true.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Live from one quality in your identity inventory today — something you said you are, or want to be. Notice what it changes.', 'Tell one person: ''Something I''m building in myself right now is...'' Let yourself own it out loud.', 'Bring back: what happened when you lived from the identity quality you named? What felt true?', '', '', 'I am the author of who I am becoming. I build from values, from clarity, and from honest self-knowledge.', 'This is one of the most energising sessions of the year — after two phases of looking and releasing, the rebuild feels genuinely exciting. Keep the identity inventory fresh and forward-looking — resist the pull back into history. The ''who are you without your story?'' question can be profoundly disorienting and liberating simultaneously.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Values are not what we say we believe — they are what we demonstrate through our choices, our time, and our energy. Most people have never explicitly identified their core values. Most people''s lives are organised around values they absorbed — approval, security, success — rather than values they chose. This week we get explicit.', 'Make a quick list: what do you say your values are? Now check: how much of your time, energy, and money last week actually reflected those values? The gap between stated and lived values is the most important diagnostic tool available.', 'Values are not what we say we believe — they are what we demonstrate through our choices, our time, and our energy. Most people have never explicitly identified their core values. Most people''s lives are organised around values they absorbed — approval, security, success — rather than values they chose. This week we get explicit.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jHeeHg_MXNE', 'YouTube: Search ''values clarification ACT therapy Steven Hayes'' or ''knowing your values psychology'' for evidence-based content on values-based living. Also: search ''Russ Harris ACT values talk'' for highly accessible content. Runtime ~15 min.', '', '', '', 'What would you not trade, whatever you were offered for it?', 'VALUES EXCAVATION: In your journal, work through these steps. First, list everything that you would say you value. Then: for each item, ask — is this genuinely mine, or inherited? Is it a means (to get something else) or an end (valuable in itself)? Narrow to your top 5 genuine, chosen values. For each, write: how would my life look different if I lived this value fully? Where am I most and least aligned with it right now? Finally: rank them. When they conflict — and they will — which wins? Share: your top three values and one place they currently show up in your life.', 'Write a personal values statement — not a list, but a paragraph describing the kind of person you are choosing to be, through the lens of your top values. Make it something you could actually live from.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Make one decision today explicitly from your top value — not habit, not fear, not approval-seeking. Just the value. Notice what it feels like.', 'Share your top three values with someone who knows you well. Ask them if they see those values in how you currently live. Receive the answer honestly.', 'Bring back: where did you live most fully from your values this week — and where did you notice the gap?', '', '', 'My values are mine — chosen, explicit, lived. They are the architecture of how I build.', 'The stated vs. lived values gap exercise is often a significant reveal — many people discover they are living primarily from values they would not consciously choose. Hold space for the discomfort of that recognition. The values ranking exercise (when they conflict, which wins?) generates the most productive discussion.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

In Phase 1 we mapped existing habits. In Phase 3 we build new ones — deliberately, from identity, aligned with values. Not willpower-based habits that exhaust and fail, but identity-based habits that compound quietly into the person you are becoming. This is where the rebuild becomes daily.', 'Think of one habit — something you do or don''t do regularly — that is most misaligned with the person you said you want to become in Week 27. What''s the gap between the habit and the identity? What single small shift would start to close it?', 'In Phase 1 we mapped existing habits. In Phase 3 we build new ones — deliberately, from identity, aligned with values. Not willpower-based habits that exhaust and fail, but identity-based habits that compound quietly into the person you are becoming. This is where the rebuild becomes daily.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W1eYrhGeffc', 'YouTube: James Clear on atomic habits and identity-based change — widely available and directly relevant. Also: search ''BJ Fogg tiny habits TED Talk'' for the minimum viable habit approach. Runtime ~15–20 min.', '', '', '', 'What do you do every day that is quietly making you someone?', 'HABIT ARCHITECTURE: Choose three habits you want to install — one per domain: mind (thinking/learning), body (physical), relationship (connection). For each: State the identity it expresses (''I am the kind of person who...''). Define it in its smallest possible form — what is the minimum viable version that still moves the needle? Identify the habit stack anchor — what existing habit will it follow? Design the environment — what change to your physical space will make this easier? Set the success measure — not perfection, but minimum threshold. Share: your minimum viable habit for one domain.', 'Design your three-habit architecture in writing. Make it specific, small, anchored, and environmentally supported.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Start ONE of your three habits today — just the minimum viable version. No more than 5 minutes. The point is showing up, not performing.', 'Tell one person your identity-based habit — ''I am the kind of person who...'' and the habit it generates. Ask them to hold you to it.', 'Bring back: how many days did you show up for your minimum habit? What got in the way — and what helped?', '', '', 'I build who I am becoming through small, consistent daily practice. Every repetition is a vote for that identity.', 'This is one of the most practically valuable sessions of the year — spend generous time on the habit architecture exercise. The minimum viable habit concept often surprises people (''it''s so small — can it actually work?''). Explain the identity mechanism: the small act is a vote. The votes compound.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

The body is not the vehicle that carries you through your personal development journey — it IS the journey. Sleep, movement, nourishment, and breath are not the lifestyle habits you''ll get to once the important work is done. They are the substrate of every other capacity: attention, emotional regulation, resilience, creativity, and connection all run on physiological hardware.', 'Rate yourself honestly in four areas on a scale of 1–10: sleep (quantity and quality), movement (frequency and variety), nourishment (how well you actually feed yourself), nervous system regulation (capacity to return to calm after stress). What does this tell you about the foundation you''re building on?', 'The body is not the vehicle that carries you through your personal development journey — it IS the journey. Sleep, movement, nourishment, and breath are not the lifestyle habits you''ll get to once the important work is done. They are the substrate of every other capacity: attention, emotional regulation, resilience, creativity, and connection all run on physiological hardware.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5MuIMqhT8oY', 'YouTube: ''Sleep is Your Superpower'' by Matthew Walker — the most important sleep research available, presented accessibly. Runtime ~19 min. Also: search ''exercise antidepressant research'' for the movement evidence base.', '', '', '', 'What does your body need that you have been overriding?', 'BODY FOUNDATION AUDIT: For each of the four areas (sleep, movement, nourishment, nervous system), write: current state honestly, what the gap is between current and what you know you need, and one specific, small change that would most move the needle. Prioritise — which of the four is most foundational for everything else? That one comes first. Share: your highest-leverage body foundation change and the specific small version of it.', 'Write a ''body foundation protocol'' — your non-negotiable minimums for sleep, movement, nourishment, and regulation this week. Make it realistic, not aspirational.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Implement one body foundation habit today — the smallest possible version. If it''s sleep: go to bed 15 minutes earlier. If it''s movement: take a 10-minute walk. If it''s regulation: three extended exhale breaths before any stressful moment.', 'Tell one person about your body foundation priority. Ask them about theirs — and share what you each notice about the connection between physical state and everything else.', 'Bring back: what happened when you prioritised your body foundation this week? What changed in your energy, mood, or capacity?', '', '', 'My body is not separate from my growth. It is the ground it grows from.', 'Approach this session with warmth and zero judgment — most adults are chronically under-resourced physiologically and many feel shame about it. The key insight is that body care is not a luxury or a sign of having it together — it is the substrate everything else runs on. Start with sleep, which has the highest leverage of all.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

You are a relational being. The people you spend the most time with are not just company — they are a constant source of input that shapes your nervous system, your beliefs, your ambitions, and your sense of what is possible. Rebuilding means becoming intentional about that input.', 'Think of the five people you spend the most time with. What does each one bring into your nervous system — expansion or contraction? Energy or depletion? Who you are becoming — or who you''ve been?', 'You are a relational being. The people you spend the most time with are not just company — they are a constant source of input that shapes your nervous system, your beliefs, your ambitions, and your sense of what is possible. Rebuilding means becoming intentional about that input.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q4g_cxMWnMk', 'YouTube: Robert Waldinger ''What Makes a Good Life?'' — the Harvard Study of Adult Development findings on relationships and flourishing. One of the most important talks of this programme. Runtime ~13 min.', '', '', '', 'Who do you become around the people you spend most time with?', 'RELATIONSHIP AUDIT: Map your significant relationships in three columns. Column 1: Relationships that expand you — leave you feeling more alive, more yourself, more possible. Column 2: Neutral relationships — neither expanding nor depleting. Column 3: Relationships that consistently contract you — leave you feeling less of yourself, more anxious, or more stuck. Now: are there relationships in Column 3 that you are maintaining out of obligation, guilt, or habit rather than genuine care? Are there relationships in Column 1 that you''re not investing in sufficiently? Share: one relationship you want to invest more in — and why.', 'Write about the community you are building — both the relationships already present that you want to deepen, and the kinds of people you want to attract into your life as you grow.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Reach out to one Column 1 relationship today — someone who expands you. Tell them specifically what you value about their presence in your life.', 'Tell one person about your intention to be more intentional about your social environment. Ask them: ''Do you think you''re one of my expanding relationships?'' Be willing to hear the answer.', 'Bring back: what happened when you invested in a Column 1 relationship this week?', '', '', 'I choose my community with the same care I bring to everything else I''m building. My relationships are part of my practice.', 'The relationship energy audit can be confronting — some people will realise that relationships they feel obligated to maintain are significant sources of depletion. Hold space for that without prescribing action. The goal is awareness and intentionality, not wholesale relationship restructuring.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

In Phase 1 we identified the inner critic. In Phase 2 we built the inner coach. In Phase 3 we practise the daily language — the specific quality of internal dialogue that becomes the running soundtrack of a life. The way you habitually speak to yourself is the water you swim in. This week we make it deliberately nourishing.', 'If your inner voice were recorded for the past 24 hours and played back to you — what would it sound like? What would be its dominant tone? Its most repeated themes? Would you choose to live inside that soundtrack?', 'In Phase 1 we identified the inner critic. In Phase 2 we built the inner coach. In Phase 3 we practise the daily language — the specific quality of internal dialogue that becomes the running soundtrack of a life. The way you habitually speak to yourself is the water you swim in. This week we make it deliberately nourishing.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NiuDFBNDoSk', 'YouTube: Ethan Kross on self-talk and self-distancing — search ''Ethan Kross self-talk research'' for his talks. Also highly relevant: search ''inner dialogue quality psychology research.'' Runtime ~15 min.', '', '', '', 'What would you say to someone you loved who was where you are?', 'SELF-TALK REDESIGN: Spend one week tracking your internal dialogue in three moments each day: morning (on waking), during difficulty, and at the end of the day. For each moment: What is the actual tone and content of your self-talk? Is it accurate, compassionate, and useful? If you were talking to your best friend in this situation, what would you say instead? Design your preferred version. Share: one common self-talk pattern you''re redesigning — and what the redesigned version sounds like.', 'Write five ''anchor phrases'' — specific sentences you can use as your daily self-talk soundtrack in key moments: waking, difficulty, failure, success, and end of day. Make them genuinely yours — not borrowed affirmations.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Use your anchor phrase when you wake up tomorrow. Notice what it sets up for the day.', 'Share your anchor phrases with one person. Ask them what phrases they use — and what phrases they wish they had.', 'Bring back: what happened when you used your anchor phrases this week? What shifted in tone?', '', '', 'The way I speak to myself becomes the life I inhabit. I choose words that build, that honour, and that tell the truth.', 'This is one of the highest practical-impact sessions of Phase 3 — anchor phrases that are genuinely used daily produce measurable change in mood and self-efficacy over weeks. Help people create phrases that are genuinely theirs — not borrowed, not performed. ''I''m doing my best and that is enough today'' lands differently from ''I am amazing.''', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Most people relate to structure as something imposed — schedules, systems, rules that constrain. The rebuild inverts this: structure is a tool of freedom. A thoughtfully designed daily architecture reduces decision fatigue, protects your values, and creates the conditions in which your best work, your deepest connections, and your genuine rest can all happen.', 'Describe your current daily structure — or lack of it. What happens to your time, energy, and attention on a typical day? Where does it go that you don''t fully choose? And what important things consistently get crowded out?', 'Most people relate to structure as something imposed — schedules, systems, rules that constrain. The rebuild inverts this: structure is a tool of freedom. A thoughtfully designed daily architecture reduces decision fatigue, protects your values, and creates the conditions in which your best work, your deepest connections, and your genuine rest can all happen.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gTaJhjQHcf8', 'YouTube: Cal Newport on deep work and time blocking — search ''Cal Newport deep work time blocking'' for accessible talks. Also: search ''decision fatigue psychology Roy Baumeister'' for the cognitive load research. Runtime ~15 min.', '', '', '', 'What in your week is structure, and what is just habit?', 'DAILY ARCHITECTURE DESIGN: Map your ideal week in three tiers: 1. Non-negotiables — the anchor activities that must happen for you to function well (sleep, movement, key work blocks, connection time). 2. Important but flexible — activities that matter but can move. 3. Fillers — things that happen by default that you''re not actively choosing. Now: what needs to be protected by explicit scheduling? What ''filler'' could be reduced or removed to create space for what matters? Design your minimum viable weekly architecture. Share: your top non-negotiable and one filler you''re consciously reducing.', 'Write your minimum viable weekly architecture — the non-negotiable anchors of a week that actually serves you.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Implement one structural protection this week — block one important time in your calendar as non-negotiable. Treat it with the same respect as a meeting with your most important client.', 'Tell one person about the structural change you''re making. Ask them to support you in protecting that time.', 'Bring back: what happened when you protected your non-negotiable time this week? What did you notice?', '', '', 'My structure serves my values. I design my days to protect what matters most.', 'Structure design is highly personal — resist the urge to prescribe specific systems. Help people find the minimum viable architecture for their specific life circumstances. The ''best day'' reflection is powerful — people often already know what their ideal structure looks like; they just haven''t made it explicit or protected it.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Most of us treat rest as what happens after the work is done — the reward for sufficient productivity. This is backwards. Rest is not the recovery from life. It is the condition in which life''s highest-quality work, deepest connections, and most genuine insights become possible. This week we rebuild our relationship with rest.', 'When did you last experience genuine rest — not sleep, not distraction, not productive recovery, but genuine rest: a quality of being fully present in a nourishing activity without any performance agenda? How long ago was it?', 'Most of us treat rest as what happens after the work is done — the reward for sufficient productivity. This is backwards. Rest is not the recovery from life. It is the condition in which life''s highest-quality work, deepest connections, and most genuine insights become possible. This week we rebuild our relationship with rest.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9y1xyXtYAsg', 'YouTube: Alex Soojung-Kim Pang on rest and performance — search ''Alex Pang rest book talk'' for his talks. Also: search ''default mode network creativity rest brain'' for the neuroscience. Runtime ~15–20 min.', '', '', '', 'When did you last rest without guilt?', 'REST AUDIT: In your journal, examine your relationship with rest. When do you rest — and what does it actually look like? Distinguish between: genuine rest (nourishing, restorative, non-performance), distraction (stimulating without recovering), and productive recovery (deliberately recovering to perform better). Which of these dominates your non-work time? What does genuine rest actually look like for you specifically — the activities, the conditions, the quality of attention? Design one genuine rest practice for this week. Share: what genuine rest looks and feels like for you.', 'Write a ''rest manifesto'' — what genuine rest looks like for you, what it requires, and what you commit to protecting this week.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Schedule one genuine rest practice this week — not earned, not conditional on productivity. Just scheduled, like any other important appointment.', 'Tell one person you are practising rest as a non-negotiable. Invite them to try it too — and compare notes.', 'Bring back: what happened during your scheduled rest? What did you notice — about the quality of it, and about what followed it?', '', '', 'Rest is not a reward. It is a practice — and it is what makes everything else sustainable.', 'The rest session often provokes strong responses from high-achievers who have deeply internalised productivity culture. The 3-minute silence exercise is deliberately confronting — the discomfort is the point. Validate the discomfort and explore it rather than skipping past it. The distinction between rest and distraction is often revelatory.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Creativity is not a talent possessed by some and absent in others. It is a fundamental human capacity — the ability to make meaning, to express what is true, to bring something new into existence. When creativity is absent from a life, something essential goes unexpressed. This week we reclaim it.', 'What did you love to make, create, or express when you were a child — before it was evaluated, before there was an audience, before you decided whether you were ''good'' at it? What happened to that?', 'Creativity is not a talent possessed by some and absent in others. It is a fundamental human capacity — the ability to make meaning, to express what is true, to bring something new into existence. When creativity is absent from a life, something essential goes unexpressed. This week we reclaim it.', 'YouTube: Search ''creativity intrinsic motivation Teresa Amabile'' or ''Mihaly Csikszentmihalyi flow TED Talk'' for the research foundation. Also: Elizabeth Gilbert ''Your Elusive Creative Genius'' is perfect for this session. Runtime ~19 min.', 'Search: ''Elizabeth Gilbert creative genius TED Talk'' or ''Mihaly Csikszentmihalyi flow TED Talk'' if unavailable. Book: ''Big Magic'' by Elizabeth Gilbert is essential reading for this session.', '', '', '', 'What did you love making before anyone told you if you were good at it?', 'CREATIVITY RECLAMATION: In your journal, explore: What creative expressions were most alive in you in childhood? What happened to them — when did you stop, and why? What creative impulses arise in you now — ideas, images, things you notice you want to make or say — that you don''t act on? Design a minimal creative practice for this week — one that bypasses the inner critic by making the practice private, judgment-free, and purely for you. Share: one creative impulse you''re going to act on this week.', 'Start something creative this week — not to finish, not to share, not to evaluate. Just to begin. Five minutes. Something genuine. Do it before you have time to talk yourself out of it.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Tell one person about a creative impulse you''ve been suppressing. See what happens when you say it out loud.', 'Bring back: what did you create this week — and what was the quality of the experience of making it?', 'I am a creative being. Expression is part of my practice and part of how I know myself.', '', '', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iG9CE55wbtY', '', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Purpose is not a destination to find — it is a direction to orient toward. It is not assigned at birth or discovered in a single moment — it is cultivated through honest reflection on what you care about, what you''re good at, what the world needs, and what gives you energy. This week we orient.', 'What are you doing when you feel most useful, most alive, and most yourself — all at once? It doesn''t have to be your job. It doesn''t have to be grand. What activity or contribution produces that specific intersection?', 'Purpose is not a destination to find — it is a direction to orient toward. It is not assigned at birth or discovered in a single moment — it is cultivated through honest reflection on what you care about, what you''re good at, what the world needs, and what gives you energy. This week we orient.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fLJsdqxnZb0', 'TED Talk: ''How to Find Work You Love'' by Scott Dinsmore — practical and evidence-based exploration of purpose-oriented work. Runtime ~18 min. Also: Viktor Frankl''s ''Man''s Search for Meaning'' is the foundational text for this session.', '', '', '', 'What are you doing when you lose track of time?', 'PURPOSE EXPLORATION: In your journal, work through the Ikigai framework: What do I love — what activities make time disappear, what could I talk about or do for hours? What am I good at — what comes naturally, what do others consistently come to me for? What does the world need — what problems matter to me, what would I address if I could? Where do these overlap? What sits at the centre — even approximately, even imperfectly? Share: the approximate direction of your purpose — not a definitive statement, but an honest orientation.', 'Write a purpose statement — not as a final answer but as a current honest orientation. ''I am here to...'' Make it true to where you are right now.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Live from your purpose statement for one day — make one small choice from that orientation. Notice how it changes the texture of the day.', 'Share your purpose direction with one person. Ask them what they see as your natural contribution. Listen fully.', 'Bring back: what happened when you lived from your purpose orientation today?', '', '', 'I have a direction that is genuinely mine. I orient toward it daily — and the world receives something only I can give.', 'Purpose discussions can produce both profound clarity and profound anxiety — particularly for people who feel they ''should'' have found their purpose by now. Normalise: purpose is an orientation, not a destination. The question ''what is genuinely mine to give?'' is more accessible than ''what is my life''s purpose?''', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Few areas of human life carry more inherited story, more unexamined shame, more contradictory programming than money and material resources. We rebuild this relationship not from financial advice, but from honest self-inquiry: what stories were you given about money, what do they cost you, and what would a genuinely healthy, values-aligned relationship with resources look and feel like?', 'Complete these sentences without thinking: ''Money is...'' / ''People who have a lot of money are...'' / ''I am the kind of person who...'' with respect to finances. Now: whose voice just spoke? Where did those beliefs come from?', 'Few areas of human life carry more inherited story, more unexamined shame, more contradictory programming than money and material resources. We rebuild this relationship not from financial advice, but from honest self-inquiry: what stories were you given about money, what do they cost you, and what would a genuinely healthy, values-aligned relationship with resources look and feel like?', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8gxNHkQBkF8', 'YouTube: Search ''money scripts psychology Brad Klontz'' or ''behavioural economics money decisions'' for the research foundation. Also: search ''money and happiness research Killingsworth'' for the wellbeing dimension. Runtime ~15–20 min.', '', '', '', 'What did you learn about money before you were old enough to question it?', 'MONEY STORY AUDIT: In your journal, explore your inherited money story: What was the dominant financial culture of your upbringing? What messages did you receive — explicitly or implicitly — about money, wealth, and your relationship to it? What is your current money script (avoidance, worship, status, or vigilance)? Where does it help you — and where does it cost you? What would a values-aligned relationship with money look like — one in which money serves your genuine priorities rather than driving anxiety or shame? Share: one inherited money story and what it has cost you.', 'Write a ''values-aligned financial direction statement'' — not a budget, but a paragraph describing what right relationship with money would look and feel like for you.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Make one financial decision this week that is explicitly aligned with your values rather than driven by habit, anxiety, or inherited script.', 'Share your money story with one trusted person — the inherited version, not the financial details. Notice what it feels like to examine it openly.', 'Bring back: what happened when you made a values-aligned financial choice this week?', '', '', 'My relationship with money is built on values, not fear. I use resources in alignment with what I genuinely care about.', 'This session requires careful framing — avoid anything that feels like financial advice (refer to professionals for that). The focus is entirely on the psychological and values dimensions: inherited stories, emotional patterns, and alignment with explicit values. Some people will be dealing with genuine financial hardship — hold space for that with compassion.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Human beings are not designed for isolation. We are designed for community — the sustained experience of being known, belonging, contributing, and being contributed to by a group with shared values and shared life. Most contemporary adults are chronically under-communal. Phase 3 closes by rebuilding community as a deliberate practice.', 'Describe the quality of your current community life. Not the number of relationships — but the quality of belonging. Do you have a group of people who know you genuinely, who share your values, who challenge and support you? Or are you doing this largely alone?', 'Human beings are not designed for isolation. We are designed for community — the sustained experience of being known, belonging, contributing, and being contributed to by a group with shared values and shared life. Most contemporary adults are chronically under-communal. Phase 3 closes by rebuilding community as a deliberate practice.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q4g_cxMWnMg', 'YouTube: Robert Waldinger ''What Makes a Good Life?'' Harvard Study findings — the definitive research on community, relationships, and flourishing. Also search ''loneliness epidemic research Johann Hari'' for the cost of disconnection. Runtime ~13 min.', '', '', '', 'What do you bring that a room is worse off without?', 'COMMUNITY AUDIT: In your journal, map your current community life: Where do you experience genuine belonging — being known, valued, and included for who you actually are? Where are you present but not truly belonging — performing rather than participating? What kind of community are you actively building — or could build — around your values and your growth? What one specific commitment to community could you make this week? Share: one community commitment you''re making.', 'Write a community vision statement — not for a formal group, but for the quality of communal life you are actively building: what it feels like, who is in it, what you are contributing, and what you are receiving.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Make one community investment this week — show up more fully to an existing group, reach out to someone you want to know better, or take one step toward building something new.', 'Tell someone in your community what their presence in your life means. Be specific.', 'Bring back: what happened when you invested in community this week? What did it feel like?', '', '', 'I am building community — not as a supplement to my life, but as one of its foundations.', 'This session has particular resonance for Mindcast LIVE as a community specifically — name it. The group in the room has been building community for 38 weeks. That is the concrete example of what this session is about. Celebrate it explicitly. Use this session to deepen the bonds already present.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Thirteen weeks of rebuilding. Phase 3 closes with integration — taking stock of the identity that has been constructed, the habits that have been planted, the values that have been named, the community that has been invested in. This is not a summary. It is a threshold into Phase 4: Live It.', 'What are the three most significant things you have built in Phase 3 — not accomplished or resolved, but genuinely built? What is present in you now that wasn''t present 13 weeks ago?', 'Thirteen weeks of rebuilding. Phase 3 closes with integration — taking stock of the identity that has been constructed, the habits that have been planted, the values that have been named, the community that has been invested in. This is not a summary. It is a threshold into Phase 4: Live It.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sPOuCd6cBao', 'YouTube: ''This Is Water'' by David Foster Wallace — the perfect closing reflection on awareness, choice, and the ongoing practice of conscious living. Runtime ~9 min.', '', '', '', 'What is different about how you live now?', 'REBUILD INTEGRATION: In your journal, spend 15 minutes: 1. What identity have I built that I want to carry forward? 2. What values am I now living from, explicitly? 3. Which habits are beginning to feel like mine? 4. What relationships have been deepened? 5. What am I now bringing to my community that I wasn''t before? 6. What am I walking into Phase 4 with — and what do I commit to continuing to build? If the group is willing: read one insight aloud — witnessed in silence by everyone present.', 'Write a letter to the version of you who began Phase 3 — thirteen weeks ago. What do you want them to know about what was built? What are you proud of?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Revisit Week 27 journal entries. Notice the gap between who arrived and who is leaving Phase 3.', 'Tell one person who has been part of your community this year: ''Something I have genuinely built in the past 13 weeks is...'' Own it fully.', 'Come to the final Phase 3 session ready to share: what are you bringing into Phase 4?', '', '', 'I have built something real. I arrive at Phase 4 with a foundation, a direction, and a practice.', 'Create ceremony — this is the third major threshold crossing and deserves full honour. The letters read aloud (if people consent) create one of the most moving moments of the year. Ensure Phase 4 is framed with genuine excitement: ''The work of the first three phases has been to develop yourself so you have something real to give. Phase 4 is the giving.'' Build anticipation.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Three phases of inner work — seeing, unlearning, rebuilding — have been preparation for this: the turn outward. Phase 4 is not about more self-development. It is about the natural expression of genuine development: service. When you have done the inner work, you have something real to give. This week we make the turn.', 'What has this year''s inner work given you that you did not have before? And who in your life — or your community — could genuinely benefit from what you now carry?', 'Three phases of inner work — seeing, unlearning, rebuilding — have been preparation for this: the turn outward. Phase 4 is not about more self-development. It is about the natural expression of genuine development: service. When you have done the inner work, you have something real to give. This week we make the turn.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lmyZMtPVodo', 'TED Talk: ''Why Good Things Happen to Good People'' — search for research-based talks on the health benefits of service and generosity. Also: search ''Viktor Frankl meaning service talk'' for the philosophical foundation. Runtime ~15 min.', '', '', '', 'Who is better off because of the work you''ve done this year?', 'SERVICE INVENTORY: In your journal, explore: What capacities, insights, or qualities have you developed this year that could genuinely benefit others? Who specifically — in your immediate relationships, your community, or the wider world — could use what you have to offer? What form of service feels most aligned with your values and your nature (from Week 28 and 36)? What is the smallest possible act of genuine service you could take this week — not grand, just real? Share: one capacity you want to offer outward.', 'Write a ''service offering'' — not a formal commitment, just an honest statement of what you now have to give and who you want to give it to.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Make one small act of service today — not grand, not performed. Something genuine, from fullness, offered freely.', 'Tell one person: ''Something I''ve been through this year has given me something I want to offer. Can I share it with you?'' And then share it.', 'Bring back: what happened when you offered something from your inner work outward? How did it land?', '', '', 'I have done the inner work. Now I give what I have grown — freely, genuinely, from fullness.', 'This is a pivotal session — the conceptual pivot from inward to outward. It should feel genuinely exciting, not like an obligation. The distinction between service-from-fullness and service-from-depletion (people-pleasing) is essential to make clearly. Reference Phase 2 Week 19 explicitly.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

The deepest form of learning is teaching. When you explain what you know to someone else — when you put your understanding into words that another person can receive — you discover what you actually know versus what you only think you know. Phase 4 includes teaching as a practice, not just an activity.', 'Think of the single most important insight from this year''s work — the thing that has most changed how you see yourself or how you move through the world. Now: could you explain it clearly to someone who has never done this work? Try it right now, out loud or in writing.', 'The deepest form of learning is teaching. When you explain what you know to someone else — when you put your understanding into words that another person can receive — you discover what you actually know versus what you only think you know. Phase 4 includes teaching as a practice, not just an activity.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FLbqzbAaEiI', 'YouTube: Search ''protégé effect learning by teaching research'' or ''Feynman technique learning explained'' for the evidence base. Runtime ~10 min.', '', '', '', 'What do you know now that you wish someone had told you?', 'TEACHING PREPARATION: Choose one insight from this year that you want to transmit. Write it as if explaining it to someone who has never heard it — in plain language, with a concrete example, and with an honest account of how it changed you. Test it on someone today: share it in conversation and notice where it lands clearly and where it gets murky. That murkiness is where you still have learning to do. Share: the insight you are most ready to teach — and one place where trying to explain it revealed a gap.', 'Write a ''teaching letter'' — an explanation of your most important insight from this year, written for someone who is just beginning the inner work you''ve done.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Share something you''ve learned this year with one person today — not as advice, but as honest sharing of your own experience.', 'Ask one person: ''Can I share something I''ve been learning this year?'' Then share your teaching letter version of it. Notice what lands.', 'Bring back: what happened when you tried to teach your most important insight? What did you discover about your own understanding?', '', '', 'The deepest measure of what I''ve learned is whether I can give it away. I teach — and in teaching, I deepen.', 'The ''try to explain it and notice the gaps'' exercise is one of the most practically powerful of Phase 4. Build in genuine time for people to attempt this in pairs in the room — not just plan to do it later. The discomfort of discovering gaps in articulation is productive and important.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Living It — Phase 4 — requires something that all the inner work has been building toward: the courage to be genuinely seen. Not the performance of authenticity, not carefully managed vulnerability, but the actual lived experience of being known — in your community, your work, your relationships — as the person you have genuinely become.', 'Where in your life are you still operating in ''development mode'' — building, preparing, getting ready — rather than actually showing up as who you''ve become? What is preventing you from going live?', 'Living It — Phase 4 — requires something that all the inner work has been building toward: the courage to be genuinely seen. Not the performance of authenticity, not carefully managed vulnerability, but the actual lived experience of being known — in your community, your work, your relationships — as the person you have genuinely become.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iCvmsMzlF7o', 'TED Talk: ''The Power of Vulnerability'' by Brené Brown — the foundational research on the courage to be seen. Runtime ~20 min.', '', '', '', 'What is true about you that you have never let anyone see?', 'VISIBILITY AUDIT: In your journal, map where you are currently visible vs. hidden: In which relationships are you being genuinely seen — as the person you''ve become this year? In which relationships are you still performing the old version of yourself? In which domains (work, community, family, friendship) are you most invisible? What specifically would becoming visible in each domain require — and what is the cost of staying hidden? Share: one domain where you''re ready to be more genuinely seen.', 'Write a declaration: ''This is who I actually am now. This is what I am no longer willing to hide.'' You don''t have to share it — but write it as if you will.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Show up more genuinely today in one interaction — stop managing one thing you usually manage. Let someone see something real.', 'Tell one person: ''I want you to know me as I actually am now, not who I was before this year.'' Then show them. One genuine thing.', 'Bring back: what happened when you let yourself be a little more seen? What surprised you?', '', '', 'I am ready to be seen — not performed, not managed, but genuinely known. That is the practice.', 'This session builds on everything from Phase 1 Week 10 (masks) and Phase 2 Week 22 (armour). Reference both explicitly. The shift from ''development mode'' to ''production'' is a framing that resonates with many adults who have been doing inner work for years without translating it into how they live publicly.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Values are easy to hold in quiet moments. The test is whether they hold under pressure — when it costs something to live them, when the easier path is compromise, when the people around you expect something different. This week is about the practice of values-integrity when it genuinely matters.', 'Think of the last time you compromised a value you explicitly named in Week 28 — not a small slip, but a meaningful choice to act against what you said mattered. What happened? And what does that moment tell you about the gap between stated and lived values?', 'Values are easy to hold in quiet moments. The test is whether they hold under pressure — when it costs something to live them, when the easier path is compromise, when the people around you expect something different. This week is about the practice of values-integrity when it genuinely matters.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jHeeHg_MXNE', 'YouTube: Search ''moral courage values under pressure psychology'' or ''living your values difficult moments research talk'' for evidence-based content. Runtime ~15 min.', '', '', '', 'When did you last act against your own values, and what was the pressure?', 'PRESSURE-TEST YOUR VALUES: Take your top three values from Week 28. For each, identify: A recent situation where you held this value under pressure — what happened? A recent situation where you compromised it — what happened? A likely future scenario where this value will be tested. Pre-decide now: what will you do in that scenario? Write it specifically enough that you have a rehearsed answer when the moment comes. Share: one value you are pre-deciding to hold under pressure — and the specific scenario.', 'Write your pre-decisions for your top three values under their most likely pressure scenarios.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Today, notice once when a value is under mild pressure. Hold it — even slightly, even imperfectly. Notice what it costs and what it gives.', 'Tell one person about a value you are practising holding under pressure. Ask them to notice if they see you doing it.', 'Bring back: did a value come under pressure this week? What happened? Did the pre-decision help?', '', '', 'My values hold under pressure. Not because I am perfect — because I have practised and pre-decided.', 'The pre-decision technique is one of the most practically powerful of Phase 4. The research on pre-deciding vs. in-the-moment deciding is compelling — share it clearly. This session pairs directly with Phase 3 Week 28 (values) and should explicitly reference the values identified there.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Conflict is not the opposite of growth. For most people it is the primary site of it — the place where values meet reality, where differences become visible, where the quality of all the inner work is actually tested. Most people manage conflict rather than engage it. Phase 4 treats it as a practice.', 'Think of a current or recent conflict that you''ve been managing rather than engaging. What would it mean to engage it honestly — to bring your full, values-aligned self to it rather than managing around it?', 'Conflict is not the opposite of growth. For most people it is the primary site of it — the place where values meet reality, where differences become visible, where the quality of all the inner work is actually tested. Most people manage conflict rather than engage it. Phase 4 treats it as a practice.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l7ToNudVd2I', 'YouTube: Search ''Nonviolent Communication Marshall Rosenberg'' for his foundational talks. Also: search ''John Gottman conflict research relationships'' for the relationship science. Runtime ~15–20 min.', '', '', '', 'What conflict have you been avoiding, and what are you protecting?', 'CONFLICT PRACTICE: Identify a current low-to-moderate conflict or tension in your life. Apply the NVC framework in writing: Observation (what specifically happened — no interpretation). Feeling (what you actually feel — not ''I feel that they...'', but an actual emotion). Need (what underlying value or need of yours is not being met). Request (what specific, actionable thing would genuinely help). Now: is there a conversation you''re ready to have? Share: the observation and feeling from your framework — not the conflict details, but the quality of what it''s like to name these clearly.', 'Write the conversation you want to have — using the NVC framework — that you haven''t had yet. Write your part honestly. Then write what you genuinely hope they might say in response.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'In one difficult interaction today, try to identify the need beneath the behaviour — yours and theirs. Notice what changes when you see it.', 'Have one honest conversation you''ve been avoiding. Use the framework. See what happens.', 'Bring back: what happened when you engaged the conflict rather than managed it?', '', '', 'Conflict is not the opposite of growth. Engaged honestly, it is one of its most powerful forms.', 'The NVC framework is powerful but needs practical time to learn — do the four-step exercise in pairs in the room, not just in journals. Reference Phase 1 Week 11 (seeing others clearly) and Phase 2 projection work explicitly. This session may surface real current conflicts — hold the room carefully.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Generosity is not an occasional act. It is an orientation — a way of moving through the world that sees abundance rather than scarcity, that gives freely from what has been developed and cultivated, that trusts that contribution does not diminish the contributor. Phase 4 cultivates generosity not as a behaviour but as a practice of being.', 'Think about your typical orientation when you arrive at a gathering, a conversation, or a relationship. Do you arrive asking — even unconsciously — ''what will I get from this?'' Or do you arrive asking ''what can I offer here?'' Be honest. Most people operate from the first far more than the second.', 'Generosity is not an occasional act. It is an orientation — a way of moving through the world that sees abundance rather than scarcity, that gives freely from what has been developed and cultivated, that trusts that contribution does not diminish the contributor. Phase 4 cultivates generosity not as a behaviour but as a practice of being.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=M7SBFnFvPeY', 'YouTube: ''Are You a Giver or a Taker?'' by Adam Grant TED Talk — evidence-based and directly relevant to this session. Also: Elizabeth Dunn ''Helping Others Makes Us Happier'' TED Talk. Runtime ~13–15 min.', '', '', '', 'What do you give that costs you nothing and matters to someone?', 'GENEROSITY AUDIT: In your journal, examine your current generosity practice. In what domains — time, attention, money, knowledge, emotional presence — are you genuinely generous? In what domains are you habitually calculating or withholding? What is driving the withholding — scarcity thinking, self-protection, exhaustion, or something else? Design one deliberate act of generosity this week that costs you something real (time, money, or genuine effort) and is given without expectation of return. Share: one domain where you want to develop a more generous orientation.', 'Write a ''generosity commitment'' — not a list of donations, but a description of the quality of presence and orientation you are choosing to practise.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Make one genuinely generous act today — something that costs you something real, given freely, without expectation of return.', 'Tell one person specifically what you appreciate about them — give them something genuine and specific that costs you nothing but attention.', 'Bring back: what happened when you gave generously this week? What did you notice in yourself?', '', '', 'I give from fullness. Generosity is not what I do occasionally — it is who I am becoming.', 'The Adam Grant ''givers vs takers'' research is highly engaging and should be shared in some depth. The distinction between self-erasing generosity and sustainable otherish giving is essential — reference Phase 2 Week 19 people-pleasing explicitly. The ''quality of arrival'' framing is powerful.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Phase 3 Week 20 examined the scarcity mindset. Phase 4 goes further: what does it actually feel like to live from sufficiency — not as a belief, but as a practice? Not as an achievement of having enough, but as a daily orientation that returns to gratitude, presence, and the genuine recognition that what is here, right now, is enough to begin from.', 'What would have to be true for you to feel that you have enough — right now, today — to begin living fully? Not to stop growing, but to stop waiting? Most people''s answer is some future condition. Examine that condition honestly.', 'Phase 3 Week 20 examined the scarcity mindset. Phase 4 goes further: what does it actually feel like to live from sufficiency — not as a belief, but as a practice? Not as an achievement of having enough, but as a daily orientation that returns to gratitude, presence, and the genuine recognition that what is here, right now, is enough to begin from.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oHGKTZSe_k4', 'YouTube: Search ''Lynne Twist soul of money sufficiency talk'' or ''hedonic treadmill research happiness explained'' for the research base. Also: Robert Emmons on gratitude research is widely available. Runtime ~15–20 min.', '', '', '', 'What is already enough that you keep treating as not yet?', 'SUFFICIENCY PRACTICE: In your journal, explore three questions: What do you already have — right now — that is genuinely sufficient to begin living from? (Not what you''ll have when conditions are met, but what is present today.) Where in your life is ''not enough'' thinking most active — and what does it cost you? Design a daily sufficiency practice: one moment each day where you deliberately notice what is already enough. Share: one thing that is genuinely enough that you have been treating as insufficient.', 'Write a daily sufficiency statement — one specific sentence you can say to yourself each morning that honestly names what is already enough to begin from today.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Say your sufficiency statement when you wake up tomorrow. See what it changes about how the day begins.', 'Tell one person what you genuinely have enough of — not what you''re grateful for in general, but one specific thing you recognise as enough right now.', 'Bring back: what happened when you practised the sufficiency statement for one week?', '', '', 'I have enough to begin from. Right now. Today. And from this enough, I continue to grow.', 'The hedonic treadmill research is essential context for this session — it de-pathologises the scarcity drive while showing clearly why it cannot work as a path to genuine sufficiency. The daily sufficiency statement practice is highly practical. Reference Week 20 explicitly as the earlier exploration of this territory.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

We live in a culture of instant feedback, rapid results, and the expectation that growth should be visible and immediate. The inner work done in this year does not follow that rhythm. Some of it has already changed you. Some of it will show up in five years. Some of it you will not understand until you look back. This week is about developing the orientation of the long game.', 'Think of the most significant positive change in your life — one that you can see clearly now but could not see while it was happening. How long did it take? And were you aware of it as it was occurring? What does that tell you about the long game?', 'We live in a culture of instant feedback, rapid results, and the expectation that growth should be visible and immediate. The inner work done in this year does not follow that rhythm. Some of it has already changed you. Some of it will show up in five years. Some of it you will not understand until you look back. This week is about developing the orientation of the long game.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TQMbvJNRpLE', 'YouTube: Search ''Angela Duckworth grit and perseverance TED Talk'' — the foundational research on long-game thinking and persistence. Runtime ~6 min.', '', '', '', 'What are you working on that has not shown results yet?', 'LONG GAME MAPPING: In your journal, write a letter to yourself to be opened in five years. Not a fantasy letter — a grounded one, based on the direction you''ve been building this year. What are you building toward? What do you trust will be true in five years if you continue showing up consistently? What would you want your future self to know you committed to today? Seal it (literally or metaphorically). Share: one thing you are trusting the long game with.', 'Write your long-game intention for the next year — not goals, but direction. The quality of person you are continuing to build toward.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Today, show up for one practice you''ve built this year — not because you can see immediate results, but as a vote for who you are becoming over time.', 'Tell one person: ''Something I''m playing the long game with is...'' — and name specifically what that means for how you''ll show up this week.', 'Bring back: what did it feel like to play the long game deliberately — to act without immediate feedback?', '', '', 'I am building something that takes time. I show up every day. The compound interest is working.', 'The five-year letter exercise is one of the most powerful of Phase 4 — encourage people to actually seal and store it. The compound interest metaphor is worth spending time on. Some people will be impatient with how subtle the year''s changes have felt — this session directly addresses that.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

One of the simplest and most demanding practices available: leaving people better than you found them. Not dramatically better — not rescuing or fixing. Just slightly more seen, more valued, more capable of being themselves because of their encounter with you. This is the lived expression of everything this year has built.', 'Think of someone who has left you genuinely better than they found you — not through dramatic intervention, but through the consistent quality of their presence and their regard. What specifically did they do? What was the quality of their attention?', 'One of the simplest and most demanding practices available: leaving people better than you found them. Not dramatically better — not rescuing or fixing. Just slightly more seen, more valued, more capable of being themselves because of their encounter with you. This is the lived expression of everything this year has built.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cDDWvj_q-o8', 'YouTube: Search ''Jane Dutton high quality connections research'' or ''micro-affirmations Mary Rowe MIT workplace'' for the research base. Also: search ''the power of genuine attention relationships research.'' Runtime ~10–15 min.', '', '', '', 'Who left you better than they found you, and how?', 'LEAVING BETTER PRACTICE: Think about the five people you interact with most regularly. For each: Do they regularly leave interactions with you feeling more seen, more valued, and more capable? Or less? What one specific change in how you show up in each relationship would most reliably leave them better? Design a ''leaving better'' practice for your most significant relationships — specific, observable, and genuine. Share: one relationship where you want to commit to leaving people better — and what that will look like.', 'Write a ''leaving better'' intention for your three most important relationships — specific, observable, genuinely yours.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'In every interaction today, ask yourself: ''Will this person be slightly better for having encountered me?'' Even once — notice what happens when you orient toward that.', 'Give one person this week the gift of your full, undivided attention — with no agenda except their experience of being genuinely received.', 'Bring back: what happened when you deliberately oriented toward leaving someone better? What did you notice — in them and in yourself?', '', '', 'Every encounter is an opportunity. I leave people better — seen, valued, more capable of being themselves.', 'The research on high-quality connections (Jane Dutton) is powerful and practical — brief encounters characterised by genuine regard have measurable positive effects. This is one of the most immediately actionable sessions of Phase 4. The ''ten minutes of undivided attention'' practice is a specific and powerful commitment.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Legacy is not what you leave after you die. Legacy is what you are building right now — through how you show up, what you model, what you teach, what you create, and who you help become. At 35, at 50, at 70: legacy is a present practice, not a future inheritance. This week we think about what we are actually building beyond ourselves.', 'If the people closest to you were asked to describe your legacy — not after your death, but right now, based on how you''re currently living — what would they say? Is that the legacy you are choosing to build?', 'Legacy is not what you leave after you die. Legacy is what you are building right now — through how you show up, what you model, what you teach, what you create, and who you help become. At 35, at 50, at 70: legacy is a present practice, not a future inheritance. This week we think about what we are actually building beyond ourselves.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qp0HIF3SfI4', 'YouTube: Search ''generativity psychology Erikson legacy research'' or ''what is your legacy Dan McAdams talk'' for the research base. Also: Stephen Covey ''Begin with the end in mind'' is widely available. Runtime ~15 min.', '', '', '', 'What do you want to be true because you were here?', 'LEGACY DESIGN: In your journal, explore: What do you want to be the ongoing effect of your presence in the lives of your most important relationships? What qualities, values, or capacities do you want to pass on — not as instruction, but as modelling? What are you currently building that will outlast you — in your community, your relationships, your work? And: is how you''re currently living genuinely building toward that legacy — or is there a gap? Share: one legacy you are consciously building right now.', 'Write your current legacy statement — not what you hope to leave eventually, but what you are actively building right now, through how you live daily.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Make one choice today that is explicitly oriented toward the legacy you want to build — a quality of presence, a word honestly said, a model worth following.', 'Share your legacy statement with one person who is part of it. Tell them specifically what you are building — and invite them to hold you to it.', 'Bring back: what happened when you oriented toward legacy in an ordinary daily moment?', '', '', 'I am building something that will outlast me. I build it now — in how I live, how I love, and how I show up.', 'The generativity concept (Erikson) is highly resonant for adults in midlife — name it explicitly. The distinction between legacy as future inheritance vs. legacy as present practice is the central reframe. The question ''what is lasting in them from you right now?'' is the most productive prompt in this session.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Gratitude is not a feeling you have when good things happen. It is a practice you choose regardless of circumstances — the deliberate, specific attention to what is already present and valuable. Research on gratitude is unambiguous: practised consistently, it is one of the most effective interventions available for wellbeing, resilience, and quality of relationship.', 'What is one genuine, specific thing in your life right now that you are genuinely grateful for — not a performance of gratitude, but something real that, when you actually stop and attend to it, produces a felt sense of genuine appreciation? Let yourself feel it for a moment.', 'Gratitude is not a feeling you have when good things happen. It is a practice you choose regardless of circumstances — the deliberate, specific attention to what is already present and valuable. Research on gratitude is unambiguous: practised consistently, it is one of the most effective interventions available for wellbeing, resilience, and quality of relationship.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WPPPFqsECz0', 'YouTube: Robert Emmons on gratitude research — search ''Robert Emmons gratitude research talk YouTube.'' Widely available and directly relevant. Also: search ''gratitude and brain structure neuroscience.'' Runtime ~15 min.', '', '', '', 'What is good right now that you had stopped noticing?', 'GRATITUDE PRACTICE DESIGN: Design a sustainable, specific gratitude practice for the next year. Not ''write three things I''m grateful for'' in a generic sense — but a practice that is specific enough to be genuinely yours: a particular time, a particular format, a particular level of specificity. The practice should name not just WHAT you''re grateful for but WHY it specifically matters to you. This week: practise it every day. Share: your gratitude practice design — the specific format and one example of what specific gratitude looks like for you.', 'Write five specific gratitude statements — each naming exactly what you''re grateful for, exactly why, and the specific felt quality of it.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Practise your designed gratitude practice every day this week without missing a day.', 'Express specific gratitude to one person every day this week — not ''thank you,'' but what specifically you appreciate about them and why.', 'Bring back: what happened when you practised specific gratitude consistently for one week?', '', '', 'Gratitude is my daily practice — specific, felt, genuine. It is how I keep my attention calibrated toward what is real.', 'The specificity point is essential to communicate clearly — generic gratitude produces much weaker effects than specific gratitude. The practice design should be genuinely personalised, not a template. The expressed gratitude practice (telling someone specifically what you appreciate) is the highest-impact exercise of this session.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

There is no arrival. Not in Week 52, not in five years, not ever. The inner work is not a problem to be solved and a destination to be reached. It is a practice — ongoing, deepening, always unfinished, always richer. This week we embrace that truth not as disappointing but as liberating.', 'What has shifted in how you relate to the idea of ''having it together'' or ''being sorted'' over the course of this year? How has your relationship with the ongoing nature of growth changed?', 'There is no arrival. Not in Week 52, not in five years, not ever. The inner work is not a problem to be solved and a destination to be reached. It is a practice — ongoing, deepening, always unfinished, always richer. This week we embrace that truth not as disappointing but as liberating.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sPOuCd6cBao', 'YouTube: ''This Is Water'' by David Foster Wallace — about the ongoing, daily work of conscious living. One of the most important pieces of content of the year. Runtime ~9 min.', '', '', '', 'What will you keep doing when this year ends?', 'PRACTICE SUSTAINABILITY AUDIT: In your journal, for each of the four Phase areas: Which practices from Phase 1 (seeing) do you want to maintain ongoing? Which from Phase 2 (releasing) are still active — what is still unlearning? Which from Phase 3 (rebuilding) needs continued daily attention? Which from Phase 4 (living) are you committed to as permanent orientation? Design your ''ongoing practice'' — not a year-long programme, but a sustainable daily/weekly rhythm you can maintain indefinitely. Share: your ongoing practice design.', 'Write your ongoing practice — the sustainable rhythm of inner work that you will maintain beyond this year.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Choose one practice from this year and commit to it for the next month — no programme, no group, just you and the practice. Notice what it''s like to own it fully.', 'Tell one person that the inner work doesn''t end — and that you''re not trying to finish it. Share what your ongoing practice looks like.', 'Bring back: what does it feel like to embrace the ongoing nature of the practice?', '', '', 'I am not arriving. I am practising. The practice is the destination.', 'The reframe of ''there is no arrival'' can be profoundly liberating — or initially disappointing for people who have been holding Week 52 as a finish line. Name that tension directly and address it honestly. The ongoing practice design is one of the most important practical outcomes of the whole year.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Fifty-two weeks. Four phases. One year of genuine inner work — seeing clearly, unlearning what no longer serves, rebuilding from values, and living it outward into the world. Week 52 is not a graduation. It is a milestone in an ongoing practice. Today we honour the work, acknowledge the transformation, witness each other, and step forward carrying everything this year has made possible.', 'If you had to name the single most significant shift that has occurred in you over the past 52 weeks — not the most visible or the most dramatic, but the most real — what would it be?', 'Fifty-two weeks. Four phases. One year of genuine inner work — seeing clearly, unlearning what no longer serves, rebuilding from values, and living it outward into the world. Week 52 is not a graduation. It is a milestone in an ongoing practice. Today we honour the work, acknowledge the transformation, witness each other, and step forward carrying everything this year has made possible.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sPOuCd6cBao', 'YouTube: ''This Is Water'' by David Foster Wallace — the closing piece of content for the year. Also consider showing a brief meditative ''year in review'' montage if you have created video content across the year. Runtime ~9 min.', '', '', '', 'Who were you a year ago, and what would you tell them?', 'YEAR IN REVIEW — THE CEREMONY: In your journal, write the full answer to these four questions. Take as long as you need. 1. Who was I when I walked into Week 1? (Be honest — not harsh, but genuine.) 2. What has genuinely shifted — in how I see, what I''ve released, what I''ve built, how I now live? 3. What do I carry forward from this year that I didn''t have before? 4. What is my commitment for the next year — the ongoing practice I am choosing? Then, in the group: each person shares one answer from any question — witnessed in silence by the whole community. No advice. No commentary. Just witnessing. The witnessing is the ceremony.', 'Write a letter to someone who might begin this journey next year. What do you want them to know?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Live one day this week with total intentionality — from every practice this year, in full expression. Notice what a life built from this year''s work actually feels and looks like.', 'Tell someone outside this group: ''I''ve done a year of serious inner work. One thing that genuinely changed is...'' Own it. Fully. Without qualification.', 'Come to the final session ready to share your four-question year review — or one line from it.', '', '', 'I have done this work. I carry it forward. The practice continues — deeper, richer, more genuinely mine.', 'MAKE THIS SESSION EXTRAORDINARY. This is the ceremony. The year''s arc completing. People have done real, durable, genuine inner work. Honour it fully: candles, music, physical space transformed, letters read aloud, witnessed silence. The community that has formed over 52 weeks deserves to be explicitly celebrated. The commitment to ongoing practice is the closing act — not ''goodbye'' but ''continuing.''', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

You''re surrounded by other people''s opinions, social media, and expectations — so much that most of us don''t know what we actually think or feel anymore. This session is about starting to notice the difference between what''s genuinely yours and what you''ve absorbed.', 'Quick show of hands — no judgment: Who''s ever said something or made a choice, then later thought — ''wait, that wasn''t actually what I wanted''? That''s the gap we''re exploring today.', 'You''re surrounded by other people''s opinions, social media, and expectations — so much that most of us don''t know what we actually think or feel anymore. This session is about starting to notice the difference between what''s genuinely yours and what you''ve absorbed.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Thlbqg2sKEM', '7 Hard Truths for Teens — a no-sugarcoating talk on ownership, time, habits, friendship, and the regret of wasted time. Runtime ~10 min.', '', '', '', 'What are you carrying that nobody around you knows about?', 'SEVEN TRUTHS, ONE SIGNAL: The video names seven hard truths. Write down as many as you remember. Next to each, mark SIGNAL (something calling you to see clearly and act) or NOISE (something you''ve been tuning out, dodging, or hoping isn''t real). Now circle the one that stung the most. Underneath it write: ''What is this truth trying to get me to see — and what one small choice would I make today if I took it seriously?'' Share the number you circled — not the full answer, unless you want to.', 'Which of the seven truths hit you hardest — and what is it asking you to see about your life that you''ve been avoiding?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Catch a waiting moment. One time today you catch yourself waiting for something to happen TO you instead of making it happen. Name it out loud.', 'Run a phone audit. Check your screen time, multiply it by 365, and look at the number. Then set one boundary for today — one app deleted, or notifications off except for real people.', 'Take one small risk this week — something you''d regret NOT doing. Try it, fail, look silly. Then write down the story. That''s the signal you lived.', '', '', 'I stop waiting for rescue. I am the main character, and today counts.', 'Teens need psychological safety first. Don''t push sharing. Make it clear that honesty with yourself is the point — not performance. Keep it real and slightly light in tone, but let the content be genuine.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

A lot of the beliefs we have about ourselves — about our abilities, our worth, what''s possible for us — weren''t decided by us. They were handed to us. Today we figure out which stories are actually true versus which ones we''ve just been repeating.', 'Finish this sentence silently, no sharing yet: ''I''m just not the kind of person who...'' Notice how quickly that answer came. That speed? That''s a story on autopilot.', 'A lot of the beliefs we have about ourselves — about our abilities, our worth, what''s possible for us — weren''t decided by us. They were handed to us. Today we figure out which stories are actually true versus which ones we''ve just been repeating.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pN34FNbOKXc', 'YouTube: ''Growth Mindset vs Fixed Mindset'' — animated RSA-style explanation of Carol Dweck''s research on how beliefs about ability shape outcomes. Runtime ~10 min.', '', '', '', 'What''s something you''ve always been told you are — and is it actually true?', 'TRACK LISTING: Write down 3 beliefs you seem to carry about yourself — about your ability, your worth, what you''re allowed to want. For each one: How old do you think you were when you started believing this? Was there a moment that ''installed'' it? Circle the one that feels most like it''s been running your life without your permission. Share: was it easy or hard to find them?', 'If your best friend had the same belief about themselves that you have about yourself, what would you tell them?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Notice once today when a story seems to be making a choice for you before you even think about it.', 'Tell one person one story you''re examining — not to explain or justify it, just to name it out loud.', 'Bring back one moment where you caught a story running. What happened when you noticed it?', '', '', 'I can see where my stories came from. That means I''m bigger than them.', 'Some teens may become emotional accessing early memories. Normalise it: ''noticing is brave.'' Never ask anyone to share traumatic content publicly. Written exercise keeps it private and safe.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

You know those moments where you react to something and immediately think ''why did I do that''? That''s the pattern. Today we figure out what''s actually triggering your automatic reactions — and whether you can find the gap.', 'Raise your hand if you''ve ever sent a text, said something, or walked away from a situation and immediately thought ''I shouldn''t have done that.'' What does that feel like?', 'You know those moments where you react to something and immediately think ''why did I do that''? That''s the pattern. Today we figure out what''s actually triggering your automatic reactions — and whether you can find the gap.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RcGyVTAoXEU', 'YouTube: Search ''Simon Sinek How to Control Your Emotions'' for a practical, accessible take on the pause between stimulus and response. Runtime ~8–12 min.', '', '', '', 'When did you last snap at someone and wish you hadn''t?', 'MY TRIGGER INVENTORY: Think of a pattern you want to interrupt. Trace it back: what usually sets it off (person, feeling, situation, time of day)? What does the reaction give you right now in the moment? What does it cost you later? Smallest possible interrupt: when you notice the trigger, what''s one word you could say to yourself before the reaction runs? Share your trigger word (not the pattern) with one other person.', 'What''s one automatic reaction you have that you''d like to pause before it runs? What do you think it''s actually protecting?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Use your trigger word once today — even if the pattern still runs. The noticing is enough for now.', 'Tell one person about the pattern you''re working with. Not the details — just that you''re working on something.', 'Bring one moment from the week where you tried to interrupt a pattern — what happened, even if it didn''t go perfectly?', '', '', 'I''m not my reactions. I''m the one who notices them — and that means I have a choice.', 'Naming amygdala hijack de-shames the reaction. Keep the trigger inventory light — don''t push into trauma territory. The trigger word should be chosen privately by each teen.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Your body is constantly sending you signals — about safety, stress, excitement, dread. Most of us learned to ignore them or push through. This week we learn to actually read what the body is saying.', 'Without thinking about it: where in your body do you feel nervous? Point to it. Where do you feel excitement? How do you know when you''re actually hungry vs. just bored? Most people have never been asked these questions.', 'Your body is constantly sending you signals — about safety, stress, excitement, dread. Most of us learned to ignore them or push through. This week we learn to actually read what the body is saying.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ks-_Mh1QhMc', 'TED Talk: ''Your Body Language May Shape Who You Are'' by Amy Cuddy — evidence-based exploration of how physical state influences mental and emotional state. Runtime ~21 min.', '', '', '', 'Where do you feel it in your body when you''re nervous?', 'SENSATION MAPPING: Facilitator names a scenario and teens put their hand on where they feel it in their body: ''The moment before you walk into a room full of people you don''t know.'' / ''Getting a really good text from someone you like.'' / ''Sunday night before a hard week starts.'' / ''That moment when everything just clicks.'' Discuss: are these signals or just nerves? What might each one be telling you?', 'Think of a time your body gave you a strong signal that you ignored. What happened? What do you wish you''d listened to?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Do a 1-minute body scan at three different times today. Write one word for what you notice each time.', 'Tell someone one thing your body has been trying to tell you that you''ve been ignoring.', 'Bring back one observation from your body scan practice this week.', '', '', 'My body and my mind are the same team. I''m learning to let them work together.', 'Keep this entirely positive and non-aesthetic — this is about intelligence and signals, NOT appearance or fitness standards. Watch for any content that might touch on body image issues.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

How we see ourselves shapes literally everything — the choices we make, the risks we take, the people we let in. Most teens have a self-image built from comparison, other people''s opinions, and their worst moments. This week we build a more honest one.', 'Quick question — no right answer: When you scroll through social media, do you feel better or worse about yourself afterwards? And does the image you project online match who you actually are?', 'How we see ourselves shapes literally everything — the choices we make, the risks we take, the people we let in. Most teens have a self-image built from comparison, other people''s opinions, and their worst moments. This week we build a more honest one.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Lp7E973zozc', 'YouTube: Jonathan Haidt on social media and teen mental health — widely available, evidence-based, highly relevant. Runtime ~15–20 min depending on version.', '', '', '', 'If you had to describe yourself with no filter and no put-downs, what would you say?', 'REAL MIRROR vs. COMPARE MIRROR: Two columns. Column A: ''What I actually see when I look honestly at myself'' — strengths, limitations, things I''m still figuring out. Column B: ''What I think I look like compared to others'' — who do you compare yourself to, in what areas, and is that comparison fair? Key question: Which mirror are you living by? And which do you actually want to use? Share: ''One thing I''m ready to stop comparing'' — anonymously if preferred.', 'If your social media profile showed who you actually are — not who you want to be seen as — what would it include that you currently leave out?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Do a social media audit: after 20 minutes of scrolling, check in with your body. How do you feel? Make a note.', 'Ask someone who knows you well: ''What do you see in me that I don''t seem to see in myself?''', 'Bring back your social media audit observation and the answer from Wednesday''s question.', '', '', 'I am building my self-image on honest ground — not comparison, not performance, not other people''s opinions.', 'Highly relevant session for teens. Avoid moralising about social media — stay evidence-based and curious. The social media audit is practical and powerful. Goal is self-awareness, not guilt.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Comparison is the background noise of teen life — and social media has turned the volume up to maximum. But here''s what most people don''t know: the comparison loop literally never pays off. Not once. This week we find the exit.', 'Be honest: in the last week, how many times did you feel worse about yourself after looking at someone else''s social media? How many times better? What''s the ratio?', 'Comparison is the background noise of teen life — and social media has turned the volume up to maximum. But here''s what most people don''t know: the comparison loop literally never pays off. Not once. This week we find the exit.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P6FORpg0KVo', 'TED Talk: ''Quit Social Media'' by Cal Newport — practical, evidence-based case for intentionality over comparison culture. Runtime ~13 min. Note: not anti-technology, pro-intentionality.', '', '', '', 'Who do you compare yourself to, and what do you think they''ve got?', 'THE EXIT INTERVIEW: Imagine you are interviewing the Comparison Loop for a job. Write its job description: What does it promise to deliver? What does it actually deliver? What are its side effects? Would you rehire it? Now write the job description for what you WANT instead — what would a healthy inner metric look like? What would it measure? How would you know it was working? Share: what would you measure yourself by if social media didn''t exist?', 'Write three things you''ve done or overcome in the past year that nobody necessarily saw. Things that were for you. Are they in your self-story?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'For one day, do a conscious comparison fast — notice every comparison thought and redirect to: ''How am I measuring up to my own values today?''', 'Tell one person about something you''re proud of that you rarely talk about. Watch what happens when you claim it.', 'Bring back what happened on your comparison fast day — what did you notice?', '', '', 'My story is mine. I measure it by my values, my growth, and my own honest effort.', 'The comparison fast is highly practical and can be genuinely transformative. Avoid shaming social media use — frame as intentionality. The ''things nobody saw'' exercise is powerful for teens who feel unseen.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

That voice in your head that says ''you''re not good enough,'' ''everyone can see how awkward you are,'' ''you''ll fail'' — we all have one. Today we find out where it came from, why it does what it does, and why listening to it is optional.', 'Honest question: would you talk to your best friend the way you talk to yourself? If someone said to your best friend what your inner voice says to you on a bad day — would you call that friendship?', 'That voice in your head that says ''you''re not good enough,'' ''everyone can see how awkward you are,'' ''you''ll fail'' — we all have one. Today we find out where it came from, why it does what it does, and why listening to it is optional.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IvtZBUSplr4', 'YouTube: Kristin Neff TED Talk on self-compassion — same resource as adults, completely accessible for teens. Alternatively search ''how to silence your inner critic animated'' for shorter versions. Runtime ~10–20 min.', '', '', '', 'If that voice was a person in your group chat, would you keep them in it?', 'THE HECKLER vs. THE COACH: Write your inner critic''s three favourite lines about you. For each one write: ''A good coach who wanted me to actually improve would say...'' Notice the difference — the critic shuts down, the coach opens up. Now: what would you need to believe about yourself to replace the critic with the coach? Write that as a statement. Share: the most common thing the heckler says.', 'Write a text message from your inner critic. Then write the reply you''d send it as your wiser, more honest self.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Notice today how often the critic fires. Don''t fight it. Just count. Awareness without judgment — for now.', 'Tell one person something you''ve been hard on yourself about. Notice what it feels like to say it out loud to someone who''s on your side.', 'Bring back: how many times did the critic fire this week? And did noticing change anything?', '', '', 'I hear the critic. It''s not me. I choose the voice of someone who''s actually on my side.', 'Teen inner critics are often ferocious and normalised — many don''t realise how harsh their self-talk is until they compare it to what they''d say to a friend. The ''text message from the critic'' exercise is effective and often funny enough to defuse shame.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Feelings aren''t weakness. They''re not drama. They''re data. Every emotion is trying to tell you something — about what you value, what you need, what your limits are. This week we learn to actually read them instead of either ignoring them or getting wrecked by them.', 'Raise your hand if you''ve ever reacted to something emotionally and genuinely had no idea WHY you reacted that way. That gap — between the emotion and the meaning — is what we''re working on today.', 'Feelings aren''t weakness. They''re not drama. They''re data. Every emotion is trying to tell you something — about what you value, what you need, what your limits are. This week we learn to actually read them instead of either ignoring them or getting wrecked by them.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tGdsOXZpyWE', 'YouTube: Marc Brackett on emotional intelligence — search ''Marc Brackett emotion scientist'' or his talk on the RULER framework. Alternatively: search ''permission to feel Marc Brackett'' for interviews. Runtime ~15–20 min.', '', '', '', 'What were you actually feeling right before you got angry?', 'EMOTION ARCHAEOLOGY: Think of a recent strong emotional reaction — particularly one that felt disproportionate or confusing. Dig down: What emotion did I express or act from? (Level 1). What emotion was I actually feeling underneath that? (Level 2). And underneath that? (Level 3 — often the most true). Example: Snapped at a friend → anger (L1) → felt ignored (L2) → fear that I don''t matter (L3). Share your Level 1 emotion. You don''t have to share Levels 2 or 3 if you don''t want to.', 'Write about an emotion you don''t let yourself feel very often. What do you think you''re protecting yourself from by keeping it away?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'When you notice a strong feeling today, try to name it with more precision than ''good'' or ''bad.'' What is it actually?', 'Tell one person about a feeling you usually hide or dismiss. Not the story — just the feeling and what you think it''s actually pointing at.', 'Bring back one time you practised emotion archaeology this week. What did you find underneath?', '', '', 'My emotions are information. They point at what matters. I''m learning to read them.', 'The emotion archaeology exercise is powerful but can surface unexpected material. Have a ''parking lot'' option — teens can write things down to process later rather than in the group. The concept of emotional layers is a foundational tool they will use throughout the year.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

All of us have been hurt — by experiences, relationships, or things that happened that we didn''t fully understand. And some of those hurts are still shaping how we act today, even if we''ve never talked about them. This week we acknowledge what we carry — not to relive it, but to start understanding it.', 'Honest question — you don''t have to answer out loud: is there something that happened in your past — something that hurt — that you think is still affecting how you act today? How you treat people, or how you let people treat you?', 'All of us have been hurt — by experiences, relationships, or things that happened that we didn''t fully understand. And some of those hurts are still shaping how we act today, even if we''ve never talked about them. This week we acknowledge what we carry — not to relive it, but to start understanding it.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=95ovIJ3dsNk', 'TED Talk: ''How Childhood Trauma Affects Health Across a Lifetime'' by Nadine Burke Harris — fully accessible for teens and deeply relevant. Runtime ~16 min.', '', '', '', 'What happened to you that you''ve never really talked about?', 'PRIVATE REFLECTION — NOT FOR SHARING: In your journal (private — nobody reads this): write about one thing that hurt you — past or recently — that you think is still with you. How does it show up today? What does it make you do or avoid? If someone who really cared about you knew about this wound, what would they want you to know? Fold your journal closed when done. After writing: take a slow breath. Look around the room. You''re here. You''re okay.', 'Write privately: what is one coping strategy I use that I think came from being hurt? Is it still helping me — or costing me more than it gives?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Notice once today when something small triggers a big feeling — and ask yourself: ''Does this feel older than now?''', 'If there''s one person in your life you trust — just one — consider telling them one small true thing about what you carry. Notice what happens.', 'Bring back: did anything shift this week after the journalling exercise? You don''t have to share what — just whether the awareness felt different.', '', '', 'What happened to me does not define me. I see it. I carry it honestly. And I decide what happens next.', 'CRITICAL: Ensure journalling is explicitly PRIVATE and cannot be read by facilitators or peers without consent. Have a wellbeing resource card available (counsellor contacts, helpline numbers) for anyone who needs support. Follow mandatory reporting requirements if any disclosures indicate current safety risks.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Pretty much everyone your age is performing — performing toughness, coolness, confidence, happiness, not-caring. Some of it is genuinely useful social navigation. But when you can''t remember who you are underneath the performance, that''s when it starts costing you. Today we look at the masks.', 'Quick and honest: rate yourself 1–10 on how authentic you are in these contexts — with parents, with close friends, at school, on social media, when alone. What does the range tell you?', 'Pretty much everyone your age is performing — performing toughness, coolness, confidence, happiness, not-caring. Some of it is genuinely useful social navigation. But when you can''t remember who you are underneath the performance, that''s when it starts costing you. Today we look at the masks.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IVlU-2OBdts', 'YouTube: ''To This Day'' — Shane Koyczan spoken word animation about identity, performance, and the cost of hiding. Intensely moving, highly relevant to teens. Runtime ~8 min.', '', '', '', 'Is there something about you that you''ve never let anyone see?', 'AUTHENTICITY MAP: Draw yourself in the middle of a page. Around you draw the different contexts of your life (friend groups, home, school, online). For each context: draw how much of ''you'' actually shows up there — you could use percentages. Now: where do you feel most like yourself? Why? Where do you feel most masked? What are you protecting there — and from what? Share: one context where you feel most real, and one where you feel most masked.', 'Write a letter from your authentic self to your most performative self. What does the real you want the performed version to know?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Notice once today when you shift into performance mode. Ask yourself: is this genuinely necessary — or just habit?', 'Show one person — even a little — something real about you that you usually manage or hide. Watch what happens.', 'Bring back: what happened when you tried showing something real? What did it feel like?', '', '', 'I know who I am underneath the performance. And that person is worth knowing.', 'Let teens make the authenticity map as creative as they want. Honour the developmental complexity — trying on identities is appropriate at this stage. Avoid implying that being ''themselves'' is simple or that they should know exactly who that is yet.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Most of the drama in relationships — with friends, family, partners — isn''t really about the other person. It''s about what we''re bringing to them from our own history. Today we develop the skill of actually seeing people — instead of just seeing our story about them.', 'Think of someone who really irritates you. What specifically do they do? Now, honestly: does any version of that quality exist in you? Even a little?', 'Most of the drama in relationships — with friends, family, partners — isn''t really about the other person. It''s about what we''re bringing to them from our own history. Today we develop the skill of actually seeing people — instead of just seeing our story about them.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cDDWvj_q-o8', 'YouTube: ''Empathy: The Human Connection to Patient Care'' — Cleveland Clinic short film. While medical in context, it''s a universally moving illustration of the invisible experiences everyone is carrying. Runtime ~4 min.', '', '', '', 'Think of someone who annoys you. What might be going on for them?', 'THEIR SIDE: Think of a current or recent conflict with someone. Write a 2-paragraph ''defence brief'' FOR THEM — arguing their side as generously and specifically as possible. What might they be experiencing? What might they be afraid of? What might your behaviour look like from their perspective? This is not about deciding they were right. It''s about seeing them clearly. Share: one thing you discovered when you tried to argue their side.', 'Write about the last significant conflict you were part of: what was your role? What did you bring to it from your own history that might have made it more charged?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Once today in a conversation, try to listen with 100% focus — no preparing what you''ll say, no half-attention. Just listen. Notice what that''s like.', 'Tell someone about a relationship where you''ve realised you might have been seeing your story more than the person.', 'Bring back: what happened when you tried the deep listening practice this week?', '', '', 'I see the people in my life as clearly as I can — knowing my own lens is always in the way a little.', 'The ''defence brief'' exercise can be revelatory — some teens will discover they''ve been part of a dynamic they weren''t fully owning. Keep it non-shaming: ''This isn''t about who was right. It''s about developing the capacity to see.''', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

About half of what you do every day isn''t a decision — it''s a habit running on autopilot. That''s not bad. But it means if you want your life to look different, you need to understand how habits actually work — because ''trying harder'' is the least effective strategy that exists.', 'Quick: name one thing you do every day without really thinking about it. Now — when did that start? Did you decide to do it, or did it just develop?', 'About half of what you do every day isn''t a decision — it''s a habit running on autopilot. That''s not bad. But it means if you want your life to look different, you need to understand how habits actually work — because ''trying harder'' is the least effective strategy that exists.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W1eYrhGeffc', 'YouTube: ''The Power of Habit'' animated book summary of Charles Duhigg''s work. Clear, engaging, and directly relevant. Runtime ~10 min.', '', '', '', 'What do you always do when you''re stressed, without even deciding to?', 'MY HABIT LOOP: Pick one habit — a behaviour pattern you repeat regularly. Map it: What triggers it? (Time, place, feeling, person, situation?) What do you do? (The habit.) What do you get from it in the moment? (Be honest.) What does the reward actually represent? (Stress relief? Escape? Connection?) Is there something else that could meet the same underlying need more helpfully? Share: your trigger and your reward — not necessarily the habit itself.', 'Write about a habit and trace it back: when did it start? What was happening? What was it originally solving?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Today, catch one habit in the act of running. Note the cue. You don''t have to change anything — just see it.', 'Tell someone about the underlying need a habit is meeting — not the habit itself, just the need. See if they recognise something similar in themselves.', 'Bring back your complete habit map — cue, routine, reward, underlying need, and one alternative idea.', '', '', 'I understand my patterns. Understanding them is power — not judgment.', 'The brain science explanation de-shames the pattern and gives teens agency. The identity reframe (''I am someone who...'') is worth spending extra time on — it''s one of the most practically powerful concepts of the year.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

You''ve done 13 weeks of genuinely hard looking. Not perfectly — nobody does it perfectly. But you''ve looked. Today we take stock of what''s actually shifted, what you now see, and what you''re taking into the next chapter. This is a threshold, not a finish line.', 'What is one thing — about yourself, your patterns, or how you see — that you now know that you genuinely didn''t know (or wouldn''t look at) 13 weeks ago?', 'You''ve done 13 weeks of genuinely hard looking. Not perfectly — nobody does it perfectly. But you''ve looked. Today we take stock of what''s actually shifted, what you now see, and what you''re taking into the next chapter. This is a threshold, not a finish line.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jqONINYF17M', 'YouTube: ''The Power of Believing That You Can Improve'' by Carol Dweck — affirms the transformation that comes from genuine self-examination and the growth mindset that makes Phase 2 possible. Runtime ~10 min.', '', '', '', 'What have you worked out about yourself this term?', 'PHASE 1 LETTER: Write a letter to yourself at the start of this journey. What do you want them to know? What would you tell them about what''s coming? What do you know now that would have helped them then? You are not the same person who walked in to Week 1. Even if you can''t exactly articulate how — something has opened. Share, if you choose: one line from your letter.', 'Write three things you now see that you couldn''t (or wouldn''t) see at Week 1 — one about yourself, one about your patterns, one about how you relate to others.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Revisit Week 1 journal entries if you kept them. What do you notice about the gap between then and now?', 'Tell one person who isn''t in this group something genuinely honest about what you''ve learned about yourself in the past 13 weeks.', 'Come back to the final session ready to share one line from your letter — if you want to.', '', '', 'I see more clearly than I did. That clarity is mine, and it''s the foundation of what comes next.', 'Create ritual and ceremony — teenagers respond powerfully to being genuinely seen and acknowledged. If letters are shared, do it with real reverence. Ensure the transition to Phase 2 is framed with excitement: ''what you''ve seen is the gift. What you do with it is the adventure.''', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

A lot of the things you actually want to do — the things that feel most like you — you''ve been putting off because you''re waiting for someone to say it''s okay. A parent. A friend. The right feeling. Enough confidence. This week: that permission was always yours.', 'What''s one thing you''ve wanted to do — creatively, personally, socially — that you haven''t started because you were waiting to feel ready, or waiting for someone to say it was okay?', 'A lot of the things you actually want to do — the things that feel most like you — you''ve been putting off because you''re waiting for someone to say it''s okay. A parent. A friend. The right feeling. Enough confidence. This week: that permission was always yours.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8CrOL-ydFMI', 'YouTube: ''Do Schools Kill Creativity?'' by Ken Robinson — explores how external approval systems suppress authentic expression and self-directed action. Highly engaging and directly relevant. Runtime ~19 min.', '', '', '', 'What are you waiting for permission to do?', 'DRAFT VS. SEND: Think of something you''ve been keeping in ''draft'' — a project, a conversation, a direction, a version of yourself. Write: What specifically are you waiting for before you ''send'' it? What''s the worst realistic outcome if you do? What''s the cost of keeping it in draft indefinitely? What''s the smallest possible version of ''sending'' it this week? Share: what''s in your draft folder — without necessarily sharing what it is, just how long it''s been there.', 'Who are you waiting to impress before you let yourself begin? What would it mean if that person never gave you the green light?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Today, do one tiny thing you''ve been waiting to feel ready for. Not the whole thing. Just one tiny move.', 'Tell one person about something you''ve been keeping in draft. Say it out loud. Notice what happens.', 'Come back with what happened when you made the tiny move. How did it feel?', '', '', 'I don''t need permission to become who I actually am.', 'Some teens are waiting for parental permission in a very literal sense — be sensitive to family dynamics. The framing is about inner authority, not rebellion. Distinguish between appropriate consultation and chronic approval-seeking.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

There''s probably a version of you that other people have planned out — a career path, a type of success, a kind of life. And there''s the version of you that actually exists. This week we figure out which parts of your future belong to you — and which parts were handed to you without asking.', 'Be honest: what do you think the people closest to you expect your life to look like in 10 years? Now: is that actually what you want? How much overlap is there?', 'There''s probably a version of you that other people have planned out — a career path, a type of success, a kind of life. And there''s the version of you that actually exists. This week we figure out which parts of your future belong to you — and which parts were handed to you without asking.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NiuDFBNDoSk', 'YouTube: ''There''s More to Life Than Being Happy'' by Emily Esfahani Smith — explores authentic meaning vs. inherited happiness scripts. Highly relevant for teens navigating expectation. Runtime ~12 min.', '', '', '', 'Whose expectations are you living inside?', 'THE EXPECTATION MAP: Draw a page with two sections. Section 1: ''The life people around me seem to expect for me'' — be specific about career, values, relationships, lifestyle markers. Who specifically expects this? Section 2: ''The life I actually find myself drawn to'' — even if it''s unclear, even if it seems unrealistic, even if you''ve never said it out loud. Now: where do these maps overlap? Where do they diverge most significantly? Share: one divergence point — without necessarily resolving it.', 'Write about one expectation someone has of your future that you''ve never questioned out loud. What happens when you question it now?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Notice one moment today where a choice you''re making is genuinely yours — not inherited, not performed. What does that feel like?', 'Tell one trusted person about one way your actual direction diverges from the expected path. Notice their response — and notice what you feel after saying it.', 'Bring back: what was it like to draw the expectation map? What surprised you?', '', '', 'I am not obligated to become the person someone else planned. My life is mine to define.', 'This is potentially a session where teens may disclose family conflict around expectations — particularly around academic or career pressure. Keep the framing on self-discovery rather than family critique. The goal is inner clarity, not rebellion.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Holding onto anger or resentment toward someone feels powerful — like you''re making them pay. But research shows the only person actually paying is you. This week we look at what forgiveness actually means — and why it''s one of the most self-interested things you can do.', 'Think of someone you''re angry at or haven''t forgiven. You don''t have to name them. Just notice — how much mental space does this take up? When does it show up? How often does it replay?', 'Holding onto anger or resentment toward someone feels powerful — like you''re making them pay. But research shows the only person actually paying is you. This week we look at what forgiveness actually means — and why it''s one of the most self-interested things you can do.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ik_V3UIqoQ0', 'YouTube: Search ''science of forgiveness teen'' or ''Fred Luskin forgiveness research'' for accessible content on the physiological benefits of forgiveness. Runtime ~10–15 min.', '', '', '', 'Who are you still angry at, and what does staying angry give you?', 'THE BACKGROUND APP AUDIT: Think of one person or situation you''re carrying resentment toward. Write: What exactly happened? What did it cost you? How often do you replay it? What has holding this cost you in energy, relationships, or peace? Now write: What would ''closing this app'' actually look like? Not forgetting — just stopping the replay. Share: how much mental RAM is this taking up — without naming the specific app.', 'Write honestly: what are you getting from holding onto this resentment? (There''s usually something — a sense of justice, a protection, a way of staying connected to what happened.) Is it worth the cost?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'When the resentment replays today, try saying internally: ''I know this hurt. I''m choosing to stop paying for it.'' Notice what happens.', 'Tell one person you''re working on releasing something you''ve been carrying. Notice how it feels to say that.', 'Bring back: what shifted — even a little — when you tried the internal reframe this week?', '', '', 'I release what I''ve been carrying — not for them, but for myself. That energy is mine now.', 'For teens, forgiveness of peers — social exclusion, betrayal, online harm — can be extremely raw. Never minimise the hurt. The session is entirely about their own wellbeing, not about the other person. Make that distinction very clearly and repeatedly.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

You know all those mistakes, embarrassments, and bad calls you keep replaying — especially at 2am? This week we talk about why being permanently hard on yourself isn''t the same as accountability. And why the most powerful thing you can do is actually learn from something and then let it go.', 'What''s one thing from the past — a mistake, an embarrassment, something you said or did — that you still replay? Be honest about how often it comes up.', 'You know all those mistakes, embarrassments, and bad calls you keep replaying — especially at 2am? This week we talk about why being permanently hard on yourself isn''t the same as accountability. And why the most powerful thing you can do is actually learn from something and then let it go.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IvtZBUSplr4', 'YouTube: Kristin Neff self-compassion talk — accessible for teens and directly addresses the difference between self-compassion and making excuses. Also search ''self-forgiveness teen psychology'' for shorter accessible clips. Runtime ~15–20 min.', '', '', '', 'What have you done that you still haven''t forgiven yourself for?', 'THE 2AM AUDIT: Think of one thing you replay — a mistake, a failure, a moment you''re not proud of. Work through: What actually happened? What would genuine accountability look like (acknowledging, understanding, repairing if possible)? Have you actually done those things — or are you still just punishing yourself? If a friend told you the same story, what would you actually say to them? Write them that message — then read it back to yourself. Share: one insight from this process.', 'Write the honest version of the story — what happened, what you learned, what you''d do differently. Then write: ''That is enough. I release the rest.''', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'When the replay starts today, try interrupting it with: ''I''ve heard this. I''ve learned from it. I''m closing this tab.''', 'Tell one person something you''ve been replaying — and let them respond. Notice what it feels like when someone who cares about you hears the whole thing.', 'Bring back: what happened when you tried closing the tab this week?', '', '', 'I am accountable and I am compassionate with myself. I learn and I move forward.', 'The 2am framing resonates deeply with teens — it normalises a universal experience without glamorising it. The key distinction between shame and guilt is worth spending extra time on. Be alert for anyone who seems to be carrying significant self-blame — offer professional referral resources gently.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Last time we met the inner critic. Now we do something with it. Not silence it forever — but replace it with something way more useful: a voice that''s actually honest AND on your side. Think of the best coach, mentor, or teacher you''ve ever had. That''s the voice we''re building.', 'Think of the best teacher, coach, or mentor you''ve ever had — real or from a film or book. What made their voice different from the critic''s? What did they say that the critic never says?', 'Last time we met the inner critic. Now we do something with it. Not silence it forever — but replace it with something way more useful: a voice that''s actually honest AND on your side. Think of the best coach, mentor, or teacher you''ve ever had. That''s the voice we''re building.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pN34FNbOKXc', 'YouTube: ''Growth Mindset vs. Fixed Mindset'' animated explainer — Carol Dweck''s research on the language of growth vs. the language of judgment. Runtime ~10 min.', '', '', '', 'What would a good coach have said to you instead?', 'CRITIC vs. COACH REWRITE: Take 3 things your inner critic commonly says to you. For each, write the coach version using this structure: Acknowledge (''That was hard / didn''t go as planned''). Observe specifically (''The specific thing that happened was...''). Question forward (''What could I try differently / what did I learn?''). Affirm capacity (''You''ve handled hard things before / you can figure this out''). Read the coach versions aloud — even quietly to yourself. Notice what it feels like in your body. Share: one coach line that you actually believe.', 'Write a pre-game coach briefing for yourself before something challenging this week — the kind of thing the best coach would say.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Today when the critic fires, try running just the first line of the coach script: ''That was hard. And I can work with this.'' Notice the difference.', 'Tell one person your coach voice — what it says, how it''s different. Ask them to remind you of it when you slip back into critic mode.', 'Bring back: when did you use the coach voice this week? What happened?', '', '', 'My inner coach is honest and on my side. I''m building that voice, one rep at a time.', 'Have teens write their coach scripts on actual cards they keep — a physical reminder is more effective than a mental one. The rep-by-rep framing resonates with teens who understand athletic or skill development. Reinforce: this is brain training, not positive thinking.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Do you ever agree to things you don''t want to do just to avoid the awkwardness of saying no? Say things you don''t mean to keep the peace? Pretend to be fine when you''re not? That''s people-pleasing — and it feels kind but it''s actually one of the most exhausting and self-erasing things you can do. This week we look at where it comes from and how to start changing it.', 'Honest check-in: In the past week, how many times did you say yes when you meant no? Agree with something you didn''t agree with? Pretend to be okay when you weren''t? How much energy did that take?', 'Do you ever agree to things you don''t want to do just to avoid the awkwardness of saying no? Say things you don''t mean to keep the peace? Pretend to be fine when you''re not? That''s people-pleasing — and it feels kind but it''s actually one of the most exhausting and self-erasing things you can do. This week we look at where it comes from and how to start changing it.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MIte_1vcOqs', 'YouTube: Search ''people pleasing psychology teens'' or ''how to say no without guilt'' for accessible, practical content. Alternatively: Patrick Teahan or Dr Ramani on people-pleasing roots. Runtime ~10–15 min.', '', '', '', 'When did you last say yes when you really meant no?', 'THE YES/FEAR AUDIT: Think of your last 10 significant ''yeses.'' For each one, honestly ask: Did I say yes because I genuinely wanted to — or because I was afraid of what would happen if I didn''t? Sort them into two columns: ''Genuine yes'' and ''Fear yes.'' What''s the ratio? Now: pick one ''fear yes'' pattern. What specifically am I afraid will happen if I say no? How realistic is that fear? Share: the ratio — without naming specific situations.', 'Write about the person whose approval you most shape yourself around. What would happen to your relationship if you started being more honest? What''s the best realistic outcome if you did?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Try one small no today — something low-stakes. Notice what you feel before, during, and after. Record it.', 'Tell one person about a ''fear yes'' pattern you''re working on. Ask them to notice when you''re doing it.', 'Bring back: what happened with your small no this week? Fear vs. reality?', '', '', 'I say yes when I mean yes. I say no when I need to. Both are acts of respect.', 'People-pleasing is deeply tied to social belonging needs in teens — acknowledge that the fear of rejection is real and the brain genuinely experiences it as dangerous. The goal is not fearlessness but gradually expanding the window of tolerance for discomfort when acting from values.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

There''s a thought that runs constantly in the background for most people: not enough time, not enough success, not good enough. It drives comparison, competition, and the feeling that you''re always slightly behind. This week we look at where that thought actually comes from — and whether it''s actually true.', 'What do you feel like you never have enough of? Time? Friends? Success? Recognition? Attention? Pick the one that hits hardest. Where did you first learn to feel scarce about that thing?', 'There''s a thought that runs constantly in the background for most people: not enough time, not enough success, not good enough. It drives comparison, competition, and the feeling that you''re always slightly behind. This week we look at where that thought actually comes from — and whether it''s actually true.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RZWf2_2L2v8', 'YouTube: Search ''scarcity mindset vs abundance mindset explained'' for clear animated or talk-format explainers. Also: Brené Brown on ''never enough'' culture is widely available. Runtime ~10–15 min.', '', '', '', 'What do you hold back on, just in case?', 'ENOUGH AUDIT: What are the three main areas where you feel ''not enough''? For each one: When did this start? What specific evidence are you using to decide you''re not enough in this area? If your best friend had exactly your situation, would you tell them they weren''t enough? What would ''genuinely enough'' actually look like — not perfect, just enough? Share: one ''not enough'' story you''re questioning.', 'Write about what your life would look like if you genuinely believed you were enough — not perfect, not finished, but fundamentally, currently enough. What would you do differently?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Notice one ''not enough'' thought today. Ask: is this actually true? Or is it a programme running on old data?', 'Tell one person about an area where you''re practising ''enough'' thinking. Ask them to reinforce it when you slide back.', 'Bring back: what happened when you questioned the ''not enough'' thought this week?', '', '', 'I am enough, right now, for today. And from that place, I keep growing.', '''Not enough'' is the background hum of most teens'' inner worlds — naming it directly often produces strong recognition. The shift is not to false positivity but to questioning whether the measure is real and whether it''s theirs. This session pairs powerfully with Weeks 5 and 6 from Phase 1.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

You didn''t choose your family, your early friendships, or the first people who taught you what love and trust look like. But those relationships installed some pretty powerful programmes about how you connect with people. Today we look at those programmes — and decide which ones to keep.', 'Think of the relationship — family, friend, or other — that has most shaped how you trust and connect with people. What did it teach you about what relationships feel like?', 'You didn''t choose your family, your early friendships, or the first people who taught you what love and trust look like. But those relationships installed some pretty powerful programmes about how you connect with people. Today we look at those programmes — and decide which ones to keep.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WjOowWxOXCg', 'YouTube: Search ''attachment styles explained teen'' or ''how childhood affects adult relationships'' for accessible content. Alternatively: search ''anxious avoidant secure attachment animated'' for visual explainers. Runtime ~10–15 min.', '', '', '', 'What did you learn about love from the people who raised you?', 'MY RELATIONSHIP BLUEPRINT: Think about one significant relationship from your past — a parent, a close friend, a first romantic interest. What did that relationship teach you about: trust (is it safe to rely on others?), closeness (is intimacy safe?), and conflict (what happens when things go wrong?). Now: where do those same patterns show up in your current relationships? Which patterns are helpful? Which ones create problems? Share: one pattern you''ve noticed repeating across different relationships.', 'Write about a relationship pattern you''ve noticed in yourself. Where do you think it came from? Does it help you or hurt you in current relationships?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Notice once today in a friendship or family interaction when an old pattern seems to be running. Just name it silently — ''there''s the template.''', 'Tell one trusted person about a relational pattern you''ve noticed in yourself. Ask them if they see it too — and be willing to hear the answer.', 'Bring back: what did you notice about relational patterns this week?', '', '', 'I understand how I was taught to connect. I choose which patterns I carry forward — and I can build new ones.', 'Some teens may recognise painful or even traumatic relational patterns for the first time in this session. Have professional referral resources available. The tone should be empowering, not pathologising — these patterns were formed for good reasons and can be changed.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

We all develop ways of protecting ourselves when things feel unsafe — humour, sarcasm, not caring, never letting anyone get too close. Those strategies made sense once. But if the armour never comes down, you end up safe and alone. This week we look at what you''re protected against — and what you''re also blocking.', 'What''s your most reliable emotional defence? Do you get funny when things are serious? Go quiet? Get sarcastic? Pretend not to care? Agree to avoid conflict? Most of us have a signature move — what''s yours?', 'We all develop ways of protecting ourselves when things feel unsafe — humour, sarcasm, not caring, never letting anyone get too close. Those strategies made sense once. But if the armour never comes down, you end up safe and alone. This week we look at what you''re protected against — and what you''re also blocking.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iCvmsMzlF7o', 'TED Talk: Brené Brown on vulnerability — directly addresses the armour that teens most relate to (cool detachment, irony, numbing). Runtime ~20 min. Can be shown in clips.', '', '', '', 'What are you protecting, and who''s stuck on the outside of it?', 'FIREWALL AUDIT: Identify your top two or three emotional defences. For each: What situation most reliably triggers it? What was the original threat it was built against? What does it successfully protect you from? What does it also block that you actually want? What would it take — what conditions would need to be present — for you to safely lower it, even briefly? Share: one defence and what it costs you.', 'Write about the thing you most protect others from seeing in you. What would actually happen if they saw it?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Choose one low-risk moment this week to lower a small piece of your defence — let something genuine show. Notice what happens.', 'Tell one trusted person about a defence strategy you use. See how they respond to the honesty itself.', 'Bring back: what happened when you lowered the defence a little? Fear vs. reality?', '', '', 'I am strong enough to be real. Connection is worth the risk of being seen.', 'The armour session is particularly potent for teens who have experienced significant social pain or betrayal. Never pressure anyone to lower their defences in a group setting — the session is about building awareness, not demanding vulnerability. Model appropriate vulnerability as a facilitator.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Grief isn''t only about death. It''s also about things ending — friendships that changed, versions of yourself you had to leave behind, futures you imagined that didn''t happen. Most people were never taught how to grieve properly. This week we learn what grief actually requires — and why moving through it (not around it) is where growth lives.', 'What''s something that ended in your life — a friendship, a chapter, a version of yourself, something you hoped for — that you never fully got to grieve? That maybe you just... pushed through?', 'Grief isn''t only about death. It''s also about things ending — friendships that changed, versions of yourself you had to leave behind, futures you imagined that didn''t happen. Most people were never taught how to grieve properly. This week we learn what grief actually requires — and why moving through it (not around it) is where growth lives.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=khkJkR-ipfw', 'YouTube: Search ''David Kessler grief teenager'' or ''processing loss teen psychology'' for accessible content. Also: search ''post-traumatic growth explained'' for the growth-through-loss research. Runtime ~10–15 min.', '', '', '', 'What ended that you never really got over?', 'ENDINGS THAT DESERVE ACKNOWLEDGMENT: In your journal, write about one ending in your life that you never properly processed. What was lost — specifically? What did it mean to you? What did you do instead of grieving it? What would properly acknowledging it look and feel like? And: is there anything this loss has given you or made possible, even in a painful way? Share: one ending you''re beginning to honour — without necessarily sharing the full detail.', 'Write a short goodbye to something that ended — a friendship, a chapter, a dream. Say what it meant. Thank it. Let it go.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Allow yourself one quiet moment this week to acknowledge an ending you''ve been avoiding. Write it down, or just sit with it for five minutes.', 'Tell one trusted person about something you''ve lost that you haven''t talked about. Let them simply hear it.', 'Bring back: what was it like to write the goodbye? What shifted — even a little?', '', '', 'I honour my losses. Moving through them is how I make space for what''s next.', 'Adolescent grief is often unacknowledged in adult frameworks. Make explicit that loss here includes friendship endings, relationship breakdowns, family changes, identity losses — not only death. Follow CRITICAL guidelines: have wellbeing resources available, do not push anyone to share more than they are comfortable with.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Fear is useful — when it''s pointing at real danger. But most of the fear that shapes our decisions isn''t about real danger. It''s about embarrassment, failure, judgment, and uncertainty. This week we learn to tell the difference — and to stop letting discomfort run disguised as danger.', 'What''s one fear that regularly shapes your choices? Not a scary movie fear — a real one that stops you doing things you actually want to do.', 'Fear is useful — when it''s pointing at real danger. But most of the fear that shapes our decisions isn''t about real danger. It''s about embarrassment, failure, judgment, and uncertainty. This week we learn to tell the difference — and to stop letting discomfort run disguised as danger.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZizdB0TgAVM', 'YouTube: Search ''how to overcome fear psychology teen'' or ''exposure therapy explained animated'' for accessible content on the neuroscience of rewiring fear. Runtime ~10–15 min.', '', '', '', 'What are you scared of that has never actually happened?', 'DANGER vs. DISCOMFORT: List 5 fears that shape your choices. For each, honestly classify: genuine danger, or discomfort disguised as danger? For your ''discomfort'' fears: what specifically are you afraid will happen? How realistic is it? What have you missed by avoiding this? What''s the smallest step toward it? Share: one discomfort fear — and what avoiding it has cost you.', 'Write about the gap between what your fear predicts will happen — and what has actually happened the times you''ve pushed through it anyway.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Walk toward one small discomfort fear today. Notice: prediction vs. reality.', 'Tell someone about a fear you''re rewiring. Ask them to call it out gently when they see you avoiding it.', 'Bring back: what was the fear''s prediction? What actually happened?', '', '', 'I feel the fear. I name what it actually is. And I move toward what matters.', 'The fear prediction vs. reality exercise is one of the most practically powerful of the year. Teens often discover their fear''s predictions are dramatically worse than reality. Build in time for genuine reflection on past experiences of walking through fear.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

In Phase 1 we found the stories running in the background. Now we do something about them. Not all stories are ready to go — but some of them are. This week we write the upgrade: the same events, a more complete interpretation, a new author in charge.', 'Think of a story you''ve been carrying about yourself since Phase 1 — one that has shaped choices you''ve made, things you''ve avoided, how you see yourself. Has anything shifted in how you hold it over the past 12 weeks?', 'In Phase 1 we found the stories running in the background. Now we do something about them. Not all stories are ready to go — but some of them are. This week we write the upgrade: the same events, a more complete interpretation, a new author in charge.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=D9Ihs241zeg', 'YouTube: Brené Brown on stories and meaning — or search ''narrative identity teen psychology'' for accessible research-based content. Runtime ~15 min.', '', '', '', 'What story about yourself is out of date?', 'STORY UPDATE: Choose one significant story about yourself you''re carrying. Write the current version — exactly as you''ve been telling it. Then write the expanded version: What have you left out? What strengths emerged from the hard parts? What did you survive or learn that the current story doesn''t credit you for? What would the full, honest, complete story enable that the edited version prevents? Share: the opening line of the new story.', 'Write the first line of a new chapter in your story — the one that starts now, from here, having come through what you''ve come through.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Live from the new story for one day this week. Make one choice that the new story enables but the old one would have prevented.', 'Tell one person the new story — or just the direction of it. Notice what it feels like to own it.', 'Bring back: what was it like to write the new story? Did anything change?', '', '', 'I am the author of what my story means. I write from here — forward.', 'This is one of the most empowering sessions of the year — handle the writing exercise with care and adequate time. The shift from ''things happened to me'' to ''here is what I made from what happened'' is paradigm-shifting for many teens. Celebrate the new story openings that are shared.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Thirteen weeks of unlearning. Today we close Phase 2 by taking stock of what you''ve actually released — not what you''ve fixed, but what you''ve set down. What''s lighter. What has more space. And what you''re walking into Phase 3 with that you didn''t have before.', 'Name three things — even small ones — that feel lighter after these 13 weeks. Not fixed. Not solved. Just lighter. What has loosened its grip even a little?', 'Thirteen weeks of unlearning. Today we close Phase 2 by taking stock of what you''ve actually released — not what you''ve fixed, but what you''ve set down. What''s lighter. What has more space. And what you''re walking into Phase 3 with that you didn''t have before.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jqONINYF17M', 'YouTube: Carol Dweck ''The Power of Believing That You Can Improve'' — a perfect bridge between the work of unlearning and the work of rebuilding. Runtime ~10 min.', '', '', '', 'What have you put down, and what are you still holding?', 'RELEASE AND COMMIT: In your journal, complete these four sentences: ''In Phase 2, I have released or loosened...'' ''Something I see more clearly now is...'' ''I arrive at Phase 3 carrying...'' ''One commitment I make for the rebuild is...'' If you choose: share one line from any of these. It is witnessed by everyone in this room. That witnessing matters.', 'Write a letter to yourself from the beginning of Phase 2 — what do you want them to know about what''s coming, and what they''re capable of?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Revisit something you wrote at the beginning of Phase 2. Notice the gap. Acknowledge it.', 'Tell one person who has supported your journey: ''Something that is genuinely lighter for me now is...'' Let them hear it.', 'Come back ready to share one line from your release statement — if you''re willing.', '', '', 'I have done real work. I arrive at Phase 3 lighter, clearer, and ready to build.', 'Create genuine ceremony — even small rituals matter deeply at this age. The release statements shared in silence are powerful. If the group has developed strong trust over Phase 2, this session can be one of the most moving of the year. Honour every share. End with genuine excitement for Phase 3.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

After two phases of looking honestly at what you''ve absorbed and what you''re releasing, we arrive at the most important question of Phase 3: who are YOU? Not the roles, not the labels, not the history. The actual you — right now — with the agency to choose who you''re becoming. Today we begin building that deliberately.', 'Here''s the question: if you could design your character from scratch — the qualities, values, and ways of being that you most want to embody — what would you build? Don''t start with what''s realistic. Start with what''s true.', 'After two phases of looking honestly at what you''ve absorbed and what you''re releasing, we arrive at the most important question of Phase 3: who are YOU? Not the roles, not the labels, not the history. The actual you — right now — with the agency to choose who you''re becoming. Today we begin building that deliberately.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W1eYrhGeffc', 'YouTube: Search ''identity formation teen psychology'' or James Clear on identity-based habits — ''Atomic Habits identity change.'' Highly practical and directly relevant. Runtime ~10–15 min.', '', '', '', 'If nobody had ever told you who you were, who would you be?', 'IDENTITY BUILDER: In your journal, answer from your most honest self: ''The three qualities I most want to embody are...'' / ''The kind of person I am choosing to become is...'' / ''What I stand for — my non-negotiables — are...'' / ''The things I want people to genuinely experience when they''re around me are...'' Now: look at what you''ve written. Does your current daily life reflect this? Where is the biggest gap? Share: one quality you''re actively building.', 'Write ''I am the kind of person who...'' five times — completing it each time with something you genuinely want to be true. Read it back to yourself daily this week.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Live from one identity quality today. Act as if you are already that person, in at least one interaction.', 'Tell one person: ''Something I''m genuinely building in myself right now is...'' Notice what it feels like to own it.', 'Bring back: what happened when you acted from your identity quality? What felt true?', '', '', 'I am building the person I actually want to be — on purpose, from values, one day at a time.', 'The identity builder exercise is one of the most genuinely exciting of the year — create space for teens to really sit with it. The ''I am the kind of person who...'' reframe should be practised in the room, not just discussed. Have them write it on cards they keep.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Values aren''t what you say you believe — they''re what you demonstrate with your time, energy, and choices. Most people have never actually thought about what their values are. And most people are living primarily from absorbed values — other people''s ideas about what matters — rather than ones they actually chose. This week we get explicit.', 'Quick: what are your values? If you can list them confidently — what actually determines your choices day to day? If it''s harder than expected, that''s completely normal. Most people haven''t done this work. Today we do.', 'Values aren''t what you say you believe — they''re what you demonstrate with your time, energy, and choices. Most people have never actually thought about what their values are. And most people are living primarily from absorbed values — other people''s ideas about what matters — rather than ones they actually chose. This week we get explicit.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jHeeHg_MXNE', 'YouTube: Search ''values clarification teen psychology'' or ''knowing your values animated'' for accessible content. Russ Harris on ACT values is excellent and accessible. Runtime ~10–15 min.', '', '', '', 'What would you not give up, whatever you were offered?', 'VALUES EXCAVATION: List everything you think you value. Then for each: Is this genuinely mine — or have I absorbed it? Is it a means to something else (like ''success'' to get approval) or valuable in itself? Narrow to your top 5. For each of the 5: Write a specific, observable behaviour that would demonstrate this value. Where are you most aligned? Least? If two values clash — freedom vs. loyalty, honesty vs. kindness — which wins? Share: your top three values and one way they show up in your life.', 'Write your personal values as ''I am the kind of person who...'' statements — one for each of your top values. Read them back to yourself. Notice which ones feel true already and which ones are aspirational.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Make one decision today explicitly from your top value. Notice what changes.', 'Share your top values with one person who knows you well. Ask: do you actually see these in me? Receive the answer.', 'Bring back: where did you live most clearly from your values this week?', '', '', 'My values are mine — chosen, not absorbed. They are the compass I build from.', 'The ''absorbed vs. chosen values'' distinction is the key insight of this session. Give teens genuine time to wrestle with it — the discomfort of realising you''ve been living from values you didn''t choose is productive and important. Celebrate any moment of genuine self-authorship.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

We mapped habits in Phase 1 and cleared some in Phase 2. Now we build the ones that actually express who you''re choosing to be. Not willpower-based habits that burn out — identity-based ones that compound quietly. This is where Phase 3 gets real.', 'Think of one quality from your identity builder in Week 27. Now: what''s the smallest daily habit that would actually express that quality? Not a big commitment — the tiniest version that still counts.', 'We mapped habits in Phase 1 and cleared some in Phase 2. Now we build the ones that actually express who you''re choosing to be. Not willpower-based habits that burn out — identity-based ones that compound quietly. This is where Phase 3 gets real.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W1eYrhGeffc', 'YouTube: James Clear on atomic habits — search ''James Clear atomic habits summary'' for short accessible versions. Also: BJ Fogg ''Tiny Habits'' for the minimum viable approach. Runtime ~10–15 min.', '', '', '', 'What do you do every day that''s quietly making you someone?', 'HABIT DESIGN: Choose two habits to build — one for your inner life (mind, reflection, learning) and one for your outer life (body, relationships, creative expression). For each: Write the identity it expresses (''I am the kind of person who...''). Define the SMALLEST possible daily version. Identify the habit stack anchor. Design one environmental change to support it. Share: your two minimum viable habits.', 'Write your two-habit design out in full — identity statement, minimum version, anchor, environment change.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Start your first minimum habit TODAY. Doesn''t have to be perfect. Just has to happen.', 'Tell one person your identity-based habit and the minimum version. Ask them to check in with you next week.', 'Bring back: how many days did you show up? What helped? What got in the way?', '', '', 'I build the person I''m becoming one small, consistent habit at a time.', 'The minimum viable habit concept is genuinely liberating for teens who have attempted and failed large habit changes. Emphasise: the smallness is the point, not a compromise. Starting is everything. Have them physically write the habit on a card they carry.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Everything we''ve been building — self-awareness, emotional intelligence, identity, values — runs on your physical hardware. Sleep, movement, and how you fuel yourself are not separate from personal development. They ARE personal development. This week we treat the body like the foundation it is.', 'Honest check-in: How many hours of sleep did you get last night? When did you last move your body in a way that felt good? How did you fuel yourself today? No judgment — just data. What does this baseline tell you?', 'Everything we''ve been building — self-awareness, emotional intelligence, identity, values — runs on your physical hardware. Sleep, movement, and how you fuel yourself are not separate from personal development. They ARE personal development. This week we treat the body like the foundation it is.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5MuIMqhT8oY', 'YouTube: ''Sleep is Your Superpower'' by Matthew Walker — directly relevant to teens and highly engaging. Runtime ~19 min. Also: search ''exercise and teen mental health research'' for movement evidence.', '', '', '', 'What does your body need that you keep ignoring?', 'BODY AUDIT: Rate yourself 1–10 in four areas: sleep, movement, nourishment, ability to calm down when stressed. For your lowest score: what one small change would most move the needle? Not the perfect change — the most accessible one. Design the minimum viable version and the environment change that supports it. Share: your lowest area and your one small upgrade.', 'Write your minimum body foundation protocol for this week — what you commit to for sleep, movement, nourishment, and one stress regulation practice.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Implement your lowest-score area change today — the smallest possible version. Track it for seven days.', 'Tell one person about your body foundation goal. Ask them what they''ve noticed about the connection between their physical state and how they show up mentally and emotionally.', 'Bring back: what changed in your mood, energy, or capacity when you prioritised your body this week?', '', '', 'My body is the foundation everything else grows from. I take care of it like it matters — because it does.', 'Be extremely careful not to let this session tip into body image territory — this is entirely about function, energy, and wellbeing, not appearance. Acknowledge the very real structural barriers to sleep and healthy eating for teens (school schedules, family systems, finances). The goal is the highest-leverage small change, not the perfect protocol.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

The people you spend the most time with have more influence on who you become than almost anything else. Not through dramatic conversations — just through daily presence, what gets normalised, what gets reinforced, what gets expanded or contracted. This week we get intentional about who''s in your circle.', 'Think of the three people you spend the most time with. After spending time with each of them, do you generally feel better or worse about yourself? More or less like who you want to be? That''s important data.', 'The people you spend the most time with have more influence on who you become than almost anything else. Not through dramatic conversations — just through daily presence, what gets normalised, what gets reinforced, what gets expanded or contracted. This week we get intentional about who''s in your circle.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q4g_cxMWnMk', 'YouTube: Robert Waldinger ''What Makes a Good Life?'' — the Harvard Study findings on relationships, presented accessibly. Genuinely moving and highly relevant. Runtime ~13 min.', '', '', '', 'Who do you become when you''re with your closest mates?', 'RELATIONSHIP ENERGY AUDIT: Think of your 5–6 most significant relationships. For each, honestly: After spending time with this person, do I feel more or less like the person I want to be? Expanded or contracted? Closer to or further from my values? Sort them into two columns: Expanding and Contracting. Now: are there expanding relationships you''re under-investing in? Contracting ones you''re staying in out of habit or obligation? What would intentional action look like? Share: one relationship you want to invest more in.', 'Write about the social environment you are actively building — who you want to attract into your life as you grow, and what you offer to the people who choose to be close to you.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Reach out to one expanding relationship today — tell them specifically what you value about them.', 'Tell one expanding person in your life: ''I want you to know that time with you genuinely helps me grow.'' Notice what that does for both of you.', 'Bring back: what happened when you invested in an expanding relationship this week?', '', '', 'I choose my circle with intention. The people I spend time with are part of how I build.', 'The energy audit can be genuinely challenging — teens may realise that their primary social group is contracting rather than expanding. Emphasise the distinction between ending relationships and relating to them differently. The goal is intentionality, not social restructuring.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

The voice in your head is the one you''ll hear more than any other person''s voice in your entire life. What quality is it? What does it say on a hard day? What does it say when you succeed? What does it say when you first wake up? This week we make that voice deliberately good.', 'If I asked you to play me a 10-second clip of your most common internal soundtrack — the running commentary in your head on a normal day — what would it sound like? What would the dominant tone be?', 'The voice in your head is the one you''ll hear more than any other person''s voice in your entire life. What quality is it? What does it say on a hard day? What does it say when you succeed? What does it say when you first wake up? This week we make that voice deliberately good.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NiuDFBNDoSk', 'YouTube: Ethan Kross on self-talk research — search ''Ethan Kross chatter self-talk'' for highly accessible and directly relevant talks. Runtime ~15 min.', '', '', '', 'What would you say to a mate who was where you are?', 'SELF-TALK REDESIGN: For three situations — waking up, a moment of difficulty, and after something goes wrong — write: your current typical self-talk, and your redesigned version using the principles above. The redesigned version should be: honest (not fake positive), compassionate, specific rather than global, and forward-oriented (''what next?'' rather than ''why again?''). Create 3 anchor phrases for key daily moments. Share: your redesigned self-talk for one of the three situations.', 'Write your three anchor phrases on a card you''ll keep somewhere visible. Use them deliberately for seven days and track what shifts.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Use your morning anchor phrase tomorrow and report what it does for the start of your day.', 'Share your anchor phrases with one trusted person. Ask them what self-talk they most wish they could change.', 'Bring back: how did your anchor phrases change your day? What surprised you?', '', '', 'The voice in my head is worth choosing. I make it honest, compassionate, and on my side.', 'Anchor phrases work best when they''re genuinely personalised — spend time helping teens craft ones that sound like them, not like a motivational poster. The self-distancing technique (using your own name) is one of the most evidence-based and easily practised tools of the year — make sure it''s properly understood.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Structure isn''t the enemy of freedom — it''s what makes freedom possible. When you design your time deliberately, you stop spending energy deciding what to do next, you protect the things that actually matter, and you stop being at the mercy of whatever is loudest. This week we design your personal architecture.', 'Think about your average day. When does your time and energy go to things you''ve actively chosen — and when does it just get absorbed by whatever''s loudest? What important things consistently get crowded out?', 'Structure isn''t the enemy of freedom — it''s what makes freedom possible. When you design your time deliberately, you stop spending energy deciding what to do next, you protect the things that actually matter, and you stop being at the mercy of whatever is loudest. This week we design your personal architecture.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gTaJhjQHcf8', 'YouTube: Cal Newport on daily structure and deep work — search ''Cal Newport schedule daily structure'' for accessible versions. Runtime ~10–15 min.', '', '', '', 'What in your week is helping you, and what''s just habit?', 'DAILY DESIGN: Map your ideal school/work day in three categories: 1. Non-negotiables — the things that must happen for you to function and grow (sleep, movement, study focus, real connection). 2. Valuable but flexible — things that matter but can move around. 3. Default fillers — things that happen automatically that you''re not actively choosing (e.g. endless scrolling, reacting to notifications). Now: what needs explicit scheduling? What default filler could be reduced to create space for what actually matters? Share: your one biggest structural change.', 'Write your minimum viable daily structure — the non-negotiable anchors that make a good day possible.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Implement one structural protection this week — block one important daily activity as non-negotiable. Test it for seven days.', 'Tell one person about your structural change. Ask them to check in on whether you protected it.', 'Bring back: what happened when you protected your structural time? What became possible?', '', '', 'I design my days around what matters. Structure is how I protect what I''m building.', 'Many teens resist ''structure'' because they associate it with restriction. Reframe explicitly: structure is the container that protects your freedom. The three-category exercise (non-negotiable/valuable/filler) is eye-opening — most teens have not audited where their time actually goes.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Rest isn''t what happens after you''ve earned it. Rest is part of the practice — just as important as effort, study, and creation. This week we rebuild the relationship with rest: what it actually is, why it matters, and why you might be confusing distraction with recovery.', 'What does rest actually look like for you right now? Be honest. Is it genuine recovery — or is it just different stimulation? What''s the difference in how you feel after each?', 'Rest isn''t what happens after you''ve earned it. Rest is part of the practice — just as important as effort, study, and creation. This week we rebuild the relationship with rest: what it actually is, why it matters, and why you might be confusing distraction with recovery.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9y1xyXtYAsg', 'YouTube: Search ''default mode network rest creativity teen brain'' or ''why rest matters neuroscience'' for accessible content. Also: Matthew Walker on sleep as the foundation of rest. Runtime ~10–15 min.', '', '', '', 'When did you last properly rest and not feel guilty?', 'REST vs. DISTRACTION AUDIT: For the past week, track every ''rest'' period — what you actually did, and how you felt after. Categorise each as: genuine rest (felt genuinely replenishing), distraction (passed time but didn''t restore), or productive recovery (served a function but not deeply restorative). What''s the ratio? What would genuine rest look like for you specifically — what activities, conditions, duration? Design one genuine rest practice. Share: what rest actually looks like for you when it works.', 'Design your personal rest protocol — specific activities, conditions, and frequency — and schedule it for this week as a non-negotiable.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Take one genuine rest break today — not earned, not conditional. Just scheduled. Notice what follows it.', 'Tell one person about your rest practice. Ask them what rest actually looks like for them — and whether they''re getting enough of it.', 'Bring back: what happened during your genuine rest? What did you notice in the hours after it?', '', '', 'Rest is part of my practice — not a reward for finishing. It''s how I sustain everything else.', 'Many teens are chronically stimulation-saturated and have lost the capacity for genuine rest. The five-minute silence in the session is often profoundly uncomfortable for this age group — honour that, explore it, and use it as evidence for why the practice matters. Frame rest as performance strategy, not indulgence.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Creativity isn''t a talent some people have and others don''t. It is a fundamental human capacity — the ability to make something that didn''t exist before and express what is true for you. Most people shut it down by making it about evaluation rather than expression. This week we reclaim it.', 'What do you make, create, or express — even privately, even badly — just because it feels good? Is there something you used to make that you stopped? What happened?', 'Creativity isn''t a talent some people have and others don''t. It is a fundamental human capacity — the ability to make something that didn''t exist before and express what is true for you. Most people shut it down by making it about evaluation rather than expression. This week we reclaim it.', 'YouTube: Elizabeth Gilbert ''Your Elusive Creative Genius'' TED Talk — one of the most accessible and permission-giving talks about creativity available. Runtime ~19 min.', 'Search: ''Elizabeth Gilbert creative genius TED Talk'' if unavailable. Alternative: search ''creativity is for everyone not just artists'' for accessible shorter content.', '', '', '', 'What did you love making before someone told you if you were good at it?', 'CREATIVE RECLAMATION: Write about: What creative expression feels most alive for you — even if you barely do it? What do you notice you want to make, say, or express that you don''t act on? What specifically stops you (evaluation, comparison, time, fear of ''not being good'')? Design a private creative practice for this week — something made for nobody but you, not to be evaluated, shared, or judged. Just made. Share: the creative form that feels most alive for you.', 'Begin something creative this week — private, judgment-free, just for you. 10 minutes minimum. No evaluation.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Tell one person about a creative impulse you''ve been suppressing. Notice what happens when you claim it aloud.', 'Bring back: what did you make? And how did the MAKING feel — regardless of the output?', 'I make things because expression is part of being alive. The making is the point.', '', '', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iG9CE55wbtY', '', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Purpose isn''t a big dramatic declaration about your future career. It''s a direction — the sense that what you''re doing matters, connects to something bigger than just you, and expresses something genuine about who you are. This week we find that direction — not as a final answer, but as a starting orientation.', 'What makes you lose track of time? What problems or injustices genuinely bother you — that you find yourself wanting to do something about? What comes so naturally to you that you forget other people might find it difficult? Those three questions are the beginning of purpose.', 'Purpose isn''t a big dramatic declaration about your future career. It''s a direction — the sense that what you''re doing matters, connects to something bigger than just you, and expresses something genuine about who you are. This week we find that direction — not as a final answer, but as a starting orientation.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fLJsdqxnZb0', 'YouTube: ''How to Find Work You Love'' by Scott Dinsmore — highly accessible and directly relevant for teens. Runtime ~18 min. Also: search ''ikigai explained teen'' for shorter animated versions.', '', '', '', 'What are you doing when you lose track of time?', 'PURPOSE MAPPING: In your journal, work through three circles: 1. What I love — activities that make time disappear, things I could do or talk about for hours. 2. What I''m good at — what comes naturally, what others come to me for. 3. What I care about in the world — problems that bother me, things I wish were different. Now: where do these overlap? What sits at the centre — even imperfectly? That''s your current purpose direction. Share: your three circles and the approximate overlap.', 'Write your current purpose orientation as: ''I am here to contribute...'' — not as a final answer, but as an honest starting point.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Make one choice today from your purpose orientation — one small act that aligns with your direction.', 'Share your purpose direction with one trusted person. Ask them: ''What do you think I''m naturally here to contribute?'' Listen to their answer.', 'Bring back: what happened when you acted from your purpose direction this week?', '', '', 'I have a direction that is genuinely mine. And from that direction, I contribute something the world needs.', 'Avoid framing purpose as career planning — this shuts down genuine exploration. Frame it as direction and contribution. Some teens will find clear overlaps immediately; others will need more time. Both are appropriate. The key takeaway: having any direction matters more than having the perfect answer.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Money is one of the most loaded, confusing, and rarely discussed topics in most families — which means most of us have absorbed a lot of stories about it without ever examining them. This week we look at what you''ve inherited about money and resources, and begin to build a healthier relationship with it.', 'What were you taught — explicitly or by osmosis — about money growing up? Was it talked about openly or in hushed tones? Was there enough of it, or chronic worry? What did you learn about whether people like you had it?', 'Money is one of the most loaded, confusing, and rarely discussed topics in most families — which means most of us have absorbed a lot of stories about it without ever examining them. This week we look at what you''ve inherited about money and resources, and begin to build a healthier relationship with it.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8gxNHkQBkF8', 'YouTube: Search ''money psychology teens inherited beliefs'' or ''behavioural economics money explained teen'' for accessible content. Also: search ''money and happiness research'' for the wellbeing dimension. Runtime ~10–15 min.', '', '', '', 'What did you learn about money growing up?', 'MONEY STORY AUDIT: In your journal: What is the dominant financial story from your family? What did money represent — security, status, shame, freedom, conflict? What do you currently believe about whether you deserve financial abundance? What is your default money script? Where does it help you — and where does it limit you? What would a healthy, values-aligned relationship with money look like for you? Share: one thing you''ve inherited about money that you want to examine.', 'Write your values-aligned financial orientation: ''Money in my life is for...'' and ''I want to relate to resources by...'' Keep it about values and relationship, not amounts.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Make one resource decision this week that is deliberately aligned with your values rather than habit or anxiety.', 'Share one thing you''ve inherited about money with one trusted person. Just naming it out loud changes its power.', 'Bring back: what came up when you examined your money story? What surprised you?', '', '', 'My relationship with money is mine to build. I use resources in alignment with what I genuinely value.', 'Be sensitive to the very wide range of financial circumstances in the room. Keep the focus entirely on the psychological relationship, not financial outcomes or status. For any teen experiencing genuine financial hardship, have referral resources available (school counsellor, social services).', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Humans are social animals — we are literally designed for community. The quality of your connections isn''t a nice extra to sort out later. It''s one of the foundations of everything: your mental health, your resilience, your ability to grow. This week we get intentional about building the community you actually want.', 'Think about your social life honestly: do you have people who genuinely know you — not your performance, but the real you? People who you can be honest with, who challenge you to be better, and who you feel safe being imperfect with? How many? And is that enough?', 'Humans are social animals — we are literally designed for community. The quality of your connections isn''t a nice extra to sort out later. It''s one of the foundations of everything: your mental health, your resilience, your ability to grow. This week we get intentional about building the community you actually want.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q4g_cxMWnMg', 'YouTube: Robert Waldinger ''What Makes a Good Life?'' — the Harvard Study findings, completely accessible for teens. One of the most important talks of the year. Runtime ~13 min.', '', '', '', 'What do you bring that a room is worse without?', 'COMMUNITY MAP: Draw a map of your social world. At the centre: you. Around you in concentric circles: people you feel most genuinely known by (inner circle), people you''re connected to but not deeply known (middle circle), people you''d like to know better (outer circle). Now: is your inner circle large enough? What would it take to grow it? Who in your outer circle would you like to move closer? Share: one person you want to invest in more — and one step you''ll take.', 'Write about the community you are building — the quality of connection you want, what you''re willing to offer, and the kind of relationships you''re actively cultivating.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Reach out to one person in your outer circle this week — move them a step closer. Or invest more deeply in your inner circle.', 'Tell one person in your inner circle something specific about what they mean to you. Be genuine.', 'Bring back: what happened when you invested in a real connection this week?', '', '', 'I build real community — people who know me, who I know, and who we grow together with.', 'The loneliness paradox (more connected, less belonging) resonates deeply with teens. Validate the experience without amplifying it. The community map activity creates a genuinely useful visual of where to invest. Celebrate the community already present in the room — 38 weeks of this group is the concrete example.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Thirteen weeks of rebuilding. Today we close Phase 3 by naming what has actually been built — not what you''ve fixed or resolved, but what is genuinely present now that wasn''t before. And we step toward Phase 4 with something real to bring.', 'What is the most significant thing you have built in Phase 3 — not achieved or accomplished, but genuinely built in yourself? Something that feels more truly yours than it did 13 weeks ago?', 'Thirteen weeks of rebuilding. Today we close Phase 3 by naming what has actually been built — not what you''ve fixed or resolved, but what is genuinely present now that wasn''t before. And we step toward Phase 4 with something real to bring.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jqONINYF17M', 'YouTube: Carol Dweck ''The Power of Believing That You Can Improve'' — the perfect bridge between building and contributing. Runtime ~10 min.', '', '', '', 'What''s different about how you live now?', 'PHASE 3 LETTER: Write a letter to the version of you who began Phase 3 — thirteen weeks ago. What do you want them to know about what was built? What are you proud of that they couldn''t yet see? What are you walking into Phase 4 with? Share one line — if you''re willing. It is witnessed by everyone here.', 'Write three things you have built in Phase 3. Then write: ''I am bringing this into Phase 4: ...''', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Live from one thing you built in Phase 3 today — one intentional expression of the identity, values, or habit you''ve been constructing.', 'Tell someone who has witnessed your journey: ''Something I''ve genuinely built this phase is...'' Own it.', 'Come back ready to share: what are you bringing into Phase 4?', '', '', 'I have built something real. I arrive at Phase 4 ready to live from it — and offer it.', 'Give genuine ceremony to this closing — this is the third threshold and the community has now been together for 39 weeks. The letters read aloud are powerful. The acknowledgment that Phase 4 is about contribution and outward expression generates real excitement. Honour everything that has been built.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

You''ve spent almost a year doing serious inner work — seeing yourself clearly, releasing old patterns, building something real. Phase 4 is the turn outward: taking what you''ve built and offering it to the people around you. Not because you should. Because you genuinely have something to give now.', 'What is one thing you''ve learned about yourself or life this year that you wish someone had told you earlier? Who around you could use that knowledge right now?', 'You''ve spent almost a year doing serious inner work — seeing yourself clearly, releasing old patterns, building something real. Phase 4 is the turn outward: taking what you''ve built and offering it to the people around you. Not because you should. Because you genuinely have something to give now.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lmyZMtPVodo', 'YouTube: Search ''teen service and wellbeing research'' or ''why helping others makes you happier science'' for accessible evidence-based content. Runtime ~10 min.', '', '', '', 'Who''s better off because of the work you''ve done this year?', 'SERVICE INVENTORY: What has this year given you? List the insights, capacities, and qualities you''ve genuinely developed. For each: who in your life could benefit from this? What specific form would giving it take — a conversation, showing up differently, sharing something you''ve learned, being present in a new way? What is the smallest, most genuine act of service you could offer this week? Share: one thing you''ve grown that you want to give.', 'Write a note to someone in your life about something you''ve learned this year that you think would help them. You don''t have to send it — but write it as if you will.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Do one thing today that gives something you''ve genuinely built this year to someone who could use it.', 'Tell one person about something from your inner work this year that you want to share. Then share it.', 'Bring back: what happened when you offered something outward? How did it feel to give from fullness rather than obligation?', '', '', 'I have something real to give now. I turn toward others — freely, genuinely, from everything this year has built.', 'The turn to service can feel abstract for teens — make it immediate and specific. ''Who in your life needs what you''ve learned?'' is the right question. Avoid framing this as volunteering or grand altruism — the most powerful service teens offer is presence, honesty, and willingness to share their genuine experience with peers.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

The best way to test whether you actually understand something is to try to explain it to someone else. If you can teach it clearly, you genuinely know it. If you get stuck, you''ve found where you still have learning to do. This week we teach — and discover what we actually know.', 'What is the most important thing you''ve learned this year? Write it down right now — the core of it, in one or two sentences. Now: is it actually clear? Could someone who doesn''t know you understand it from what you''ve written?', 'The best way to test whether you actually understand something is to try to explain it to someone else. If you can teach it clearly, you genuinely know it. If you get stuck, you''ve found where you still have learning to do. This week we teach — and discover what we actually know.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FLbqzbAaEiI', 'YouTube: Search ''Feynman technique explained simply'' or ''learning by teaching protégé effect teen'' for accessible content. Runtime ~8–10 min.', '', '', '', 'What do you know now that you wish someone had told you?', 'TEACH IT: Choose one insight from this year. Write it in two versions: Version 1 — explain it as if to your best friend (conversational, honest, from your own experience). Version 2 — explain it as if to a younger kid who''s going through something you''ve been through. Notice where it''s easy and where you get stuck. The stuck places are the learning edges. Share: your Version 1 explanation — and one place it got stuck.', 'Write a ''what I know now'' letter — one page, honest, from your own experience this year. Keep it. It will matter to someone someday.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Share one thing you''ve learned with one person today. From your experience, not from a textbook. Notice what lands.', 'Ask a younger person or a peer: ''Can I share something I''ve been learning this year?'' Then share it. Notice their response.', 'Bring back: what did you discover about your own understanding when you tried to teach it?', '', '', 'I know this year''s work fully enough to give it away. Teaching is how I complete the learning.', 'Build in time in the session for actual peer explanation attempts — not just writing. The experience of explaining something to another person in the room and feeling where it lands and where it doesn''t is irreplaceable. Celebrate the stumbles as much as the clarity.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

All this inner work — all the honesty and growth and becoming — only matters when it shows up in how you actually live. Phase 4 is about the courage to be genuinely seen: to show up as who you''ve actually become, not the managed version, not the performance. Today we practise that.', 'Think of the gap between who you are privately — who you know yourself to be from this year''s work — and who you present publicly in your main social group. How big is that gap? What are you hiding or managing?', 'All this inner work — all the honesty and growth and becoming — only matters when it shows up in how you actually live. Phase 4 is about the courage to be genuinely seen: to show up as who you''ve actually become, not the managed version, not the performance. Today we practise that.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iCvmsMzlF7o', 'TED Talk: Brené Brown on vulnerability and genuine connection — directly relevant to this session. Runtime ~20 min. Can show in clips.', '', '', '', 'What''s true about you that you''ve never let anyone see?', 'VISIBILITY AUDIT: In which relationships are you most genuinely yourself? In which are you most performing? What specifically are you hiding in the performing relationships — and why? What is the cost of maintaining the performance? What would one step toward genuine visibility look like in your most performing relationship? Share: one thing you want to stop hiding.', 'Write: ''What I want people to actually know about me is...'' and ''What I''m ready to stop hiding is...'' You don''t have to share this — but write it as a genuine statement.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'In one interaction today, drop one managed performance. Let something real show. Notice what happens.', 'Tell one trusted person something genuine about yourself that you usually manage or hide. Notice their response.', 'Bring back: what happened when you let yourself be a little more genuinely seen?', '', '', 'I show up as who I actually am. That is the only way to be genuinely connected.', 'The belonging vs. fitting in distinction (Brené Brown) is one of the most resonant concepts for this age group — name it explicitly. The gap between private self and public self is often largest in adolescence. Validate the difficulty while reinforcing the reward: genuine connection is only possible through genuine presence.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Values are easy when everything is fine. The real test is whether they hold when something costs you — when your friends expect something different, when it''s easier to compromise, when the pressure to go along is strong. This week we practise holding our values when it actually matters.', 'Think of a time this year when you compromised something you said mattered to you — when you went along with something that felt wrong, or didn''t speak up when you should have. What happened? What made it hard to hold?', 'Values are easy when everything is fine. The real test is whether they hold when something costs you — when your friends expect something different, when it''s easier to compromise, when the pressure to go along is strong. This week we practise holding our values when it actually matters.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jHeeHg_MXNE', 'YouTube: Search ''peer pressure and values teen psychology research'' or ''standing up for your values under pressure'' for accessible content. Runtime ~10–15 min.', '', '', '', 'When did you last go against what you believe because of pressure?', 'PRESSURE SCENARIOS: For each of your top three values, write: One recent moment you held this value under pressure — what happened? One recent moment you compromised it — what happened honestly? One likely upcoming scenario where this value will be tested. Pre-decide now: what will you specifically do or say? Make it concrete. Share: one pre-decision you''ve made for an upcoming pressure test.', 'Write your pre-decisions for your top three values under their most likely pressure scenarios. Keep it somewhere you''ll see it.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Today, notice once when a value is under even mild pressure. Hold it — even imperfectly. Notice what it feels like to choose it anyway.', 'Tell one trusted person one of your pre-decisions. Ask them to hold you to it.', 'Bring back: did a value come under pressure this week? What happened? Did having pre-decided help?', '', '', 'My values are mine — I hold them under pressure. Not perfectly. Consistently.', 'The pre-decision technique is essential to teach explicitly — many teens have never heard of it. The neuroscience of peer pressure (social threat system) is important to name because it de-shames the difficulty. This session should reference Week 28 values explicitly.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Most people treat conflict as something to avoid or win. Both miss the point. Conflict — handled honestly — is one of the fastest routes to genuine understanding, better relationships, and knowing yourself more clearly. This week we learn how to actually engage conflict rather than manage around it.', 'Think of a current conflict or tension in your life — with a friend, family member, anyone. What are you arguing about at the surface level? Now go deeper: what do you actually need that you''re not getting? What do you think they need?', 'Most people treat conflict as something to avoid or win. Both miss the point. Conflict — handled honestly — is one of the fastest routes to genuine understanding, better relationships, and knowing yourself more clearly. This week we learn how to actually engage conflict rather than manage around it.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l7ToNudVd2I', 'YouTube: Search ''Nonviolent Communication explained simply teen'' or ''how to handle conflict constructively teen psychology'' for accessible content. Runtime ~10–15 min.', '', '', '', 'What argument have you been avoiding, and what are you protecting?', 'CONFLICT REFRAME: Think of a current conflict. Write: What is the surface argument — what are you fighting about? What do you actually NEED underneath the argument — autonomy, respect, to be heard, safety, fairness? What do you think THEY need underneath it? Now: is there any way both needs could be met — not perfectly, but genuinely? Write a request (specific, actionable, positive — ''I need you to...'' not ''stop doing...''). Share: the need underneath your position — not the conflict details.', 'Write the conversation you want to have — starting with your need, not your position. What would change if you began there?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'In one difficult interaction today, try naming what you actually need rather than what you want the other person to do. Notice what changes.', 'Have one difficult conversation you''ve been avoiding. Start with your need. See what happens.', 'Bring back: what happened when you named the need instead of the position?', '', '', 'I bring my genuine self to conflict — with honesty, with curiosity, and with care for both our needs.', 'The needs vs. positions reframe is genuinely transformative for teens — many have never had this framework. The exercise of identifying your own need and guessing the other person''s need is powerful done in pairs. Acknowledge that not all conflicts resolve — some needs are genuinely incompatible. The goal is honest engagement, not guaranteed resolution.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Generosity isn''t about grand gestures or having a lot to give. It is a way of being in the world — of arriving at every encounter asking ''what can I offer?'' rather than ''what will I get?'' It''s one of the most powerful orientations available. And research shows it makes the generous person happier, not just the recipient.', 'On a normal day, what percentage of your interactions are ''what can I get?'' and what percentage are ''what can I give?'' Be honest — not what you aspire to, but what you actually notice.', 'Generosity isn''t about grand gestures or having a lot to give. It is a way of being in the world — of arriving at every encounter asking ''what can I offer?'' rather than ''what will I get?'' It''s one of the most powerful orientations available. And research shows it makes the generous person happier, not just the recipient.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=M7SBFnFvPeY', 'YouTube: ''Are You a Giver or a Taker?'' by Adam Grant — accessible, evidence-based, highly engaging for teens. Runtime ~13 min.', '', '', '', 'What do you give that costs you nothing and means a lot to someone?', 'GENEROSITY INVENTORY: In what ways are you already generous — with time, attention, honesty, encouragement, skills? What has this generosity cost you? In what ways are you habitually withholding — and what is driving that withholding? Design one deliberate act of generosity this week that costs you something real and is given freely, without expectation. Share: one form of generosity you''re committing to practise.', 'Write your generosity commitment — not a list of acts, but a description of the quality of presence you want to practise.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Make one genuinely generous act today — something that costs you real time or attention, given freely.', 'Tell one person something specific and genuine that you appreciate about them. Give it as a genuine gift.', 'Bring back: what happened when you gave generously? What did you notice?', '', '', 'I give freely from what I''ve built. Generosity is my way of being in the world.', 'The Adam Grant research genuinely shifts perspectives — share it clearly. The distinction between otherish giving and self-erasing matters particularly for teens who have people-pleasing patterns. The forms of generosity available to teens (presence, honesty, encouragement, showing up) should be named explicitly and celebrated.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

There is always going to be someone with more followers, better grades, more opportunities, a better body, more popularity. The ''more'' game never ends. This week we practise something radical: deciding that what you have right now is enough to start from. Not to stop growing — but to stop waiting.', 'What condition are you waiting for before you''ll feel like you have enough — enough confidence, enough success, enough followers, enough of whatever it is? Now honestly: will that condition, when met, actually feel like enough? Or will the threshold move?', 'There is always going to be someone with more followers, better grades, more opportunities, a better body, more popularity. The ''more'' game never ends. This week we practise something radical: deciding that what you have right now is enough to start from. Not to stop growing — but to stop waiting.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oHGKTZSe_k4', 'YouTube: Search ''arrival fallacy Tal Ben-Shahar happiness research'' or ''gratitude practice research teen wellbeing'' for accessible content. Runtime ~10–15 min.', '', '', '', 'What''s already enough that you keep treating like it isn''t?', 'ENOUGH AUDIT: Write honestly: What conditions are you waiting for before you feel like you have enough? For each condition: Is the threshold fixed — or will it move when you meet it? What would you do differently today if you genuinely believed you already had enough to start? Design one daily sufficiency practice — one specific moment where you deliberately notice what is already enough. Share: one thing that is genuinely enough that you''ve been treating as insufficient.', 'Write your personal sufficiency statement. One sentence. Honest, specific, yours. Say it to yourself when you wake up for the next seven days.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Say your sufficiency statement tomorrow morning. Notice what it does to the start of the day.', 'Tell one person one genuine thing you recognise as enough — not a gratitude performance, but a real acknowledgment.', 'Bring back: what happened when you practised the sufficiency statement for one week?', '', '', 'I have enough to begin from. I stop waiting and start living from what is already here.', 'This session explicitly builds on and extends Week 20 (scarcity) and Weeks 5–6 (comparison loop). Reference both. The arrival fallacy concept is highly resonant for achievement-focused teens. The daily sufficiency statement is the most practically powerful take-home of this session.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

We live in an instant culture — instant feedback, instant results, instant gratification. But the most important things in life — character, genuine skill, deep relationships, real wisdom — all take time. This week we practise the orientation of the long game: trusting the process even when you can''t see the results yet.', 'Think of someone you admire — someone who has genuinely developed a character quality, skill, or wisdom that you respect. How long do you think it took them to develop it? And what does that tell you about where you are right now?', 'We live in an instant culture — instant feedback, instant results, instant gratification. But the most important things in life — character, genuine skill, deep relationships, real wisdom — all take time. This week we practise the orientation of the long game: trusting the process even when you can''t see the results yet.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TQMbvJNRpLE', 'YouTube: Angela Duckworth ''Grit: The Power of Passion and Perseverance'' TED Talk — one of the most important short talks for teens on long-game thinking. Runtime ~6 min.', '', '', '', 'What are you working at that hasn''t shown yet?', 'LONG GAME LETTER: Write a letter to yourself to be opened in three years. Not a goals list — a genuine letter from who you are now to who you will be then. What are you trusting the long game with? What do you commit to showing up for consistently, even without immediate feedback? What do you want your future self to know you chose today? Share: one thing you are playing the long game with.', 'Write your long-game direction — not goals, but the quality of person and life you are building toward over years.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Today, show up for one long-game practice — not because you can see results, but as a deliberate vote for who you''re becoming.', 'Tell one person what long game you''re playing. Ask them what theirs is.', 'Bring back: what happened when you showed up for your long game practice without expecting immediate results?', '', '', 'I am building something that takes time. I show up consistently. The direction is right.', 'Angela Duckworth''s talk is genuinely short and worth showing in the session if possible. The three-year letter exercise is emotionally powerful — encourage teens to actually seal and keep it. The compound interest framing (1% better every day) resonates strongly with this age group.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Here is one of the simplest and most powerful practices available to you: leave people slightly better than you found them. Not dramatically — not fixing or saving anyone. Just: they feel slightly more seen, more valued, more capable of being themselves after being with you. That is one of the most significant things a person can do.', 'Think of someone who consistently left you better — who made you feel more seen and more capable. What specifically did they do? Was it dramatic — or was it small and consistent?', 'Here is one of the simplest and most powerful practices available to you: leave people slightly better than you found them. Not dramatically — not fixing or saving anyone. Just: they feel slightly more seen, more valued, more capable of being themselves after being with you. That is one of the most significant things a person can do.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cDDWvj_q-o8', 'YouTube: Search ''the power of being seen relationships research'' or ''micro-affirmations leaving people better YouTube'' for accessible content. Runtime ~8–10 min.', '', '', '', 'Who left you better than they found you?', 'LEAVING BETTER AUDIT: Think of the five people you interact with most. After typical encounters with you, do they leave feeling more or less like themselves? More or less seen? What one specific change would make you more reliably leave them better — a quality of attention, an honest word, showing up differently? Design one leaving-better practice for your most important relationship. Share: one specific thing you will do to leave someone better this week.', 'Write the one question you want to carry: ''Will this person be slightly better for having encountered me?'' Write how you will practise answering yes.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'In one interaction today, orient entirely toward leaving the other person better. Notice what changes — in them and in you.', 'Give one person your full, undivided attention for ten minutes. No agenda. Just genuine reception.', 'Bring back: what happened when you deliberately left someone better?', '', '', 'Every encounter is an opportunity to leave someone slightly more themselves. I take it.', 'This session should feel both inspiring and immediately actionable. Build in the ten-minute undivided attention practice as a committed exercise for the week — not optional. The ''will they be slightly better'' question is genuinely transformative when carried daily.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Legacy sounds like something old people think about. It isn''t. Legacy is what you''re building right now — through how you treat people, what you model, what you stand for, what you create. At 16 or 17 or 18, you are already leaving something in the world. Today we think about what that is — and whether it''s what you''d choose.', 'What do your closest friends and family members most reliably experience when they''re around you? What do you add to a room — and what do you take from it? Be honest.', 'Legacy sounds like something old people think about. It isn''t. Legacy is what you''re building right now — through how you treat people, what you model, what you stand for, what you create. At 16 or 17 or 18, you are already leaving something in the world. Today we think about what that is — and whether it''s what you''d choose.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qp0HIF3SfI4', 'YouTube: Search ''legacy consciousness teen purpose research'' or ''what is legacy young people'' for accessible content. Also: search ''how teens influence others role modelling research.'' Runtime ~10 min.', '', '', '', 'What do you want to be true because you were here?', 'LEGACY AUDIT: Write honestly: What are you currently adding to the lives of the people closest to you? What are you modelling — in how you treat conflict, how you handle difficulty, how you treat people who are different from you, how you pursue what matters? Is that what you''d choose to model? What would you change? Design your current legacy intention — not a grand plan, but a specific quality of presence you want to be known for. Share: what you want to be building right now.', 'Write: ''The legacy I am building right now is...'' — not what you hope for eventually, but what you are actively creating through how you currently live.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Make one choice today that is explicitly oriented toward the legacy you want to build.', 'Tell one person what you want to be building — and ask them to notice when you''re doing it.', 'Bring back: what happened when you oriented toward legacy in an ordinary moment?', '', '', 'I am building something beyond myself — right now, in how I live. That is my legacy in progress.', 'The reframe from future-legacy to present-legacy is powerful for teens who find the concept abstract. The question ''what is someone who looks up to you learning from how you live right now?'' tends to land immediately and specifically.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Gratitude is not a feeling you get when good things happen. It is a deliberate practice — choosing to notice and name what is already present and valuable, even when things aren''t perfect. And the research on what it does to your brain and your life is extraordinary. This week we make it a daily practice.', 'When was the last time you felt genuine gratitude — not performed, not obligatory, but actually felt? What specifically were you grateful for? And how often do you actually practise noticing that?', 'Gratitude is not a feeling you get when good things happen. It is a deliberate practice — choosing to notice and name what is already present and valuable, even when things aren''t perfect. And the research on what it does to your brain and your life is extraordinary. This week we make it a daily practice.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WPPPFqsECz0', 'YouTube: Robert Emmons on gratitude research — search ''Robert Emmons gratitude research talk.'' Also: search ''gratitude and brain health teen research'' for age-specific content. Runtime ~10–15 min.', '', '', '', 'What''s good right now that you''d stopped noticing?', 'GRATITUDE PRACTICE DESIGN: Design a genuine daily gratitude practice — specific format, specific time, specific level of depth. This week: three things each day, but each one specific enough that it couldn''t have been written yesterday (what happened today that you''re grateful for, exactly why, and what it actually felt like). Share: one specific example of your practice — not ''my family'' but the specific moment.', 'Write your gratitude practice design. Commit to practising it every day for the rest of the year.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Practise daily specific gratitude every day this week. Don''t miss a day. Notice what compounds.', 'Express specific gratitude to one person every day this week — tell them exactly what you appreciate and why.', 'Bring back: what happened when you practised specific gratitude consistently? What compounded?', '', '', 'Gratitude is my daily practice. Specific, felt, genuine. I train my attention on what is real and good.', 'The specificity principle is the most important practical point of this session — spend time on it. The daily practice without missing a day is a deliberate challenge — the research shows that consistency matters more than depth. Expressed gratitude (telling someone specifically) is the highest-impact exercise.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Here''s a truth that sounds discouraging at first but becomes liberating: you''re never going to be ''finished.'' There''s no point where you''ll have it all together, have figured everything out, or be done growing. And that''s actually the best news there is — because it means the journey is the point, not the destination.', 'What has shifted in how you think about personal growth over the course of this year? Do you still think of it as something you finish — or has your relationship with the ongoing nature of it changed?', 'Here''s a truth that sounds discouraging at first but becomes liberating: you''re never going to be ''finished.'' There''s no point where you''ll have it all together, have figured everything out, or be done growing. And that''s actually the best news there is — because it means the journey is the point, not the destination.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sPOuCd6cBao', 'YouTube: ''This Is Water'' by David Foster Wallace — the most important short piece of content of the year. Runtime ~9 min.', '', '', '', 'What will you keep doing after this year?', 'PRACTICE OWNERSHIP: In your journal, from each phase of the year: What do you want to keep practising from Phase 1 (seeing)? What is still releasing from Phase 2 (unlearning)? What do you want to build more of from Phase 3 (rebuilding)? What orientations from Phase 4 (living) do you want to carry forward? Design your post-Mindcast LIVE ongoing practice — the simplest sustainable version of this year''s work that you can maintain as simply yours. Share: your ongoing practice design.', 'Write your ongoing practice — the sustainable version of this year''s work that you will maintain because it is genuinely yours.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Own one practice this week — do it not as part of the programme, but as yours. No external structure. Just you and the practice.', 'Tell one person that you''re not trying to finish the journey — you''re choosing to live it. Share what that looks like for you.', 'Bring back: what did it feel like to own the practice as genuinely yours?', '', '', 'I am not finishing. I am continuing. The practice is the point — and it is mine.', 'This session needs to be held carefully — there may be both relief and grief at the idea that the structured year is ending. The gift of this session is the reframe: you''re not losing the structure, you''re owning the practice. The ongoing practice design is the most important output.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Fifty-two weeks. A whole year. You''ve seen yourself clearly, released what wasn''t yours, built something real, and started living it outward. Today we don''t call that finished. We call it the beginning of the rest of a life lived from the inside out. And we acknowledge, together, what was actually done.', 'If you had to name the one thing — just one — that has most genuinely changed in you over this year, what would it be? Not the most dramatic. The most real.', 'Fifty-two weeks. A whole year. You''ve seen yourself clearly, released what wasn''t yours, built something real, and started living it outward. Today we don''t call that finished. We call it the beginning of the rest of a life lived from the inside out. And we acknowledge, together, what was actually done.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sPOuCd6cBao', 'YouTube: ''This Is Water'' by David Foster Wallace animated — the final and most important piece of content of the year. Runtime ~9 min.', '', '', '', 'Who were you a year ago, and what would you tell them?', 'YEAR CEREMONY: Write answers to four questions. Take time. Be honest. 1. Who was I at Week 1? 2. What has genuinely shifted this year? 3. What am I carrying forward that I didn''t have before? 4. What is my commitment for the ongoing practice? Then in the group: each person shares one line from any of their four answers. Witnessed in silence. No advice. No commentary. Just witnessed. That witnessing is the ceremony.', 'Write a letter to Week 1 you. What do you want them to know?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Live one day this week with full intentionality from everything this year has built. Notice what that life feels like.', 'Tell one person outside this group: ''I''ve done a year of real inner work. One thing that genuinely changed is...'' Own it completely.', 'Come back ready to share one line from your year ceremony — if you''re willing.', '', '', 'I did this work. I carry it forward. The practice is mine now. The adventure continues.', 'MAKE THIS EXTRAORDINARY. Ceremony matters. The year''s arc. The community formed. The genuine work done. Honour all of it: candles, music, letters, witnessed silence. End not with ''goodbye'' but with the shared commitment to ongoing practice. This is the most important session of the year.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Sometimes our thoughts and feelings get really noisy — like a radio with too much static. Today we practise noticing when we feel like ourselves versus when we feel a bit lost or scrambled.', 'Can anyone tell me about a time they felt really, really good — like everything just felt right? What were you doing?', 'Sometimes our thoughts and feelings get really noisy — like a radio with too much static. Today we practise noticing when we feel like ourselves versus when we feel a bit lost or scrambled.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UOsxlVpQT14', 'Listening to My Body by Gabi Garcia (read-aloud) — sensations and feelings, and how to listen to what your body needs. Runtime ~10 min.', '', '', '', 'What''s something you''ve been thinking about that you haven''t told anyone?', 'BODY DETECTIVE: Rub your hands together fast for 30 seconds. What do you notice — heat? Tingles? Sweat? That''s a sensation. Now put your hand on your heart and jump 15 times. What changed? Your body talks through sensations and feelings. Now draw, or tell a partner, one thing your body is telling you right now.', 'Draw a picture of your body when it feels happy and calm — and a picture of your body when it''s telling you it needs something. What''s different?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Be a body detective today. Notice one sensation — hungry, wiggly, warm, tired — and tell a grown-up what you found.', 'When a big feeling comes, try horse lips: breathe in through your nose, then blow a big puff out through your lips so they flap like a horse. What happens to the feeling?', 'Give yourself a butterfly hug — wrap your arms around yourself and squeeze gently, just the way you like it. Tell a grown-up what your body said back.', '', '', 'My body talks to me, and I''m learning to listen. I know the difference between a calm body and a wiggly one.', 'Use visuals and movement where possible. Keep reflection time SHORT — 30 seconds max for young children. Story time recommended: ask children to bring a book about feelings for next week.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

We all have little voices in our head that say things about us — sometimes kind things, sometimes not-so-kind things. Today we meet those voices and find out where they came from.', 'Has anyone ever had a thought like ''I''m not good at that'' or ''that''s not for me'' — and wondered where it came from?', 'We all have little voices in our head that say things about us — sometimes kind things, sometimes not-so-kind things. Today we meet those voices and find out where they came from.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pTp0O-b0LFI', 'YouTube: ''The Most Magnificent Thing'' read-aloud — story about a girl who tries and fails and learns to persist. Runtime ~8 min. Companion book: ''What Do You Do With a Problem?'' by Kobi Yamada.', '', '', '', 'What do people say you''re like? Is that the whole story?', 'BACKPACK ACTIVITY: Each child gets a paper ''backpack'' outline to draw on. Inside the backpack, draw or write 2 things you believe about yourself — one good thing, one thing that sometimes makes you feel bad. Around the outside of the backpack, write where you learned it (e.g. ''school,'' ''a friend said,'' ''something that happened''). Share the good thing with the group. The harder thing is private unless they choose to share.', 'Draw a picture of yourself WITHOUT the heavy thing in your backpack. What do you look like?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Notice one kind thought about yourself today. Write it down or tell someone.', 'Tell a grown-up one thing in your ''backpack'' — something you believe about yourself, good or tricky.', 'Bring your backpack drawing back and be ready to share one thing from it.', '', '', 'I get to choose which stories I carry.', 'Use physical props if possible — a real small backpack to put cards in works wonderfully. Ensure children know they don''t have to share private thoughts. Have a quiet corner available.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Sometimes we do things we didn''t really mean to — like snap at someone or say something unkind — almost before we even knew we were doing it. Today we learn a superpower: the pause.', 'Has anyone ever said or done something, and then straight away wished they hadn''t? Tell me about what that feels like in your body — tummy? chest? face?', 'Sometimes we do things we didn''t really mean to — like snap at someone or say something unkind — almost before we even knew we were doing it. Today we learn a superpower: the pause.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BVAaomgzFCM', 'YouTube: ''Sesame Street — Common and Colbie Caillat: Belly Breathe'' — fun, accessible breathing and pause technique for young children. Runtime ~3 min. Companion book: ''When Sophie Gets Angry — Really, Really Angry'' by Molly Bang.', '', '', '', 'When did you last do something you wished you hadn''t?', 'THE PAUSE BUTTON ACTIVITY: Everyone gets a card with a big PAUSE symbol on it. Practise the pause together: Clap hands once (the trigger). Everyone presses their ''pause button'' card against their heart and counts 1-2-3 slowly while breathing. Role play: Facilitator pretends to say something frustrating. Children press pause, count, breathe, then decide how to respond. Practise 3 times. Make it fun and slightly silly.', 'Draw your pause button. What colour is it? What does it look like? Where on your body would it be?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'When you feel a big, fast feeling today, try pressing your imaginary pause button before you react.', 'Teach someone at home about the pause button. Show them how it works.', 'Bring your pause button drawing and a story about one time you tried to use it!', '', '', 'When I feel a big feeling, I can pause. I am in charge of what happens next.', 'The pause button card is a tangible anchor children can take home. Coordinate with parents to reinforce the language at home. Make the role-play fun so children associate it with positive feelings.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Our bodies are amazing messengers! They tell us when we''re scared, excited, tired, or happy — all with feelings inside our body. Today we learn to listen to those feelings.', 'Can you show me what your body looks like when you''re really happy? Now scared. Now proud. Did you notice your BODY changes when your feelings change? Feelings live in the body!', 'Our bodies are amazing messengers! They tell us when we''re scared, excited, tired, or happy — all with feelings inside our body. Today we learn to listen to those feelings.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nj2ofrX7jAk', 'YouTube: ''Emotions and the Brain for Kids'' — fun animated explanation of how emotions work in the body. Runtime ~5 min. Companion book: ''The Colour Monster'' by Anna Llenas — beautiful exploration of identifying feelings through colour.', '', '', '', 'Where do you feel it in your body when you''re worried?', 'FEELINGS WEATHER STATION: Each child gets a body outline. Facilitator calls out feelings: happy, scared, excited, tired, proud, embarrassed, angry, loved. Children colour or mark where they feel each one in their body. Share: ''Where do YOU feel happy? Where do you feel nervous?'' Discuss: we all feel things in slightly different places — and that''s amazing!', 'Draw what your body looks like on the inside when you feel your favourite feeling.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Three times today, ask yourself: ''What is my body telling me right now?'' Tell a friend what you find!', 'Ask a grown-up: ''Where do YOU feel nervous in your body?'' Compare answers!', 'Bring back your feelings body map and share one new thing you discovered about your feelings.', '', '', 'My body helps me understand my feelings. We are a great team.', 'Body map activity is highly engaging — use lots of colour. Keep the focus entirely on internal feelings, never on appearance. The ''feelings weather station'' language can be used throughout the whole year as a check-in tool.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Have you ever looked in a funny mirror that made you look tall or wiggly or squished? Today we think about the mirror we use to look at ourselves — and make sure it''s a good, true one.', 'If I drew a picture of you, what would I need to include to make it REALLY you? Not just what you look like — what makes you YOU?', 'Have you ever looked in a funny mirror that made you look tall or wiggly or squished? Today we think about the mirror we use to look at ourselves — and make sure it''s a good, true one.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0ZcfX2862XE', 'YouTube: ''The Dot'' read-aloud by Peter H. Reynolds — a child discovers their own creativity and ability through brave action. Runtime ~8 min. Companion book: ''I Am Enough'' by Grace Byers — affirming picture book about being exactly who you are.', '', '', '', 'What''s something you like about yourself?', 'THE TRUE MIRROR ACTIVITY: Each child draws a large mirror outline. On the LEFT side: draw or write 3 things you''re genuinely good at or proud of. On the RIGHT side: draw or write 1 thing you''re still learning or working on — this is brave! Decorate the frame with things that matter to you. Share your mirror with the group — at least one thing from each side.', 'Draw or write about something you''re proud of about yourself that you don''t talk about very much.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Tell yourself one true kind thing today. Then tell someone else one true kind thing about THEM.', 'Ask a grown-up: ''What do you think I''m really good at?'' Write it on the frame of your mirror.', 'Bring your mirror drawing back and add something new you discovered about yourself this week!', '', '', 'I can see myself clearly — the strong parts AND the growing parts. Both of them are me.', 'The mirror craft is a session highlight — prepare materials in advance. Emphasise that BOTH strengths AND growing areas belong in the mirror — this normalises ongoing growth. Display mirrors on the room walls with permission — creates a powerful visual of collective self-awareness.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Sometimes we look at other people and wish we were more like them — that we had what they had or could do what they can do. Today we learn why comparing isn''t as useful as it feels, and what to do instead.', 'Has anyone ever wished they could do something that someone else can do? What does it feel like in your tummy when you compare yourself to someone else?', 'Sometimes we look at other people and wish we were more like them — that we had what they had or could do what they can do. Today we learn why comparing isn''t as useful as it feels, and what to do instead.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kMyk8xSMnzY', 'YouTube: ''You Are Special'' by Max Lucado read-aloud — a beautiful story about where worth really comes from. Runtime ~8–10 min.', '', '', '', 'Who do you wish you were more like, and why?', 'YOUR AMAZING PUZZLE: Each child gets a puzzle outline with 4–6 large pieces. In each piece, draw or write one thing you''re good at, one thing you love, one thing that makes you you. Look at your completed puzzle: no two are the same! That''s the point. Share: ''One piece of my puzzle that''s completely unique to me is...''', 'Draw or write about something you''ve gotten better at this year. How did it make you feel to notice that?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Each time you catch yourself wishing you were more like someone else, ask: ''I wonder what I''m good at that they might not be?''', 'Tell a grown-up one thing you''ve gotten better at this year that you''re really proud of.', 'Bring your puzzle back and add one new piece — something new you noticed about what makes you, you!', '', '', 'I am my own kind of amazing. My puzzle is exactly right for me.', 'The puzzle activity is very popular with this age group — make the puzzle pieces large enough for drawing. Celebrate the uniqueness of every puzzle loudly and genuinely. Avoid any competitive element in sharing.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Sometimes we have a mean little voice in our head that says unkind things about us — like ''you can''t do that'' or ''you''re not good enough.'' Today we find out that this voice isn''t telling the truth — and we learn to find the kinder, truer voice.', 'Has anyone ever had a thought like ''I can''t do this'' right before trying something hard? Where do you think that thought comes from?', 'Sometimes we have a mean little voice in our head that says unkind things about us — like ''you can''t do that'' or ''you''re not good enough.'' Today we find out that this voice isn''t telling the truth — and we learn to find the kinder, truer voice.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0ZcfX2862XE', 'YouTube: ''Beautiful Oops'' read-aloud — story about characters with inner critics learning to change perspective. Runtime ~8 min. Companion book: ''Wemberly Worried'' by Kevin Henkes — a mouse who worries about everything and learns she is more than her worries.', '', '', '', 'What does the mean voice in your head say to you?', 'MEET THE GREMLIN: Everyone draws their ''inner critic gremlin'' — what does yours look like? Name it (e.g. Doubty, Grumpy Gus, The Worrier). Now write or draw one thing your gremlin says a lot. Now draw or write what your ''inner friend voice'' says instead — the kindest, most honest thing. Share your gremlin''s name with the group — the sillier the better!', 'Draw a comic strip: Panel 1 — the gremlin speaks. Panel 2 — you notice it. Panel 3 — you choose the kind voice instead.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Every time you hear your gremlin today, give it a name and then listen for the kinder voice.', 'Tell a grown-up about your gremlin and give it a name. Ask them if they have one too!', 'Bring your gremlin drawing and your ''kind voice'' back to share with the group!', '', '', 'I have a grumpy gremlin AND a kind friend inside me. I choose to listen to the friend.', 'Children LOVE naming their gremlin — the sillier the name the better, as it immediately reduces the power of the voice. Display gremlin drawings on the wall throughout Phase 1. Remind children the gremlin is not bad or wrong to have — it''s just not the boss.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Feelings are like messages your heart sends you. Sometimes the messages are easy to understand — ''I''m happy!'' or ''I''m sad.'' But sometimes feelings are tricky and hidden, like treasure buried under sand. Today we learn to dig and find what''s really there.', 'Has anyone ever been in a bad mood and not quite known WHY? Or been really angry but not sure what you were actually upset about? That''s the feelings iceberg! Today we dig under the surface.', 'Feelings are like messages your heart sends you. Sometimes the messages are easy to understand — ''I''m happy!'' or ''I''m sad.'' But sometimes feelings are tricky and hidden, like treasure buried under sand. Today we learn to dig and find what''s really there.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=d3N7Kgb3JtE', 'YouTube: ''Inside Out emotions explained for kids'' — short clips from Pixar''s Inside Out explaining how different emotions work together. Runtime ~3–5 min for clips. Companion book: ''The Feelings Book'' by Todd Parr — bright, simple, inclusive celebration of the full range of feelings.', '', '', '', 'What were you feeling just before you got cross?', 'THE FEELINGS ICEBERG: Everyone gets an iceberg drawing — a triangle shape with half above the ''water line'' and half below. Above the water: draw or write the feeling everyone can see when you''re upset (e.g. angry, grumpy, quiet). Below the water: draw or write what might really be there underneath (e.g. scared, lonely, tired, embarrassed). Facilitator shares an example first. Share: ''Above my waterline, people might see...''', 'Draw your feelings iceberg for today. What''s above the water? What might be underneath?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'When you feel a big feeling today, whisper to yourself: ''I wonder what''s really going on underneath?''', 'Show a grown-up your iceberg drawing and explain it to them. Ask them to draw their iceberg too!', 'Bring a new iceberg drawing showing a feeling you had this week. What did you find underneath?', '', '', 'When I look underneath my feelings, I find the real message. And I am brave enough to look.', 'The iceberg is brilliantly visual for this age. Make it physical — large printed icebergs with a clear water line. The ''Inside Out'' reference will resonate strongly with this generation. Reassure children that the below-water part is for them — they don''t have to share.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Sometimes things happen that make us feel sad, scared, or hurt — and even when those things are over, we might still feel them inside. Today we talk about those feelings in a gentle, safe way, and remember that carrying something hard doesn''t mean we''re stuck with it forever.', 'Has anyone ever had a bad day, or a bad thing happen, and it kept making you feel yucky even after it was over? That''s completely normal. Today we talk about that.', 'Sometimes things happen that make us feel sad, scared, or hurt — and even when those things are over, we might still feel them inside. Today we talk about those feelings in a gentle, safe way, and remember that carrying something hard doesn''t mean we''re stuck with it forever.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7H2pBdLnmGs', 'YouTube: ''The Invisible String'' read-aloud — a beautiful story about connection that remains even through difficult times. Runtime ~8 min. Companion book: ''A Little Spot of Sadness'' by Diane Alber — child-friendly approach to grief and loss.', '', '', '', 'What''s something that made you sad that you''ve never said out loud?', 'THE STONE ACTIVITY: Everyone gets a smooth stone (or draws a stone on paper). On one side: draw or write something hard that happened — something you''re still carrying a little bit. Facilitator shares their own gentle example first. On the other side: draw or write one person, place, or thing that helps you feel better when things are hard. Share the ''helper'' side with the group. ''This stone represents your hard thing AND your helper. You carry both.''', 'Draw or write about a grown-up or friend you would go to if you were carrying something heavy. What makes them safe to talk to?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'If your stone feels heavy today, talk to a grown-up you trust about what''s making it heavy.', 'Show a grown-up your stone drawing and explain what the two sides mean.', 'Bring your stone (or stone drawing) back. Has anything gotten easier to carry since last week?', '', '', 'Hard things happen. But I don''t carry them alone — and they don''t get to be the whole story.', 'CRITICAL: Most emotionally sensitive children''s session. Do NOT ask children to share what is in their ''stone'' unless they choose to. Have a quiet space available. Coordinate with parents/caregivers before this session and provide a resource sheet for families. Have the children''s programme lead available if any disclosures are made.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Sometimes we act differently around different people — maybe you''re super silly with your best friend but quieter at school. Sometimes that''s fine! But sometimes we hide the real us because we''re worried people won''t like us. Today we talk about feeling safe enough to be yourself.', 'Let''s play a game! Can you show me your ''at school'' face? Your ''at home'' face? Your ''playing with best friends'' face? Your ''feeling shy'' face? Now — can you show me your REAL face? What makes that one different?', 'Sometimes we act differently around different people — maybe you''re super silly with your best friend but quieter at school. Sometimes that''s fine! But sometimes we hide the real us because we''re worried people won''t like us. Today we talk about feeling safe enough to be yourself.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YRaVl-VjF2g', 'YouTube: ''The Name Jar'' read-aloud — story about a child who hides their real name and finds the courage to claim it. Runtime ~8 min. Companion book: ''Stand Tall, Molly Lou Melon'' by Patty Lovell — a small girl who is completely herself despite pressure to change.', '', '', '', 'When do you pretend you''re fine?', 'MASK MAKING ACTIVITY: Each child gets a paper mask template to colour and decorate as a ''pretend face'' they sometimes wear (e.g. ''the brave face,'' ''the happy face when I''m not happy,'' ''the cool face''). On the BACK of the mask, they write or draw their real feelings or qualities. Share: ''My pretend face looks like... but on the back, I''m really...''', 'Draw two faces: your pretend face for one situation, and your real face underneath. What''s the same? What''s different?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Notice once today when you''re wearing a pretend face. You don''t have to change it — just notice it''s there.', 'Show a grown-up your mask craft. Tell them about one pretend face you wear and one time you felt safe to be your real self.', 'Bring your mask back! Has anything been different this week about showing your real face?', '', '', 'My real face is the best face. The right people will always want to see it.', 'The mask craft is one of the most enjoyable physical activities of Phase 1 — have good craft supplies available. The two-sided mask (performance on front, real self on back) is a powerful metaphor children can take home. Coordinate with families — the mask can prompt great conversations at home.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Sometimes we think we know exactly why someone did something — but we might be wrong! Today we practise the superpower of seeing things from other people''s point of view, which is one of the kindest and most useful things you can learn to do.', 'Let''s try something: (Facilitator holds up a duck/rabbit optical illusion.) What do you see? Does anyone see something different? Both are right! That''s what today is about.', 'Sometimes we think we know exactly why someone did something — but we might be wrong! Today we practise the superpower of seeing things from other people''s point of view, which is one of the kindest and most useful things you can learn to do.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9_1Rt1R4xbM', 'YouTube: ''We''re All Wonders'' read-aloud by R.J. Palacio — companion to ''Wonder,'' the gold standard for teaching children empathy. Runtime ~5 min. Full book ''Wonder'' also highly recommended.', '', '', '', 'Think of someone who was unkind. What might be going on for them?', 'THE PERSPECTIVE DETECTIVE: Facilitator presents three short scenarios (e.g. ''Tom took Maya''s pencil without asking. Maya is upset. But Tom forgot his pencils today and has a big test.''). For each: how might each person be feeling? What might each person be thinking? Is there a kind way to understand both sides? Then: think of a real situation where someone did something that confused or upset you. What might THEIR side of the story be?', 'Draw a picture of a time something seemed unfair. Then draw what it might have looked like from the other person''s point of view.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Once today when someone does something confusing, ask yourself: ''I wonder what''s going on for THEM right now?''', 'Tell a grown-up about a time you tried to see things from someone else''s point of view this week.', 'Bring back a story about a time you tried to be a ''perspective detective'' this week!', '', '', 'I can try to see how things look from where someone else is standing. That''s how I grow kinder.', 'Use physical props — perspective illusions work brilliantly for this age. The duck/rabbit or young woman/old woman illusion is classic and always provokes delight. The perspective detective game should be kept fun and curious, not moralistic.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

A habit is something we do so often that we start doing it without even thinking! Some habits are really good — like brushing teeth. Some habits might not help us as much. Today we look at habits and figure out how they work.', 'Let''s make a list together: what are some habits that HELP us? (Brushing teeth, saying please, getting enough sleep.) What are some habits that might NOT help as much? Which ones did you decide? Which ones just... happened?', 'A habit is something we do so often that we start doing it without even thinking! Some habits are really good — like brushing teeth. Some habits might not help us as much. Today we look at habits and figure out how they work.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hpnI3MCTJSA', 'YouTube: ''The Power of Yet'' — Carol Dweck animated for kids, about the habit of giving up vs. the habit of persisting. Runtime ~5 min. Companion book: ''The Bad Seed'' by Jory John — hilarious story about a seed who always did things one way and decides to change.', '', '', '', 'What do you always do when you''re upset?', 'THE HABIT DETECTIVE GAME: Facilitator walks through the habit loop using a fun example (e.g. ''Whenever I see the biscuit tin — TRIGGER — I open it and take one — ACTION — and it tastes yummy — REWARD''). Children brainstorm their own habits — good and less helpful. For each habit: what''s the TRIGGER? What''s the ACTION? What''s the REWARD? Then: ''Could we change the ACTION while keeping the same REWARD? What could we do instead?''', 'Draw your habit loop: trigger → action → reward. Then draw what a NEW action could look like that still gets the same reward!', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Today, catch one habit as it''s about to happen. You don''t have to change it — just notice the trigger and say ''ah, there it is!''', 'Tell a grown-up about one habit you noticed this week. What was the trigger? What was the reward?', 'Bring back your habit loop drawing AND a story about one habit you noticed!', '', '', 'I notice my habits. Noticing them means I can choose what I want to do next.', 'The three-part habit loop is perfectly age-appropriate for primary school children. Use physical role-play for the habit detective game — act it out with the whole group. Send a ''habit detective worksheet'' home for family engagement.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

We''ve been on a big adventure together for 13 weeks — looking at feelings, habits, patterns, and all sorts of things about ourselves. Today we celebrate how brave we''ve been, and get ready for the next exciting part of the journey.', 'Let''s go on a memory adventure! What are all the things we''ve learned about ourselves over the past 13 weeks? (Let children call out — signals and noise, the pause button, the gremlin, habit detective, feelings iceberg, perspective detective...)', 'We''ve been on a big adventure together for 13 weeks — looking at feelings, habits, patterns, and all sorts of things about ourselves. Today we celebrate how brave we''ve been, and get ready for the next exciting part of the journey.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VWOgrMXBE4U', 'YouTube: Search ''growth mindset celebration kids'' for an affirming short animation to celebrate learning and bravery. Runtime ~3–5 min. Companion book: ''Last Stop on Market Street'' by Matt de la Pena — about seeing what you have and where you''re going.', '', '', '', 'What have you found out about yourself this term?', 'BACKPACK CELEBRATION: Each child gets a backpack outline and draws all the ''tools'' they''ve collected over 13 weeks. Decorate the backpack with favourite colours, patterns, anything that feels like ''them.'' Circle time: each child shares ONE favourite tool from the journey so far. Celebrate each share genuinely and specifically.', 'Draw what your ''inner self'' looks like now compared to Week 1. What has changed? What has stayed the same?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Share your backpack with someone at home — tell them about every tool in it!', 'Show a grown-up your Phase 1 drawings and tell them your favourite thing you learned about yourself.', 'Come to the next session ready to show your backpack and share your FAVOURITE thing from Phase 1!', '', '', 'I have new tools. I am braver than I was. And the adventure is just beginning.', 'Make this session genuinely celebratory — balloons, music, certificates if you have them. Children deserve to have their work honoured. Put all backpack drawings up around the room together — creates genuine community pride. Phase 2 transition should feel exciting and earned.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Sometimes we don''t try things because we''re waiting for someone to say it''s okay. But some of the best, most YOU things you could do — you already have permission for. Today we find out what you''ve been waiting to try.', 'Has anyone ever had an idea or wanted to try something new — but didn''t, because they weren''t sure if they were allowed? What was it?', 'Sometimes we don''t try things because we''re waiting for someone to say it''s okay. But some of the best, most YOU things you could do — you already have permission for. Today we find out what you''ve been waiting to try.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H14bBuluwB8', 'YouTube: ''What Do You Do With an Idea?'' read-aloud by Kobi Yamada — a child learns to trust and act on their own idea despite uncertainty. Runtime ~8 min.', '', '', '', 'What are you waiting for someone to say yes to?', 'THE GO BUTTON GAME: Facilitator presents scenarios: ''You have an idea for a story. Do you need permission to write it? GO or WAIT?'' / ''You want to try a new sport. WAIT — ask a grown-up.'' / ''You want to be kinder to someone who isn''t your friend. GO?'' Play through 6–8 scenarios, getting children to identify which decisions are theirs and which need adult input. Then: ''What''s one thing YOU have been waiting to try that you actually have permission for right now?''', 'Draw your GO button. What does it look like? What would you press it to do first?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Try one small thing today that you''ve been waiting to try. It doesn''t have to be big — just something that''s yours to try.', 'Tell a grown-up about your GO button. Ask them: ''What''s something you wish you''d given yourself permission to try sooner?''', 'Come back with a story about one thing you pressed your GO button on this week!', '', '', 'I have permission to try, to create, to be curious. That permission lives inside me.', 'The GO/WAIT game is highly engaging and teaches important discernment — not all things are children''s decisions, and that''s appropriate to name. Celebrate any share about something they pressed GO on. Keep it playful and empowering.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Sometimes grown-ups and other people have ideas about what we should be when we grow up, or how we should act, or what we should like. Those ideas come from love — but sometimes they''re not exactly right for us. Today we explore what WE actually love and who WE actually are.', 'What do you love doing that feels most like YOU — not because someone told you to love it, but because you just do?', 'Sometimes grown-ups and other people have ideas about what we should be when we grow up, or how we should act, or what we should like. Those ideas come from love — but sometimes they''re not exactly right for us. Today we explore what WE actually love and who WE actually are.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H14bBuluwB8', 'YouTube: ''What Do You Do With an Idea?'' read-aloud by Kobi Yamada — about nurturing the things that belong most deeply to you. Runtime ~8 min. Companion book: ''The Dot'' by Peter Reynolds — about the courage to make your own mark.', '', '', '', 'Who are you trying to make happy?', 'MY OWN PICTURE: Each child gets a blank piece of paper (not a colouring-in page — a completely blank one). ''Draw or write things that feel most like you — what you love, what you''re curious about, what you dream about, what makes you feel most alive.'' No templates. No outlines. Completely theirs. Share: ''One thing in my picture that might surprise people who think they know me.''', 'Write or draw about something you love that feels completely, uniquely yours — maybe something not everyone understands.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Today, do one thing just because YOU love it — not because anyone told you to.', 'Show a grown-up your ''My Own Picture'' drawing. Tell them one thing about yourself they might not know.', 'Bring your ''My Own Picture'' back and add something new you discovered about yourself this week!', '', '', 'Who I am is already here. I get to discover it — and it belongs to me.', 'The blank page exercise is deliberately unstructured — resist the urge to add prompts or templates. The blankness is the point. Celebrate every drawing as completely valid. This session plants a seed about intrinsic identity that will deepen throughout the year.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Sometimes people hurt our feelings or do things that aren''t fair — and it can be really hard to stop feeling angry or sad about it. Today we talk about something called forgiveness — what it really means, and how it can help US feel better.', 'Has anyone ever felt really angry or sad about something someone did — and kept thinking about it even when you didn''t want to? What does that feel like?', 'Sometimes people hurt our feelings or do things that aren''t fair — and it can be really hard to stop feeling angry or sad about it. Today we talk about something called forgiveness — what it really means, and how it can help US feel better.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7H2pBdLnmGs', 'YouTube: ''Each Kindness'' by Jacqueline Woodson read-aloud — about the weight of things left unresolved and the power of choosing differently. Runtime ~8 min. Companion book: ''Enemy Pie'' by Derek Munson — about releasing a grievance and discovering friendship.', '', '', '', 'Who are you still cross with?', 'THE HOT ROCK ACTIVITY: Each child gets a smooth stone. On it they write (or the facilitator helps write) something that happened that hurt them — a time someone was unkind. Then: hold the stone tight in your fist. Feel how heavy it is. How it doesn''t feel nice to keep squeezing it. Now slowly open your hand and just... rest it there. You''re not throwing it away. You''re just stopping squeezing. Discuss: what''s the difference between holding tight and just resting it in your open hand?', 'Draw a picture of you holding the hot rock. Then draw a picture of you with your hand open, the rock resting in it. What''s different about your face?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'When you think about something that hurt you today, try opening your fist instead of squeezing it tighter.', 'Tell a trusted grown-up about something you''re still feeling hurt about. Ask them to help you think about it.', 'Bring back: did you try opening your hand this week? What happened?', '', '', 'I can put down heavy things. Letting go is one of the bravest things I can do.', 'The hot rock exercise is highly physical and effective for this age. Ensure children understand clearly: forgiveness is not saying the hurt was okay, and it doesn''t mean having to be friends with the person. Have a check-in with parents after this session if any significant hurts are disclosed.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Sometimes we do things we feel really bad about — maybe we said something unkind or made a mistake that hurt someone. It''s good to feel sorry. But today we learn that after we''ve said sorry and tried to make it right, we don''t need to keep feeling bad forever.', 'Has anyone ever done something by accident or on purpose that they felt really bad about? What did it feel like? Did you say sorry? And did you feel better afterwards — or did the bad feeling stay for a long time?', 'Sometimes we do things we feel really bad about — maybe we said something unkind or made a mistake that hurt someone. It''s good to feel sorry. But today we learn that after we''ve said sorry and tried to make it right, we don''t need to keep feeling bad forever.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nDPHBzWBFBg', 'YouTube: ''The Invisible String'' or search ''sorry steps for kids animated'' — various short animations on apology and self-forgiveness for young children. Runtime ~5 min. Companion book: ''Sorry!'' by Trudy Ludwig — a story about what a real apology looks and feels like.', '', '', '', 'What did you get wrong that you''re still cross with yourself about?', 'THE SORRY STEPS: Teach the four steps on a poster or card: 1. SAY WHAT HAPPENED (no excuses). 2. SAY SORRY and mean it. 3. MAKE IT RIGHT if you can (what can you do?). 4. LEARN and do better next time. Role-play scenarios together. Then: think of something you still feel bad about. Have you done all four steps? If yes — you have permission to let the bad feeling go. If not — which step is still needed?', 'Draw the four sorry steps as a little comic strip. When would you use them?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'If you still feel bad about something today, work through the four steps. What still needs to be done?', 'Show a grown-up the four sorry steps. Ask them about a time they had to forgive themselves for something.', 'Bring back: did you use the four sorry steps this week? What happened?', '', '', 'I can make mistakes and still be a good person. I say sorry, I make it right, and I keep going.', 'Ensure the four-step process is concrete and memorable — put it on a card they can take home. Distinguish clearly between guilt (healthy, processable) and shame (unhealthy, prolonged). The goal is not to minimise accountability but to show children how to complete the cycle.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Remember the gremlin from a few weeks ago? Today we give more power to the OTHER voice — the kind, honest, encouraging one. We''re going to build our own inner coach — a voice that''s on our side AND tells us the truth.', 'Think about a coach, teacher, or grown-up who really believed in you. What did they say? How did it feel different from when someone was just mean or critical?', 'Remember the gremlin from a few weeks ago? Today we give more power to the OTHER voice — the kind, honest, encouraging one. We''re going to build our own inner coach — a voice that''s on our side AND tells us the truth.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VXez46_LZSE', 'YouTube: Search ''inner coach for kids animated'' or ''positive self-talk for children'' for short accessible animations. Runtime ~5 min. Companion book: ''The Girl Who Never Made Mistakes'' by Mark Pett — about learning to be your own kind witness.', '', '', '', 'What would a kind coach have said to you instead?', 'THE COACH VS. GREMLIN GAME: Facilitator presents scenarios and groups decide: gremlin or coach? ''You''ll never get this right'' vs. ''That was tricky — let''s try it a different way.'' ''You''re so embarrassing'' vs. ''That felt awkward, but you were brave to try.'' ''Nobody wants to play with you'' vs. ''Making friends can be hard — who could you start with?'' Then: for your own gremlin''s favourite line, write or draw what YOUR coach would say instead. Share your coach line with the group.', 'Draw your inner coach. What do they look like? What is their name? What is their most important saying?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'When the gremlin speaks today, try having your coach answer back. Even quietly.', 'Introduce your inner coach to a grown-up. Tell them the coach''s name and what they say.', 'Bring your inner coach drawing back! Did they help you this week?', '', '', 'My inner coach is kind AND honest. The more I listen, the louder they get.', 'Children love creating and naming their inner coach — it becomes a long-running character they can reference throughout the year. Display coach drawings alongside gremlin drawings from Week 7 — the visual comparison is powerful. Coordinate with parents so they can reinforce the coach language at home.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Sometimes we do things we don''t really want to do, or say we''re okay when we''re not, just so other people feel happy. That''s called people-pleasing — and while it feels kind, it can actually stop us from being honest and taking care of ourselves. Today we learn the difference between being kind and trying to make everyone happy all the time.', 'Has anyone ever done something they didn''t really want to do just so someone else wouldn''t be upset? What did that feel like?', 'Sometimes we do things we don''t really want to do, or say we''re okay when we''re not, just so other people feel happy. That''s called people-pleasing — and while it feels kind, it can actually stop us from being honest and taking care of ourselves. Today we learn the difference between being kind and trying to make everyone happy all the time.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IRVxOCKxDyI', 'YouTube: Search ''saying no for kids read aloud'' or ''personal boundaries for children'' for short accessible animations. Runtime ~5 min. Companion book: ''My Body Belongs to Me'' by Jill Starishevsky — extends into body boundaries and personal authority.', '', '', '', 'When did you say yes when you wanted to say no?', 'KIND or PEOPLE-PLEASING? Play through scenarios: ''Your friend wants to play a game you find boring. You play anyway because you love them and it will make them happy.'' (KIND — genuine choice.) ''Someone asks if you like their drawing. You say yes even though you don''t, because you''re scared they''ll be upset.'' (PEOPLE-PLEASING.) ''You don''t want to go to the party but say you do because you''re worried everyone will be mad at you.'' (PEOPLE-PLEASING.) Discuss: what''s the difference? How can you tell from the inside? What does each one feel like in your body?', 'Draw a picture showing the difference between being kind (from the heart) and people-pleasing (from fear).', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Today, notice if you do something just to make someone happy rather than because you genuinely want to. You don''t have to change it — just notice.', 'Tell a grown-up about the difference between being kind and people-pleasing. Ask them if they ever do it too.', 'Bring back: did you notice a people-pleasing moment this week? What happened?', '', '', 'I can be kind AND honest. I don''t need to pretend to take care of myself.', 'Keep this session warm and non-shame-based — many children are actively taught to prioritise others'' feelings above their own. The goal is discernment, not selfishness. Involve parents by sending home a note about the session so they can reinforce the language.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Sometimes we worry that there isn''t enough — enough time, enough love, enough things that are good. Today we practise noticing all the things there actually ARE enough of — and how our brains can sometimes trick us into thinking things are scarcer than they are.', 'Has anyone ever worried that there wasn''t enough of something — like that they didn''t have enough friends, or that someone didn''t love them enough? What was that like?', 'Sometimes we worry that there isn''t enough — enough time, enough love, enough things that are good. Today we practise noticing all the things there actually ARE enough of — and how our brains can sometimes trick us into thinking things are scarcer than they are.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rrkrvAUbU9Y', 'YouTube: Search ''The Giving Tree read aloud Shel Silverstein'' — a classic story about generosity and what replenishes vs. what depletes. Runtime ~8 min. Also: ''Have You Filled a Bucket Today?'' read-aloud — about how kindness replenishes rather than depletes.', '', '', '', 'What do you not want to share, and why?', 'ENOUGH TREASURE HUNT: Children have 5 minutes to write or draw as many things as they can think of in their life that are ''enough'' or ''plentiful'': ''I have enough...'' — people who love me, fun things to do, things I''m good at, ways I''m kind, good memories. Share the lists. Then: facilitator points out that sharing kindness or ideas never made them smaller. Discuss: what happens to love when you give some away? Does it get smaller — or bigger?', 'Draw a picture of all the things in your life that there is ENOUGH of. Make it as full as you can!', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Today, share one kind thing with someone — and notice if it made your kindness smaller or bigger.', 'Tell a grown-up about one thing in your life that you have plenty of. Ask them what they feel they have plenty of too.', 'Bring back your ''enough'' drawing and add three more things you noticed this week!', '', '', 'I have enough love, enough kindness, and enough good things in my life. And sharing them makes more.', 'The concept of non-depletable resources (love, kindness, ideas) vs. depletable resources (biscuits, time) is a wonderful distinction for this age. Make it concrete and playful. The ''bucket filling'' concept from the book is a year-round reference tool — consider making it a classroom/programme resource.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

All the people in our lives — family, friends, teachers — teach us things about what being close to someone feels like. Some of those things are wonderful. Some might be a little confusing or hard. Today we think about the people who have shaped us most — and what we want to carry with us.', 'Who is one person in your life (or who WAS in your life) who made you feel really safe and loved? What did they teach you about what it feels like to be cared for?', 'All the people in our lives — family, friends, teachers — teach us things about what being close to someone feels like. Some of those things are wonderful. Some might be a little confusing or hard. Today we think about the people who have shaped us most — and what we want to carry with us.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9_1Rt1R4xbM', 'YouTube: ''Wonder'' read-aloud clips or ''Wilfred Gordon McDonald Partridge'' read-aloud — a beautiful story about what we carry from relationships and what we give to others. Runtime ~8 min.', '', '', '', 'What have the grown-ups who look after you taught you about being kind?', 'THE RELATIONSHIP GIFTS BOX: Each child draws a gift box. Inside the box, they draw or write gifts from important relationships — ''from [name] I learned...'' Keep it positive focus: what good things did they learn? Around the outside of the box, draw or write: ''I also want to learn more about...'' (i.e. things they wish their relationships had taught them). Share: one gift from inside your box.', 'Draw a person who has shaped you and write three things you learned from being in a relationship with them.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Today, thank someone (in person, in a letter, or in your heart) for something they gave you.', 'Tell a grown-up about one thing they''ve taught you that you want to carry with you. Watch their face.', 'Bring back your gift box drawing and tell us about the best gift inside it!', '', '', 'The people who love me teach me things I carry forever. I choose the gifts I keep.', 'Keep this session positive and boundaried — focus on what was given rather than what was withheld or damaged. Children who have experienced significant relational harm need professional support, not a group session. If something concerning is disclosed, follow your duty of care protocol and refer to appropriate support.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Sometimes when we''ve been hurt before, we build a little protective wall around our heart — we might not share our real feelings, or we might try to look like nothing bothers us. Today we talk about why those walls go up, what they do, and when it might be safe to put a door in them.', 'Has anyone ever tried to look like something doesn''t bother them when it actually does? Or acted tougher than you felt? What''s that like?', 'Sometimes when we''ve been hurt before, we build a little protective wall around our heart — we might not share our real feelings, or we might try to look like nothing bothers us. Today we talk about why those walls go up, what they do, and when it might be safe to put a door in them.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4eSBQFoVCJc', 'YouTube: Search ''The Invisible String read aloud'' or ''Last Stop on Market Street read aloud'' — stories about trust and connection after difficulty. Runtime ~8 min. Book: ''The Rabbit Listened'' by Cori Doerrfeld — about allowing someone to be with you in difficulty.', '', '', '', 'When do you go quiet so nobody can see you''re upset?', 'THE SHIELD WITH A DOOR: Each child draws a shield. On the shield they draw or write what it protects them from (things that feel scary or hurtful). Then they draw a door in the shield. On the door they write: ''I open this for people who...'' (e.g. ''keep my secrets,'' ''are kind to me,'' ''make me feel safe''). Share: what your door needs before you open it.', 'Draw your ideal safe person — someone who would deserve to see behind your shield. What makes them trustworthy?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Today, notice if your shield goes up. Ask yourself: is this danger real? Or is the shield just being extra careful?', 'Show a trusted grown-up your shield drawing. Tell them who you open the door for — and why.', 'Bring back your shield drawing! Has anything changed about when you use it?', '', '', 'I have a shield to keep me safe — and it has a door I can open when I trust someone.', 'The shield/door metaphor is beautifully concrete for this age. The key message is agency — they control the door. Never push children to lower defences in a group setting. Coordinate with families so they can continue the conversation at home.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Sometimes things end or change — friends move away, pets die, families change, things we loved go away. It''s completely normal and okay to feel really sad about those things. Today we learn that it''s important to let ourselves feel sad — and that after the sadness, something new always becomes possible.', 'Has anyone ever lost something or someone that made them really sad? A friend who moved away? A pet who died? Something that changed and you miss? It''s okay to talk about those feelings today.', 'Sometimes things end or change — friends move away, pets die, families change, things we loved go away. It''s completely normal and okay to feel really sad about those things. Today we learn that it''s important to let ourselves feel sad — and that after the sadness, something new always becomes possible.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7H2pBdLnmGs', 'YouTube: ''The Invisible String'' read-aloud — a beautiful, gentle story about connection that continues even through endings and loss. Runtime ~8 min. Book: ''The Goodbye Book'' by Todd Parr — simple, reassuring, and age-appropriate for all types of loss.', '', '', '', 'What have you lost that you still miss?', 'THE FEELINGS TREE: Each child draws a tree with four sections representing the four seasons. In the autumn section: what is something that has ended or changed that makes you sad? In the winter section: what does that sadness feel like? In the spring section: what small new thing has grown or could grow because of the change? In the summer section: what do you hope the future will bring? Share: your spring section — something small that has grown.', 'Draw how you feel when something ends. Then draw how you might feel after some time has passed.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'If you''re feeling sad about something today, find a safe person to tell. You don''t have to fix the sadness — just share it.', 'Tell a grown-up about something you''ve felt sad about. Ask them to just listen — you don''t need advice, just company.', 'Bring back your feelings tree! Has anything changed in your spring or summer sections?', '', '', 'It''s okay to feel sad when things end. Sadness moves through when we let it. And something new always comes.', 'This is a sensitive session that may bring up significant losses for some children. Ensure pre-communication with parents/caregivers — particularly if any children in the group have recently experienced bereavement. The seasons metaphor is gentle and non-prescriptive. Maintain access to a pastoral support person.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Everyone feels scared sometimes — and that''s completely okay. Fear is actually really useful when it warns us about real danger. But sometimes our fear alarm goes off when things are just new or a bit uncomfortable — not actually dangerous. Today we learn to tell the difference!', 'Can anyone name something that feels scary but isn''t actually dangerous? Like talking in front of the class, or trying something new, or meeting someone you don''t know? What does scary-but-safe feel like?', 'Everyone feels scared sometimes — and that''s completely okay. Fear is actually really useful when it warns us about real danger. But sometimes our fear alarm goes off when things are just new or a bit uncomfortable — not actually dangerous. Today we learn to tell the difference!', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BVAaomgzFCM', 'YouTube: Search ''brave for kids animated fear YouTube'' or ''facing fears children animated'' for short accessible animations on being courageous about non-dangerous fears. Runtime ~5 min. Book: ''Jabari Jumps'' by Gaia Cornwall — a child who is scared to jump off the diving board and works up the courage to try.', '', '', '', 'What are you scared of that has never actually happened?', 'REAL FIRE or BURNT TOAST? Play through scenarios together: ''A stranger asks you to go somewhere alone'' — REAL FIRE (tell a trusted adult). ''You have to do a speech in front of the class'' — BURNT TOAST (scary but safe, take a breath). ''Your friends are about to jump off something really high'' — REAL FIRE. ''You want to try a new sport but feel nervous'' — BURNT TOAST. Then: think of something that feels scary in your life. Real fire or burnt toast? How do you know?', 'Draw a burnt toast fear and a real fire fear. How are they different? What do you do for each one?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'When you feel your fear alarm today, ask: real fire or burnt toast? Then decide what to do.', 'Tell a grown-up about something that''s burnt toast for you — scary but safe. Ask them about one of theirs!', 'Bring back: did you have a burnt toast moment this week? What happened when you were brave about it?', '', '', 'My fear alarm helps keep me safe. And I''m learning when to listen — and when to be brave.', 'The real fire/burnt toast distinction is brilliantly concrete and memorable for this age. Physical breathing practice can be integrated directly into the role-play. This language can become a year-round reference: ''is that a real fire?'' Coordinate with parents to use the same language at home.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Sometimes the things we believe about ourselves are a bit out of date — like a picture of you from when you were really little. The picture might have been true then, but it''s not the whole picture of you now. Today we look at old stories and think about whether it''s time to update them.', 'Think of something you used to believe about yourself that might not be as true anymore. Maybe you used to think you couldn''t do something — and now you can. What has changed about you?', 'Sometimes the things we believe about ourselves are a bit out of date — like a picture of you from when you were really little. The picture might have been true then, but it''s not the whole picture of you now. Today we look at old stories and think about whether it''s time to update them.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0ZcfX2862XE', 'YouTube: ''The Dot'' by Peter Reynolds read-aloud — about being willing to see yourself differently and discovering new capacities. Runtime ~8 min. Companion book: ''Beautiful Oops'' by Barney Saltzberg — about reinterpreting old ''mistakes'' as the beginning of something new.', '', '', '', 'What did you used to believe about yourself that isn''t true now?', 'THE UPDATED PHOTO ALBUM: Each child gets a four-page ''photo album'' template. Page 1: ''An old story I had about myself'' (draw or write). Page 2: ''What has changed or grown since then'' (draw or write). Page 3: ''Something I can do now that I couldn''t do before'' (draw or write). Page 4: ''The new updated picture of me'' (draw or write — as full and complete as possible). Share: Page 4 — the new updated picture.', 'Draw ''old you'' vs. ''new you'' — what has grown and changed? Celebrate every difference!', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Today, notice one way you are more than your old story. Tell someone about it.', 'Show a grown-up your updated photo album. Ask them to tell you one way they have seen you grow.', 'Bring your photo album back with a new entry — something that grew this week!', '', '', 'My story is growing, just like me. I add new pages all the time.', 'The photo album exercise is deeply affirming — let children spend real time on Page 4 (the new, updated picture of themselves). Display them in the room if children are happy to. Celebrate growth explicitly and specifically. This is one of the most joyful sessions of Phase 2.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

We''ve been on the second part of our big adventure — learning how to put down some heavy things, say sorry properly, be brave about our fears, and start telling new stories about ourselves. Today we celebrate everything we''ve let go — and get excited for the next part of the journey: building!', 'What is one heavy thing you''ve put down or made lighter during Phase 2? Maybe something you stopped worrying about as much. Something you said sorry for and felt better. A fear you were brave about. A story you started telling differently.', 'We''ve been on the second part of our big adventure — learning how to put down some heavy things, say sorry properly, be brave about our fears, and start telling new stories about ourselves. Today we celebrate everything we''ve let go — and get excited for the next part of the journey: building!', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VWOgrMXBE4U', 'YouTube: Search ''growth and change kids celebration animated'' for an uplifting short about completing a challenging journey. Runtime ~3–5 min. Book: ''The Journey'' by Francesca Sanna — a beautiful book about carrying what matters and leaving behind what doesn''t.', '', '', '', 'What have you let go of this term?', 'PHASE 2 CELEBRATION: Each child gets a paper ''heavy stone'' and a paper ''feather.'' On the stone, they write one heavy thing they''ve worked on putting down. On the feather, they write one thing that feels lighter now. Create a class display: all the stones in a pile, all the feathers flying around it. Read out the feathers together (keeping stones private). Celebrate every single one. Then: give each child a fresh blank page for Phase 3. ''Now we build.''', 'Draw a picture of yourself lighter — after putting down something heavy. What does your face look like? How do you stand?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Celebrate one thing you''re proud of from Phase 2. Tell someone about it!', 'Show a grown-up your stone and feather. Tell them about the heavy thing you''ve been working on and the lighter thing you feel now.', 'Come to the first Phase 3 session ready to tell us the most exciting thing you''re going to BUILD!', '', '', 'I put down some heavy things. And now my hands are free to build something new.', 'Make this session genuinely celebratory — balloons, music, something special. Children have done profound work in Phase 2. The stone/feather display is beautiful — photograph it and share with families. The transition to Phase 3 should feel like a genuine adventure beginning. Pure excitement.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

We''ve been on a huge adventure learning about ourselves — now comes the most exciting part: BUILDING! Today we start thinking about who we are CHOOSING to be — the qualities and values that make us most us — and how to grow more of them.', 'If you could choose the most important qualities about yourself — things like kindness, courage, creativity, honesty, curiosity — what would you choose? What matters most to you?', 'We''ve been on a huge adventure learning about ourselves — now comes the most exciting part: BUILDING! Today we start thinking about who we are CHOOSING to be — the qualities and values that make us most us — and how to grow more of them.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H14bBuluwB8', 'YouTube: ''What Do You Do With an Idea?'' read-aloud by Kobi Yamada — about nurturing what you are building from the inside out. Runtime ~8 min. Book: ''Beautiful Me'' by Kimberly and James Dean — affirming exploration of who you choose to be.', '', '', '', 'Who do you want to be?', 'THE QUALITY BUILDER: Each child gets a brick-wall template (8–10 bricks). In each brick, they write or draw a quality they want to build in themselves — courage, kindness, creativity, perseverance, honesty, curiosity, etc. Then: circle the three most important ones. These are the foundations of their personal rebuild. Share: their three foundation bricks. Facilitator writes a class collective wall — all the bricks together.', 'Draw a picture of ''Future Me'' — the version of you with all the qualities you''re building. What does that person look like?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Today, practise one of your foundation qualities in one real situation. Notice how it feels.', 'Tell a grown-up about your three foundation bricks. Ask them what theirs would be.', 'Bring back your brick wall and add new bricks you''ve discovered this week!', '', '', 'I am choosing who I am building. My qualities are mine to grow.', 'The building metaphor is enormously energising at this age — make it as physical and visual as possible. The collective class wall of qualities displayed in the room is a powerful image of community values. Keep the energy high — this is the most fun phase of the year.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Values are like the most important rules you make for yourself — not rules from other people, but the things YOU decide are most important about how you live and treat others. Today we find out what YOUR most important values are.', 'What is the most important rule YOU have made for yourself — something you believe about how to treat people or how to live? Not a rule from school or home — something that feels most like yours.', 'Values are like the most important rules you make for yourself — not rules from other people, but the things YOU decide are most important about how you live and treat others. Today we find out what YOUR most important values are.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IRVxOCKxDyI', 'YouTube: Search ''values for kids animated'' or ''what are values children'' for short accessible content. Runtime ~5 min. Book: ''Those Shoes'' by Maribeth Boelts — a beautiful story about knowing what you truly value versus what you want because others have it.', '', '', '', 'What''s the most important thing to you?', 'THE VALUES COMPASS: Each child gets a large compass drawn on paper (pointing N, S, E, W). In the four directions, they write or draw their four most important values. Facilitator shares examples and helps with vocabulary. Then: present dilemmas and ask children to use their compass: ''Your friend asks you to keep a secret that worries you — which value guides you?'' / ''Someone is being left out — which value helps you decide what to do?'' Share: your compass and your most important direction.', 'Draw your inner compass. Write your four most important values in the four directions. Decorate it so it looks like YOU.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'When you face a choice today, use your compass: ''Which of my values guides me here?'' Tell someone about it.', 'Show your compass to a grown-up. Tell them about the values you chose. Ask them what their compass points to.', 'Bring your compass back! Did you use it this week? What happened?', '', '', 'My values are my compass. They help me know who I am and how to treat others.', 'The compass is a brilliant physical metaphor — make it beautiful and keep it as a year-round tool. Present the dilemmas with warmth and humour. The discovery that values-based decisions feel better than approval-seeking decisions is a genuine revelation for this age.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Habits are things we practise so often they become automatic — we do them without even thinking. Today we think about the habits that GROW us — the small things we do every day that make us more of who we want to be.', 'What is something you already do every day that has made you better at something or made you feel good about yourself? (Reading, practising a sport, being kind, helping someone.) How did that habit start?', 'Habits are things we practise so often they become automatic — we do them without even thinking. Today we think about the habits that GROW us — the small things we do every day that make us more of who we want to be.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hpnI3MCTJSA', 'YouTube: ''The Power of Yet'' animated — Carol Dweck for kids, about the habit of persisting. Runtime ~5 min. Book: ''Little Acorn Becomes a Tree'' or ''What a Seed Knows'' for the growth metaphor. Also: ''Dreamers'' by Yuyi Morales — about slow, persistent building.', '', '', '', 'What do you do every day that makes you a bit better at something?', 'THE HABIT GARDEN: Each child gets a garden template with 3 plant pots. In each pot, they draw or write a small daily habit they want to grow — something that will help them build one of their quality-bricks from Week 27. Then they write: what''s the SMALLEST daily version? (E.g. ''I will read for 5 minutes before bed'' / ''I will say one kind thing to someone every day'' / ''I will draw something for 3 minutes.''). Share: their three habit seeds and the smallest daily version of each.', 'Draw your habit garden in full — name the plants, draw how they might look when they''ve grown!', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Start ONE of your habit plants today — the tiniest version. Just begin. Tell someone about it tonight.', 'Show a grown-up your habit garden. Ask them what habit they wish they had started when they were your age.', 'Bring back: how many days did you water your habit plant? What happened?', '', '', 'Small daily habits grow into big wonderful things. I water my garden every day.', 'The garden metaphor is perfect for this age — consider having small actual seed packets as a physical take-home that mirrors the metaphor. The minimum habit concept (''just the tiniest version'') dramatically reduces the activation energy. Send a habit tracking sheet home for family engagement.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Our bodies are the most amazing machines — they need certain things to work really well: good sleep, movement, healthy food, and ways to calm down when we feel stressed. Today we learn how to take care of our bodies so they can help us feel and be our best.', 'Can you tell when your body needs more sleep? How do you feel? What about when you haven''t moved around enough — how does that feel? What about when you''ve eaten mostly sugary things all day? Your body sends signals — let''s learn to read them.', 'Our bodies are the most amazing machines — they need certain things to work really well: good sleep, movement, healthy food, and ways to calm down when we feel stressed. Today we learn how to take care of our bodies so they can help us feel and be our best.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BVAaomgzFCM', 'YouTube: ''Sesame Street Belly Breathe'' or search ''kids movement and sleep importance animated'' for fun accessible content on body care for children. Runtime ~3–5 min. Book: ''I Am Yoga'' by Susan Verde — a beautiful mindful body awareness book.', '', '', '', 'What does your body need more of?', 'SUPERHERO SUIT CHECK: Each child rates their four areas with a simple traffic light (red/orange/green): Sleep, Movement, Food, Calm-Down Skills. Then for their most orange or red area: ''What is ONE small thing I could do to give this area a bit more green?'' Facilitator works through examples: sleep (same bedtime every night, dark room), movement (playing outside, dancing, walking), food (one more piece of fruit, water before lunch), calm (three deep breaths, a favourite calming activity). Share: one upgrade they''re committing to.', 'Draw your superhero suit charged up and ready. Label the four charging stations around it.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Try ONE of your charging habits today — and notice how it affects how you feel.', 'Tell a grown-up about the four charging areas. Ask them which one they find hardest to keep charged. Compare answers!', 'Bring back your superhero suit drawing — has anything changed in your charging levels?', '', '', 'When I take care of my body, I can be the best version of me. Sleep, movement, food, and calm — my four superchargers.', 'The superhero charging metaphor is endlessly engaging for this age. Make the breathing practice a regular feature of every session from this point forward — 3 breaths to open each session. Involve families in the four charging areas — send a visual home they can put on the fridge.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

The people we spend time with help shape who we become — because we learn from them, we pick up their habits and feelings, and we become more ourselves (or less ourselves) depending on who we''re around. Today we think about the people in our lives who help us grow — and how to be that kind of person for others.', 'Think of a friend or person who makes you feel really good — more yourself, happier, braver. What is it about them that makes you feel that way? What do they do that helps you grow?', 'The people we spend time with help shape who we become — because we learn from them, we pick up their habits and feelings, and we become more ourselves (or less ourselves) depending on who we''re around. Today we think about the people in our lives who help us grow — and how to be that kind of person for others.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9_1Rt1R4xbM', 'YouTube: ''Charlotte''s Web'' book read-aloud clips or search ''friendship for kids animated'' for short content on what makes a good friend. Runtime ~5–8 min. Book: ''The Invisible String'' by Patrice Karst — about the connections that matter most.', '', '', '', 'Who makes you feel like yourself?', 'THE GROWING FRIEND GARDEN: Each child gets a garden template with space for 3–4 friends. For each friend: draw or write their name, one thing they do that helps you grow, and one thing you do that helps THEM grow. Then: draw yourself in the garden too. What do you bring to your friendships? Share: one growing friend and one thing they bring to you.', 'Draw a picture showing you and a growing friend doing something together. What makes this friendship a growing one?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Do something kind or encouraging for a growing friend today — and notice how it feels to give as well as receive.', 'Tell a grown-up about one of your growing friends and why they matter to you. Ask them about their growing friends.', 'Bring back a story about something a growing friend did for you this week — or something you did for them!', '', '', 'I choose friends who help me grow — and I am a growing friend for others.', 'The growing friend concept should be kept warm and affirmative — this is not about judging friendships but about celebrating the ones that genuinely nourish. Acknowledge that all friendships have ups and downs. The seed activity (doing one kind thing for a growing friend) should have a real follow-through plan.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

We''ve been building our inner coach — the kind, honest voice inside us. This week we practise using that voice every day. Today we design our personal ''power phrases'' — the things we say to ourselves that help us feel brave, kind, and capable.', 'What is the most helpful thing a kind voice could say to you when you''re having a hard day? When you''ve made a mistake? When you''re about to try something scary? What do you most need to hear?', 'We''ve been building our inner coach — the kind, honest voice inside us. This week we practise using that voice every day. Today we design our personal ''power phrases'' — the things we say to ourselves that help us feel brave, kind, and capable.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VXez46_LZSE', 'YouTube: Search ''positive self-talk for kids animated'' or ''affirmations for children YouTube'' for short, accessible animations. Runtime ~5 min. Book: ''I Am Enough'' by Grace Byers — a beautiful collection of affirmations in picture book form.', '', '', '', 'What would you say to a friend who was where you are?', 'POWER PHRASE CREATOR: Guide children through three types of power phrase: 1. BRAVE phrase (for when something feels scary): e.g. ''I can be scared AND brave at the same time.'' 2. KIND phrase (for when you''ve made a mistake): e.g. ''I made a mistake. That doesn''t make me bad. I can try again.'' 3. STRONG phrase (for hard days): e.g. ''I am doing my best, and that is enough.'' Each child writes their own version of each type — in their own words. Share: their brave phrase with the group.', 'Write or decorate your three power phrases on a card to keep. Make it beautiful — it''s important!', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Use your brave phrase today — even if nothing scary happens, just practise saying it.', 'Teach a grown-up your three power phrases. Ask them what THEIR power phrases are.', 'Bring back your power phrase card! Which one did you use most this week?', '', '', 'I have words that help me. I say them to myself with kindness and truth.', 'Create beautiful, laminated power phrase cards for children to take home — make them special objects, not just worksheets. Involve parents: send a note explaining power phrases and asking them to use the same language at home. The three-category structure (brave, kind, strong) covers the most important emotional situations.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Having a routine — a regular order for how we do things — actually helps us feel safer, calmer, and more able to enjoy the fun parts of our day. Today we think about the routines that help us the most — and maybe design some new ones.', 'What''s a routine you have that really helps you? Maybe a bedtime routine, or how you get ready in the morning, or something you do after school? Why does it help?', 'Having a routine — a regular order for how we do things — actually helps us feel safer, calmer, and more able to enjoy the fun parts of our day. Today we think about the routines that help us the most — and maybe design some new ones.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nj2ofrX7jAk', 'YouTube: Search ''daily routine for kids animated'' for short, engaging content about healthy daily rhythms. Runtime ~5 min. Book: ''Bedtime for Frances'' by Russell Hoban — gently illustrates the importance of routine and what happens when it''s disrupted.', '', '', '', 'What part of your week do you look forward to?', 'MY DAILY RHYTHM: Give each child a simple clock/timeline template for a day. Together, fill in the key anchors: wake time, breakfast, school or activity, movement time, connection time (family/friends), quiet or creative time, bedtime. Then: ''Is there one part of your day that feels chaotic or hard? Could a small routine help?'' Design one new mini-routine for that part. Share: their new mini-routine.', 'Draw your ideal daily rhythm as a clock or timeline. What are the most important parts?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Try your new mini-routine today. Notice how it feels to have that part of your day feel more settled.', 'Tell a grown-up about your new mini-routine. Ask them to help you stick to it this week.', 'Bring back: how did your mini-routine go? Did it help?', '', '', 'A good daily rhythm helps me feel calm, settled, and ready for anything.', 'Coordinate with parents for this session — family buy-in on routine changes is essential for children. Focus on one small, achievable routine improvement rather than a whole-day redesign. Sleep routine is the highest-leverage area for most primary-age children. Send home a simple routine template families can use together.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Rest is not just sleep — it''s also the quiet, gentle times when our brain and body get to recover and refuel. Today we learn about the importance of rest, what real rest looks and feels like, and how to give our brain the recovery time it needs.', 'What do you do when you want to relax and feel better? What makes you feel most refreshed and restored? Is it different to what you do when you''re bored?', 'Rest is not just sleep — it''s also the quiet, gentle times when our brain and body get to recover and refuel. Today we learn about the importance of rest, what real rest looks and feels like, and how to give our brain the recovery time it needs.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nj2ofrX7jAk', 'YouTube: Search ''rest for kids why it matters animated'' or ''why do we need rest children YouTube'' for short accessible content. Runtime ~5 min. Book: ''The Rabbit Listened'' by Cori Doerrfeld — about the kind of quiet presence that genuinely restores.', '', '', '', 'When do you feel properly rested?', 'REST vs. BUSY BREAK: Show children two lists and sort together: REST (quiet reading, outdoor play, drawing, daydreaming, calm music, gentle movement) vs. BUSY BREAK (lots of screens, fast-paced games, scrolling, loud noise). Discuss: how does each feel in your body? How do you feel after each? Then: design your personal ''rest menu'' — three go-to genuine rest activities that work for YOU. Share: their top rest activity.', 'Draw your ''rest menu'' — three activities that give your brain real rest. Make it beautiful!', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Take a genuine rest break today — from your rest menu. Notice how you feel before and after.', 'Show a grown-up your rest menu. Ask them what rest looks like for them. Plan a rest time together this week.', 'Bring back: which rest activity did you try? How did it feel?', '', '', 'Real rest is when my brain gets to breathe. It makes everything else better.', 'The rest menu is a lovely, practical take-home from this session. The 2-minute rest practice in the session is worth doing slowly and genuinely — model it yourself. Coordinate with parents to support genuine rest practices at home, distinct from screen time. The rest/busy-break distinction is a powerful concept for both children and parents.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Making things — drawing, building, writing, singing, dancing, inventing — is one of the most wonderful things human beings can do. And everyone can do it! Today we celebrate creativity, remember what we love to make, and give ourselves permission to create without worrying about whether it''s perfect.', 'What is your absolute favourite thing to make or create? Drawing? Building? Writing? Dancing? Making music? Something else? What does it feel like when you''re deep in making something you love?', 'Making things — drawing, building, writing, singing, dancing, inventing — is one of the most wonderful things human beings can do. And everyone can do it! Today we celebrate creativity, remember what we love to make, and give ourselves permission to create without worrying about whether it''s perfect.', 'YouTube: ''The Dot'' by Peter Reynolds read-aloud — the perfect celebration of making something just because it matters to you. Runtime ~8 min. Companion book: ''Beautiful Oops'' by Barney Saltzberg — a joyful celebration of imperfect making.', 'Search: ''The Dot read aloud Peter Reynolds YouTube'' if unavailable. Alternative: ''What To Do With a Box'' by Jane Yolen — a poem-book celebrating the creativity of children.', '', '', '', 'What do you love making?', 'THE MAKING PARTY: Facilitate a free-choice creative session — provide a range of materials (drawing supplies, building blocks, collage materials, writing paper, musical instruments if available). For 15 minutes, everyone makes something — anything they want, however they want. No instructions. No right answer. No evaluation. Then: share what you made — not for judgment but for celebration. Each share receives: ''Tell us about your making — what did you enjoy about it?'' NOT ''That''s so good!'' (evaluation). Just genuine curiosity.', 'Make something today just for the joy of it — not to show anyone, not to get it right. Just because making things is wonderful.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Show a grown-up something you''ve made recently. Tell them about what you ENJOYED about making it — not whether you think it''s good.', 'Bring something you''ve made this week to share — just to celebrate the making!', 'I am creative. Making things is part of how I am most alive. I make for joy.', '', '', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0ZcfX2862XE', '', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Every person has gifts — things they''re naturally good at, things they love, and ways they can help others. When we use our gifts to help and contribute, that''s called purpose. Today we start discovering what our gifts are and how we can share them.', 'What is something you love doing AND you''re good at AND it helps other people? It might be something you haven''t thought of as a gift before.', 'Every person has gifts — things they''re naturally good at, things they love, and ways they can help others. When we use our gifts to help and contribute, that''s called purpose. Today we start discovering what our gifts are and how we can share them.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9_1Rt1R4xbM', 'YouTube: ''Wonder'' read-aloud clips or search ''purpose for kids animated gifts'' for short accessible content on contribution and gifts. Runtime ~5–8 min. Book: ''The Jelly That Wouldn''t Wiggle'' by Alexandra Parry — about each person''s unique contribution to something bigger.', '', '', '', 'What are you doing when you forget about time?', 'GIFT EXPLORER: Three prompts for each child to write or draw: 1. ''Something I love and I''m good at is...'' 2. ''Something I do that seems to help or matter to others is...'' 3. ''If I could change one thing about the world, I would...'' Then: where do these overlap? That''s the beginning of your purpose. Share: one gift they have that they want to use more.', 'Draw your ''YOU-shaped puzzle piece'' — write your gifts inside it and draw how it connects to the people and world around you.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Use one of your gifts to help someone today. Notice how it feels.', 'Tell a grown-up about one of your gifts. Ask them what gift they think you have that you might not have noticed yet.', 'Bring back your puzzle piece drawing — and a story about using one of your gifts this week!', '', '', 'I have gifts that are uniquely mine. Using them to help others is my purpose.', 'Keep purpose concrete and immediately actionable for this age — not about the future, but about what they can contribute today. Celebrate every ''gift'' that is shared generously and specifically. The puzzle metaphor reinforces both uniqueness AND interdependence — both are important values to embed.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Money is something that grown-ups think about a lot — and most children hear messages about it without fully understanding them. Today we think about what we''ve been taught about money and resources, and what a healthy, kind relationship with what we have looks like.', 'What is something you have — that doesn''t cost any money — that you''re really grateful for? And what is something you own that you love sharing with others?', 'Money is something that grown-ups think about a lot — and most children hear messages about it without fully understanding them. Today we think about what we''ve been taught about money and resources, and what a healthy, kind relationship with what we have looks like.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rrkrvAUbU9Y', 'YouTube: Search ''generosity for kids animated'' or ''gratitude and giving children YouTube'' for short accessible content. Runtime ~5 min. Book: ''Those Shoes'' by Maribeth Boelts — a beautiful story about needs vs. wants and the joy of generosity.', '', '', '', 'What would you do with ten dollars, and why?', 'NEED vs. WANT vs. SHARE: Facilitate a sorting activity with picture cards or drawn items: sort into NEED (food, shelter, warmth, healthcare), WANT (toys, treats, gadgets), and COULD SHARE (time, kindness, skills, some possessions). Discuss: ''Is it possible to share something that doesn''t cost money? What can you share that isn''t a thing?'' Then: each child identifies one thing they''re grateful for, and one non-money thing they can share this week. Share: their chosen gratitude and their generous act.', 'Draw or write about three things you have that money can''t buy — and three things you can share with others.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Do one generous act this week — something you give that doesn''t cost money.', 'Ask a grown-up: ''What''s something you have that you''re really grateful for that money can''t buy?'' Share your answer with them too.', 'Bring back: what generous act did you do this week? How did it feel?', '', '', 'I am grateful for what I have. And I am generous with what I can share.', 'Be sensitive to varying financial circumstances among children — never compare or highlight differences. Focus on non-material forms of abundance (time, kindness, skills, imagination) which are genuinely available to all. The need/want/share activity is one of the most practically valuable financial literacy exercises for this age.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

We all belong to communities — our family, our class, our sports team, our neighbourhood. A good community is one where people care for each other, help each other, and make each other feel like they belong. Today we think about the communities we''re part of — and how to make them better.', 'What communities are you part of? Name as many as you can — family, class, sports team, neighbourhood, this group. What makes each one special?', 'We all belong to communities — our family, our class, our sports team, our neighbourhood. A good community is one where people care for each other, help each other, and make each other feel like they belong. Today we think about the communities we''re part of — and how to make them better.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YRaVl-VjF2g', 'YouTube: Search ''community and belonging for kids animated'' or ''teamwork children YouTube'' for accessible short content. Runtime ~5 min. Book: ''Last Stop on Market Street'' by Matt de la Pena — a beautiful story about noticing and contributing to the community around you.', '', '', '', 'What do you bring to a group?', 'COMMUNITY BUILDER: Each child identifies two or three communities they belong to. For each: ''What does this community give me?'' and ''What do I give to this community?'' Then: ''Is there someone in one of my communities who might feel left out or could use more belonging? What is one thing I could do to include them or make them feel more part of things?'' Share: one community they love and one thing they contribute to it.', 'Draw your favourite community. Write or draw what everyone in it contributes — including yourself.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Do one thing today that makes one of your communities a tiny bit better — include someone, help someone, contribute something.', 'Tell a grown-up about one of your communities and what you love about belonging to it. Ask them about their favourite community.', 'Bring back: what did you do to make your community better this week? What happened?', '', '', 'I belong to communities that matter. And I make them better by contributing who I am.', 'The beehive metaphor is wonderful for group dynamics — every child can see themselves as essential. The ''someone who might need more belonging'' prompt is powerful and should be handled with sensitivity — make it about outward reaching, not inward inventory of who is and isn''t included.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

We''ve been building for 13 weeks! Today we celebrate everything we''ve grown and built — and get ready for the most exciting phase yet: going out into the world and USING everything we''ve built to make things better.', 'Let''s go on a memory adventure through Phase 3! What are all the things we''ve built and grown in the last 13 weeks? (Identity, values compass, habit garden, superhero suit, growing friends, inner coach voice, daily rhythm, rest, creativity, purpose puzzle piece, community...)', 'We''ve been building for 13 weeks! Today we celebrate everything we''ve grown and built — and get ready for the most exciting phase yet: going out into the world and USING everything we''ve built to make things better.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VWOgrMXBE4U', 'YouTube: ''Oh, the Places You''ll Go!'' read-aloud by Dr Seuss — the perfect send-off from building to living. Runtime ~8 min. Also: search ''children growth celebration animated YouTube'' for uplifting content.', '', '', '', 'What''s different about you now?', 'PHASE 3 CELEBRATION TOWER: Each child gets a series of ''brick'' cards (one per Phase 3 theme). They write one thing they built in each brick. Stack the bricks into a tower. Display all the towers together — the visual of everything built. Then: add one ''door'' brick at the top of each tower: ''Phase 4 — what I''m bringing into the world.'' Share: their most important brick and what''s written on their door.', 'Draw your building tower from Phase 3 — full, colourful, yours. What''s written on the door at the top?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Celebrate one thing you built in Phase 3 today — use one of your Phase 3 tools in the real world.', 'Show a grown-up your tower. Tell them everything that''s in it. Let them be genuinely amazed.', 'Come to the first Phase 4 session ready to tell us: what are you going to DO with everything you''ve built?', '', '', 'I built something real and strong. Now I get to take it into the world. Phase 4 — here I come!', 'Make this session genuinely spectacular — this is the three-phase arc completing and Phase 4 beginning. Balloons, music, a visual display of all three phases'' work together. Children should leave feeling genuinely proud, genuinely capable, and genuinely excited. The tower display is a beautiful artefact — photograph it and share with families.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

We''ve spent all year learning about ourselves — our feelings, our habits, our strengths, and our values. Now comes the most exciting part: using everything we''ve learned to make things better for the people around us! Today we think about how to share our superpowers with the world.', 'What is the most important thing you''ve learned about yourself this year? And who is one person in your life who could use that learning — who is going through something you''ve already learned about?', 'We''ve spent all year learning about ourselves — our feelings, our habits, our strengths, and our values. Now comes the most exciting part: using everything we''ve learned to make things better for the people around us! Today we think about how to share our superpowers with the world.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rrkrvAUbU9Y', 'YouTube: Search ''kindness for kids animated service'' or read-aloud of ''Each Kindness'' by Jacqueline Woodson — about the treasure of kindness and what it does when you share it. Runtime ~8 min.', '', '', '', 'Who could you help this week?', 'TREASURE MAP: Each child gets a treasure map template. They mark three ''treasures'' they''ve gathered this year — the most important things they''ve learned or built. Then they draw a path from the treasure to someone who could benefit from it. For each treasure: who would benefit? What specifically would you give them — a kindness, a conversation, a skill, an example? Share: their most important treasure and who they want to give it to.', 'Draw yourself giving one of your treasures to someone who needs it. What are you giving? What happens when they receive it?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Do one act of genuine service today — give one of your treasures to someone who needs it.', 'Tell a grown-up about one treasure you want to share and who you want to give it to. Ask them to help you do it.', 'Bring back: what treasure did you share this week? What happened?', '', '', 'I have treasures to share. Giving them to others is one of the best things I can do.', 'This session should feel genuinely joyful — the year''s arc completing in outward giving. The treasure map activity is beautiful and can be displayed. Keep the service concrete and age-appropriate. Celebrate every act of giving that is shared back.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

One of the best ways to really know something is to teach it to someone else. Today we practise sharing the things we''ve learned this year — with our families, our friends, and our community. When we teach, we learn even more deeply!', 'What is one thing you''ve learned this year that you could teach to a younger child — or to a grown-up who had never heard of it? What would you say?', 'One of the best ways to really know something is to teach it to someone else. Today we practise sharing the things we''ve learned this year — with our families, our friends, and our community. When we teach, we learn even more deeply!', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0ZcfX2862XE', 'YouTube: Search ''kids teaching each other learning animated'' or ''peer learning children YouTube'' for accessible short content. Runtime ~5 min. Book: ''The One and Only Ivan'' — about passing on what you know to those who come after.', '', '', '', 'What could you teach someone younger than you?', 'MINI TEACHER: Each child prepares a 2-minute ''lesson'' to share with the group. They choose one thing they''ve learned this year — any concept from any session — and explain it in their own words with an example. Facilitator gives 5 minutes to prepare. Then each child shares their lesson. Group responses: ''What I understood from that was...'' and ''One question I have is...'' Celebrate every share generously.', 'Write or draw your ''lesson'' from today in a simple way that someone younger could understand. Give it a title!', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Teach one thing from this year to someone at home today — a parent, sibling, or anyone who''ll listen. Notice how it feels.', 'Ask a grown-up: ''Can I teach you something I learned this year?'' Then teach them. Watch their face.', 'Bring back: who did you teach? What happened? Did you learn anything new by teaching it?', '', '', 'I have things worth teaching. When I share what I know, I learn it even more deeply.', 'The mini-teacher activity is one of the most joyful sessions of Phase 4 — children are genuinely proud of their knowledge. Give ample preparation time and make the sharing feel like a celebration, not a performance. Video the sessions with parental consent — children love watching themselves teach.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Being seen means letting people know who you really are — not just the brave face or the happy face, but the real you, with all your feelings and ideas and wonderfulness. Today we practise the courage of being genuinely, fully ourselves in front of the people we care about.', 'Think of a time when you showed up completely as yourself — no pretending, no performing — and something really good happened because of it. What was that like?', 'Being seen means letting people know who you really are — not just the brave face or the happy face, but the real you, with all your feelings and ideas and wonderfulness. Today we practise the courage of being genuinely, fully ourselves in front of the people we care about.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YRaVl-VjF2g', 'YouTube: Search ''being yourself courage kids animated'' or ''The Name Jar read aloud YouTube'' — about the courage to claim and show your real self. Runtime ~8 min.', '', '', '', 'What''s something true about you that you keep hidden?', 'THE REAL ME GALLERY: Each child creates a small ''gallery card'' about themselves — their real self. Sections: My real name and one thing about it, One thing I love that people might not know, One thing I find hard that I''m working on, One thing I''m really proud of about myself, One way I want people to know me. Cards are displayed in a ''Real Me Gallery'' around the room. Gallery walk — everyone reads each other''s cards. Share: one thing from someone else''s card that surprised or delighted you.', 'Make a small card showing the real you — something genuine that you''re ready to share with someone new.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Show your real self in one interaction today — let someone see something genuine about you that you usually keep to yourself.', 'Give your ''Real Me'' gallery card to a grown-up who loves you. Tell them you made it in your programme today.', 'Bring back: what happened when you showed your real self to someone this week?', '', '', 'The real me is wonderful. And the world gets better when I show up as exactly who I am.', 'Reference the mask craft from Phase 1 explicitly — this is a beautiful callback that shows the full arc of the year. The gallery walk is one of the most moving activities of the year — protect the time for it. Keep the emotional tone warm and celebratory, not earnest or heavy.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Sometimes it''s hard to do the right thing — especially when other people want us to do something different. Today we practise staying true to our values compass even when it''s challenging. Because that''s when our compass matters most.', 'Can you think of a time when it was hard to do what you knew was right? Maybe your friends wanted you to do something that didn''t feel right, or you had to be honest when it was easier to stay quiet. What happened?', 'Sometimes it''s hard to do the right thing — especially when other people want us to do something different. Today we practise staying true to our values compass even when it''s challenging. Because that''s when our compass matters most.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IRVxOCKxDyI', 'YouTube: Search ''standing up for what''s right kids animated'' or ''moral courage children stories YouTube'' for accessible content. Runtime ~5–8 min. Book: ''Each Kindness'' by Jacqueline Woodson — about the moment when you have the chance to do the right thing and what happens when you do and when you don''t.', '', '', '', 'When is it hardest to do the right thing?', 'STORM PRACTICE: Present 3–4 age-appropriate scenarios where a value is under pressure (e.g. ''Your friends are laughing at another child. Your kindness compass says something different. What do you do?'' / ''You broke something by accident. Your honesty compass is pointing at telling the truth. But you''re scared. What do you do?''). For each scenario: What does your compass say? What makes it hard to follow it? What could you say or do? Role-play one scenario with a partner. Share: what was hardest about following the compass in the role-play?', 'Draw a scene where you follow your compass in a stormy moment — what are you doing? What does your face look like?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Today, notice once when your values compass gives you a direction that might be uncomfortable. Try to follow it — even a little bit.', 'Tell a grown-up about one time you followed your values compass even when it was hard. What happened?', 'Bring back: did you follow your compass this week when it was hard? What happened?', '', '', 'My values compass works in storms too. Especially in storms.', 'Role-play is essential for this session — children need to practise the uncomfortable scenario, not just discuss it. Keep the scenarios age-appropriate and non-threatening. Celebrate every imperfect attempt as much as the successful ones — the practice matters more than the outcome at this stage.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Sometimes we disagree with people — friends, family, classmates. That''s completely normal! Today we learn that disagreements don''t have to break friendships. We can learn how to talk about what we need and listen to what others need — and often find a way that works for everyone.', 'Can you think of a time when you had a disagreement with someone and you worked it out — and the friendship or relationship was actually okay or even stronger afterwards? What made that possible?', 'Sometimes we disagree with people — friends, family, classmates. That''s completely normal! Today we learn that disagreements don''t have to break friendships. We can learn how to talk about what we need and listen to what others need — and often find a way that works for everyone.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9_1Rt1R4xbM', 'YouTube: Search ''conflict resolution for kids animated'' or ''problem solving disagreements children YouTube'' for accessible short content. Runtime ~5 min. Book: ''Enemy Pie'' by Derek Munson — a classic story about conflict, assumptions, and unexpected friendship.', '', '', '', 'What argument do you need to sort out?', 'THE THREE STEPS PRACTICE: Teach the three steps with a physical poster: FEEL (I feel...), NEED (What I need is...), LISTEN (Can I hear what you feel and need?). Then role-play a gentle conflict scenario in pairs: e.g. ''Two friends both want to play different games. How do they work it out using the three steps?'' Practice 2–3 scenarios. Debrief: what made it easier to sort out? What made it harder? Share: one thing they noticed about themselves during the role-play.', 'Draw the three steps as a comic strip — two characters having a disagreement and working through it with the three steps.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Try the three steps in a real disagreement this week — even a small one. Notice what happens.', 'Teach the three steps to a grown-up. Role-play it with them. Ask them if they''ve ever used something like this.', 'Bring back: did you use the three steps this week? What happened?', '', '', 'I can work through disagreements kindly. I share my feelings and needs — and I listen to others'' too.', 'Physical role-play is essential for this age. The three steps need to be practised in the room, not just taught. Have the poster displayed throughout the rest of the year. Coordinate with parents to use the same framework at home — family conflicts are the richest practice ground.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Generosity means giving something to others — and it doesn''t have to be something you buy! Time, kindness, attention, encouragement, help — these are some of the most powerful gifts there are. And here''s the amazing thing: the more you give these things, the happier YOU feel too!', 'What is one gift you have that doesn''t cost any money — a skill, a quality, a way of making people feel good — that you could give more of? Think about it honestly.', 'Generosity means giving something to others — and it doesn''t have to be something you buy! Time, kindness, attention, encouragement, help — these are some of the most powerful gifts there are. And here''s the amazing thing: the more you give these things, the happier YOU feel too!', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rrkrvAUbU9Y', 'YouTube: Search ''generosity for kids animated YouTube'' or ''Have You Filled a Bucket Today read aloud'' — the bucket-filling concept is perfect for this session. Runtime ~8 min.', '', '', '', 'What can you give that doesn''t cost anything?', 'GIFTS THAT GROW: Create a class ''gift economy.'' Each child identifies three non-money gifts they have: a skill, a quality, a kind of help. Write them on gift card templates. Then: a ''gift exchange'' — children can offer their gifts to anyone in the group. ''I offer you my patience when you''re frustrated'' / ''I offer you my help with maths'' / ''I offer you my honest encouragement.'' No obligation to accept — just offer. Debrief: what did it feel like to offer? What did it feel like to receive? Share: one gift they offered and one they received.', 'Write or draw your three non-money gifts. Decorate them like real gift cards!', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Give one of your non-money gifts today — genuinely, freely, without expecting anything back.', 'Tell a grown-up about your three non-money gifts. Ask them what their non-money gifts are. Compare notes!', 'Bring back: what non-money gift did you give this week? What happened?', '', '', 'My gifts grow when I give them away. I am generous with what I have.', 'The gift economy activity is genuinely moving and can be one of the highlights of Phase 4. Make the gift cards beautiful and keep them as mementos. The distinction between bought gifts and character gifts is important to make clearly and warmly — both matter, but character gifts are inexhaustible.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Today we practise something really important: being happy with what we have, right now — not because we stop wanting to grow and get better, but because we stop being so focused on what we don''t have that we miss all the wonderful things that ARE here.', 'What is something wonderful in your life right now that you sometimes forget to notice because you''re thinking about something you want or something that''s worrying you?', 'Today we practise something really important: being happy with what we have, right now — not because we stop wanting to grow and get better, but because we stop being so focused on what we don''t have that we miss all the wonderful things that ARE here.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rrkrvAUbU9Y', 'YouTube: Search ''gratitude for kids animated YouTube'' or ''counting your blessings children story'' for accessible content. Runtime ~5 min. Book: ''The Grateful Ninja'' by Mary Nhin — a fun, accessible exploration of gratitude practice for children.', '', '', '', 'What''s already good that you''d stopped noticing?', 'THE ENOUGH GARDEN: Each child gets a garden template. In the garden, they draw or write things they already have that are genuinely good: relationships, abilities, experiences, qualities, everyday things they love. Facilitator primes with: ''Think about the people who love you, things you can do, things you enjoy, places that feel good, qualities you have.'' Take 5 minutes to fill the garden as full as possible. Share: the most surprising thing they put in their garden — something they''d forgotten to notice.', 'Draw your enough garden at home — add things you noticed there that aren''t in the one you drew today.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Today, tell three people one thing you''re grateful for about them — something specific and genuine.', 'Show a grown-up your enough garden. Tell them what surprised you most about how much was already there.', 'Bring back your home garden drawing — what new things did you notice to add?', '', '', 'I have a beautiful garden. I notice it. I am grateful for it. And it keeps growing.', 'The garden metaphor is wonderfully concrete for this age. Give generous time for the garden-filling exercise — children often discover far more than they expected to put in it. The sharing of ''the most surprising thing'' often produces genuinely moving moments. Send the garden home as a regular practice template.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Some of the most important things take a long time to grow — like trees, like friendships, like becoming really good at something. Today we learn about patience, persistence, and why showing up every day — even when things are hard — is one of the most powerful things you can do.', 'What is something you''ve gotten genuinely good at through practice — something that was hard at first but got easier because you kept trying? How does it feel now when you do it?', 'Some of the most important things take a long time to grow — like trees, like friendships, like becoming really good at something. Today we learn about patience, persistence, and why showing up every day — even when things are hard — is one of the most powerful things you can do.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hpnI3MCTJSA', 'YouTube: Search ''persistence and patience kids animated'' or ''The Little Engine That Could read aloud YouTube'' — the classic perseverance story. Runtime ~5–8 min. Book: ''Beautiful Oops'' or ''Rosie Revere Engineer'' by Andrea Beaty — about the habit of persisting through failure.', '', '', '', 'What are you practising that''s still hard?', 'THE LONG GAME GARDEN: Each child draws a garden with plants at different stages — seed underground, seedling just emerging, growing plant, fully bloomed flower. In each stage, they draw or write something in their life that matches: something they''re just beginning (seed), something starting to show (seedling), something growing (plant), something fully developed (flower). Discuss: how does it feel when something is still underground and you can''t see it? What helps you keep watering it? Share: their seed — something they''re just beginning that they''re committed to keep watering.', 'Draw your long game plant — draw where it is now, and draw where you hope it will be in two years!', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Today, show up for one long-game practice — even if it''s just a tiny bit, even if you can''t see progress. Water the plant.', 'Tell a grown-up about your long-game plant — what it is and how you''re going to keep watering it.', 'Bring back: did you water your long-game plant this week? What did it feel like?', '', '', 'I keep showing up. I keep watering. The plant is growing, even when I can''t see it yet.', 'The underground growth metaphor is perfect for children who are experiencing discouragement about habits that haven''t yet produced visible results. The garden stages activity gives a beautiful visual of where different things are in their growth cycle. Have children take home their long game drawings as commitments.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

One of the most wonderful things you can do is make people feel better just by being with them. Not by saying the perfect thing or doing something big — just by being kind, paying attention, and making people feel like they matter. Today we practise being that kind of person.', 'Who is someone in your life who makes you feel really good just by being around them — like sunshine? What do they do that makes you feel that way?', 'One of the most wonderful things you can do is make people feel better just by being with them. Not by saying the perfect thing or doing something big — just by being kind, paying attention, and making people feel like they matter. Today we practise being that kind of person.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9_1Rt1R4xbM', 'YouTube: Search ''kindness ripple effect kids animated'' or ''Ordinary Mary''s Extraordinary Deed read aloud YouTube'' — a beautiful story about one act of kindness that ripples outward. Runtime ~8 min.', '', '', '', 'Who made you feel good this week, and how?', 'THE SUNSHINE PRACTICE: Teach three specific sunshine acts: 1. NOTICE something genuine about a person and tell them (not a compliment about looks — something real: ''I noticed how brave you were in class today''). 2. REMEMBER something someone told you and ask about it (''How did that thing with your dog go?''). 3. SHOW UP when someone needs company — just being there, present, not fixing anything. Practise each in pairs in the room. Then: design your personal sunshine practice for this week. Share: which sunshine act feels most natural for them and why.', 'Draw a sunshine person — you! — with rays of light going out to all the people you could make feel better this week.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Today, try at least one sunshine act for someone — notice something real and genuine about them and tell them.', 'Tell a grown-up about the sunshine person idea. Ask them who the ''sunshine people'' in their life are.', 'Bring back: what sunshine acts did you do this week? What happened?', '', '', 'I am a sunshine person. I leave people brighter just from being around me.', 'The sunshine metaphor is wonderful and joyful for this age. The three specific sunshine acts give children practical, concrete behaviours rather than vague kindness prompts. Practise in the room before sending them out to do it. The sunshine drawing can be displayed and taken home.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Even at your age, you are leaving something in the world — in how you treat your friends, how you show kindness, what you teach younger children, the ripples of what you do every day. Today we think about the mark you want to leave on the world around you.', 'Think about someone who has made a difference in your life — someone whose kindness or care has stayed with you. What did they do? How does it still affect you now?', 'Even at your age, you are leaving something in the world — in how you treat your friends, how you show kindness, what you teach younger children, the ripples of what you do every day. Today we think about the mark you want to leave on the world around you.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7H2pBdLnmGs', 'YouTube: Search ''kindness ripple effect kids animated'' or ''Ordinary Mary''s Extraordinary Deed read aloud YouTube'' — perfect for the ripple concept. Runtime ~8 min.', '', '', '', 'What do you want people to remember about you?', 'THE RIPPLE MAP: Each child gets a pond template with concentric circles — like ripples. In the centre: them. In the first ripple: the immediate people they affect (family, close friends). In the second ripple: wider community (classmates, neighbours, teachers). In the outer ripple: the world beyond. In each circle, they write or draw one way they want to leave a positive mark. Share: their most important ripple and how they want to create it.', 'Draw your pond and your ripples — all the ways you''re making a positive mark on the world around you.', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Today, make one deliberate positive ripple — one kind, honest, caring act. Notice how far it goes.', 'Tell a grown-up about your ripple map. Ask them about the ripples they''re trying to create.', 'Bring back: what ripple did you make this week? Did you see it go further than you expected?', '', '', 'My actions create ripples. I choose kind, honest, caring ripples — and they go further than I know.', 'The ripple metaphor is visually beautiful and completely age-appropriate. The ripple map activity can become a physical piece of art — display the class collection. The concept that legacy is present-tense and available to everyone, regardless of age, is genuinely empowering for children.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Gratitude means really noticing and appreciating the good things in your life. Not just saying ''thank you'' — actually stopping and feeling genuinely thankful. Today we learn a special gratitude superpower: when you practise noticing good things, you actually start to notice MORE good things — and that makes life feel much richer.', 'What is something that happened today — even something small — that you''re genuinely happy about? Not a big thing. A small, real thing. Let yourself actually feel happy about it for a moment.', 'Gratitude means really noticing and appreciating the good things in your life. Not just saying ''thank you'' — actually stopping and feeling genuinely thankful. Today we learn a special gratitude superpower: when you practise noticing good things, you actually start to notice MORE good things — and that makes life feel much richer.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WPPPFqsECz0', 'YouTube: Search ''gratitude practice for kids animated'' or ''thankfulness children story YouTube'' for accessible content. Runtime ~5 min. Book: ''Grateful'' by Debbie Wagenbach — a beautiful children''s book about the practice of noticing what is already present and good.', '', '', '', 'What three good things happened today?', 'THE GRATITUDE CAMERA: Each child gets a paper ''camera'' template. They take three ''photos'' today — drawing or writing three specific things they''re genuinely grateful for. Each photo must be specific enough that it couldn''t have been taken yesterday. After completing: share one photo with the group. Then discuss: what''s the difference between a specific gratitude and a general one? Why does specific feel better?', 'Make a gratitude journal for the rest of the year — every day, three specific things you''re genuinely glad about. Decorate it to make it beautiful!', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Take three gratitude photos today — specific, genuine, real. Share one with someone.', 'Teach a grown-up the three-specific-things gratitude practice. Do it with them before bed tonight.', 'Bring back your gratitude journal! What have you noticed building up over the week?', '', '', 'I notice and appreciate the good things in my life. The more I practise, the more I find.', 'Make the gratitude journal beautiful — have children decorate it in the session as a take-home keepsake for the rest of the year. The camera metaphor is perfect for this age. The specificity principle should be practised in the room with clear examples. This is one of the most joyful sessions of Phase 4.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

Growing up is not something you finish. Every day there are new things to discover, new ways to be kind and brave and curious, new things to learn about yourself and the world. Today we celebrate the fact that the adventure doesn''t end — it just keeps getting richer.', 'What is one thing you want to keep practising from this year — something that has become genuinely yours? Something that feels like part of who you are now?', 'Growing up is not something you finish. Every day there are new things to discover, new ways to be kind and brave and curious, new things to learn about yourself and the world. Today we celebrate the fact that the adventure doesn''t end — it just keeps getting richer.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VWOgrMXBE4U', 'YouTube: Search ''Oh, the Places You''ll Go Dr Seuss read aloud YouTube'' — the perfect send-off into the ongoing adventure. Runtime ~8 min.', '', '', '', 'What will you keep practising?', 'THE ADVENTURE CONTINUES: Each child gets a ''next chapter'' page — like a blank first page of a new book. They write or draw: one thing they will keep practising, one quality they are taking forward, one adventure they want to go on, and a title for their next chapter. Share: the title of their next chapter.', 'Write your next chapter title and the first line of what happens in it!', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Choose one practice to keep doing every day — make it yours, not because you have to, but because it''s become part of who you are.', 'Tell a grown-up about your next chapter title and what you''re going to keep practising. Ask them about their next chapter.', 'Bring back your next chapter page! What happened in the first week of your next chapter?', '', '', 'My adventure continues. Every day I keep growing, keep practising, keep becoming more of who I truly am.', 'This should be genuinely exciting and celebratory — not bittersweet. The ''next chapter'' activity gives children a sense of agency and ownership. Display the next chapter pages alongside all the other Phase 4 work. This session connects beautifully back to the opening ''signal and noise'' metaphor from Week 1.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;

We''ve been on an adventure together for a whole year! Today we celebrate everything we''ve seen, learned, let go of, built, and shared. And then we look forward — because this adventure doesn''t end. It just becomes the rest of your beautiful, growing life.', 'If you could go back and tell Week 1 you one thing that would help them most — what would it be?', 'We''ve been on an adventure together for a whole year! Today we celebrate everything we''ve seen, learned, let go of, built, and shared. And then we look forward — because this adventure doesn''t end. It just becomes the rest of your beautiful, growing life.', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VWOgrMXBE4U', 'YouTube: ''Oh, the Places You''ll Go!'' by Dr Seuss read-aloud — the perfect year-end celebration of the ongoing journey. Runtime ~8 min.', '', '', '', 'What can you do now that you couldn''t a year ago?', 'THE YEAR CELEBRATION: Create a full year celebration — three parts: 1. LOOK BACK: Each child names one thing from each phase (Phase 1: something I learned to see, Phase 2: something I let go, Phase 3: something I built, Phase 4: something I gave). 2. LOOK AROUND: Each child says one genuine, specific thing they appreciate about one other person in the group. 3. LOOK FORWARD: Each child states one commitment for the ongoing practice. The facilitator witnesses each with genuine acknowledgment. End with the whole group together: hands in the middle, one collective phrase: ''We did the work. We keep going.''', 'Write a letter to yourself from Week 1 — what do you want them to know?', 'Given what you noticed today, what is one thing you will do differently before next Sunday?', 'Celebrate with one act of genuine service or kindness today — a gift from everything you''ve built this year.', 'Share your letter with a grown-up who has been part of your journey. Read it to them if you can.', 'Bring your letter back. The whole group will witness it together at the final ceremony.', '', '', 'I did the work. I am growing. The adventure continues — and I am ready for it.', 'THIS IS THE FINAL SESSION OF THE YEAR. Make it everything. Ceremony, celebration, witnessed acknowledgment, genuine joy. Every child deserves to have their year of courage honoured. The letters read aloud. The collective phrase. The community celebrated. This is what it was all building toward. Make it unforgettable.', '', '', '') ON CONFLICT (week_number, audience) DO UPDATE SET phase = EXCLUDED.phase, phase_name = EXCLUDED.phase_name, heavy_week_flag = EXCLUDED.heavy_week_flag, theme_title = EXCLUDED.theme_title, session_title = EXCLUDED.session_title, ancient_wisdom_reframe = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_reframe, ancient_wisdom_vo_script = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_vo_script, ancient_wisdom_video_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_video_url, ancient_wisdom_captions_url = EXCLUDED.ancient_wisdom_captions_url, signal_metaphor = EXCLUDED.signal_metaphor, todays_world_vo_script = EXCLUDED.todays_world_vo_script, todays_world_video_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_video_url, todays_world_captions_url = EXCLUDED.todays_world_captions_url, todays_theme = EXCLUDED.todays_theme, s5_source_opening_hook = EXCLUDED.s5_source_opening_hook, s5_source_core_concept = EXCLUDED.s5_source_core_concept, video_link = EXCLUDED.video_link, video_description = EXCLUDED.video_description, video_transcript = EXCLUDED.video_transcript, video_question_1 = EXCLUDED.video_question_1, video_question_2 = EXCLUDED.video_question_2, private_write_prompt = EXCLUDED.private_write_prompt, experiential_exercise = EXCLUDED.experiential_exercise, journaling_prompt = EXCLUDED.journaling_prompt, intention_prompt = EXCLUDED.intention_prompt, weekly_practice_mon = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_mon, weekly_practice_wed = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_wed, weekly_practice_sun = EXCLUDED.weekly_practice_sun, closing_quote = EXCLUDED.closing_quote, closing_quote_attribution = EXCLUDED.closing_quote_attribution, core_affirmation = EXCLUDED.core_affirmation, facilitator_prep_notes = EXCLUDED.facilitator_prep_notes, watch_for = EXCLUDED.watch_for, first_time_note = EXCLUDED.first_time_note, previous_week_callback = EXCLUDED.previous_week_callback;
